wcasing rich text styling inside Craft CMS. Includes headings, paragraphs, lists, and links — all styled with Tailwind and optimized for readability.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": []}',1,'2025-10-07 10:44:41','2025-12-08 09:09:31','24fd4e31-3c6f-4fb5-a711-651cd02d2c57'),(615,615,1,NULL,'__temp_qidilehdbzvpsmfjihkjiogbgamgjxlbldmq',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p><strong>About this project</strong></p><p>This starter kit reflects how I structure and build modern Craft CMS projects: clean, modular, and ready for real-world production use. I’m <strong>Andi Grether</strong>, a freelance Craft CMS specialist working with creative agencies and design teams who need a reliable technical partner for high-quality implementation.</p><p>If you’re interested in working together or want support on your next Craft project, feel free to reach out via <a href=\\\"https://webworker.me\\\"><strong>webworker.me</strong></a>.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-07 10:54:16','2025-11-20 13:41:14','b8dd5aa9-82cc-49e2-a382-b4a16dbcf3e6'),(658,658,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2025-10-08 07:58:01','2025-10-08 07:58:01','2022aaa7-9c9b-4874-9dac-68469468e640'),(659,659,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Matrix Builder – Modular Content Blocks for Craft CMS\", \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Explore how flexible content creation works in Craft CMS using Matrix fields. Each component is reusable, responsive, and fits seamlessly into the custom Grid Layout system.\"}',1,'2025-10-08 07:58:01','2025-10-08 07:58:01','d7629f59-a8f0-4fad-a339-fa9189cbf924'),(666,666,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2025-10-08 07:58:27','2025-10-08 07:58:27','49b49d78-7fc9-47de-857b-029b5e9fb0c2'),(667,667,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Matrix Builder – Modular Content Blocks for Craft CMS\", \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Explore how flexible content creation works in Craft CMS using Matrix fields. Each component is reusable, responsive, and fits seamlessly into the custom Grid Layout system.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": [470]}',1,'2025-10-08 07:58:27','2025-10-08 07:58:27','1f24fdc8-a9f5-4572-bd7a-991a133d9e85'),(700,700,1,'Social OG',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-09 09:39:40','2026-03-19 08:00:21','9933f698-ebbd-4afe-bb43-f0553a59cb26'),(705,705,1,'Imprint','imprint','imprint','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Imprint\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p>Information pursuant to § 5 DDG</p><p>Andi Grether<br />Badstr. 22c<br />79379 Müllheim<br />Germany<br /><a href=\\\"mailto:webworker.ag@gmail.com\\\">webworker.ag@gmail.com</a></p><p><strong>Legal Notice</strong></p><p>The content of this website has been created and reviewed with great care. However, no guarantee can be given for the accuracy, completeness, or current validity of the information provided. This website demonstrates the Craft Kit starter kit and presents independent development work. The demo does not provide an online checkout. </p><p><strong>Illustrations and screenshots</strong></p><p>The editorial illustrations were created for Craft Kit with an image-generation model and are marked with an AI badge. The editor screenshots show the Craft Kit demo installation. Images are served locally; no Unsplash images are used.</p><p>Last updated: 13 November 2026</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 09:40:31','2026-11-13 15:54:27','c8d15680-d713-4f7a-bbba-ce6b5cfd80ea'),(706,706,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": []}',1,'2025-10-09 09:40:31','2025-12-08 09:09:31','1d3829e4-fb6d-4a53-8f37-b5953989e0bd'),(711,711,1,'Privacy policy','privacy-policy','privacy-policy','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Privacy policy\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Craft Kit is a public demonstration of a Craft CMS starter kit and its Datastar examples. It also presents my work as an independent developer. This notice explains how personal data is processed when you visit or use the demos.</p><h2>Controller and contact</h2><p>Andi Grether<br />Badstr. 22c<br />79379 Müllheim<br />Germany<br /><a href=\\\"mailto:webworker.ag@gmail.com\\\">webworker.ag@gmail.com</a></p><h2>Website delivery and server logs</h2><p>When you request a page or an asset, the hosting system processes technical information such as your IP address, request URL, time of access, browser information and response status. These data are needed to deliver the website, diagnose problems and protect it from abuse.</p><p>Logs are retained only as long as needed for these purposes or to investigate security incidents, subject to applicable retention obligations. The legal basis for operating and securing the website is our legitimate interest under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.</p><h2>Datastar interactions, search and the Todo List</h2><p>Datastar is served from this website. Navigation controls, search, filters and the demo forms send requests to this website when a server response is needed. Search terms and submitted demo values are processed to provide the requested result. They can also form part of the requested URL and technical access logs.</p><p>The Todo List stores tasks in your server-side session. A necessary session cookie can associate your browser with that session; security cookies may also be used for request protection. The demo does not create a permanent personal task account. Do not enter sensitive or confidential information into it.</p><p>Essential session and security storage is used to provide the function you request, not for advertising. The applicable basis is Article 6(1)(f) GDPR and, for strictly necessary device storage or access, Section 25(2) TDDDG.</p><h2>Cookieless Matomo analytics</h2><p>The public website uses a self-hosted Matomo installation at <strong>p-e8qn5a.project.space</strong> to understand use of the demo. The tracker is configured with cookies disabled. It records page views and link interactions; the demos also send event categories such as adding or completing a task and opening the Bitcoin data panel. The task text is not included in those custom event calls.</p><p>Analytics can process the visited URL, referrer, time of access, browser and device information, and the IP address received by the analytics server. Cookieless tracking is still data processing. IP masking and retention are controlled in the Matomo server configuration; disabling cookies alone is not a guarantee of anonymity.</p><p>The purpose is to improve the demonstration and understand which examples are useful, based on our legitimate interest under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. You may object to processing based on legitimate interests by contacting the controller. If a particular analytics configuration requires consent, it must be assessed separately; the absence of cookies does not decide that question by itself.</p><h2>OpenStreetMap on the map demo</h2><p>Opening the <a href=\\\"{entry:1029@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/map}\\\">map demo</a> loads map tiles directly from OpenStreetMap tile servers. These requests transmit technical connection data, including your IP address and the requested tile URLs, to the map service. This is separate from the locally served Leaflet code used to display the map.</p><p>The map is provided to demonstrate location filtering. Details about the service\'s data processing are available in the <a href=\\\"https://osmfoundation.org/wiki/Privacy_Policy\\\">OpenStreetMap Foundation privacy policy</a>. Other pages do not need to load those map tiles.</p><h2>AI-generated content</h2><p>All editorial texts and illustrations on this demo website were generated or revised using artificial intelligence. Actual screenshots of the Craft control panel are not AI-generated. Generated illustrations are identified by an AI badge.</p><p>AI-assisted content may contain errors. It is provided to demonstrate the starter kit and does not replace independent professional advice. Simply viewing the texts and images does not send your data to an AI service.</p><h2>Images, fonts and frontend assets</h2><p>The demo images, fonts and application UI scripts are served from this website. The Matomo analytics script is loaded separately from the analytics host described above. The editorial illustrations were created for Craft Kit and are marked with an AI badge. Viewing them does not send an image-generation request or visitor data to an AI image service. Unsplash images and remote font services are not used.</p><h2>Server-side data sources and external links</h2><p>The GitHub repository statistics and Binance BTC/USDT ticker are fetched by the website\'s server. The demo does not send your search terms or task text to those services, and your browser does not need to contact their APIs to display the results.</p><p>Links to GitHub, LinkedIn, documentation and external articles take you to other websites when you follow them. Their operators then process data under their own privacy policies.</p><h2>Contact by email</h2><p>If you send an email, your message and contact details are processed to answer your inquiry. This includes processing by the email service providers involved in delivery. The legal basis is Article 6(1)(b) GDPR for contract-related inquiries, or Article 6(1)(f) GDPR for other correspondence. Messages are deleted when no longer needed, unless legal retention obligations apply.</p><h2>Your rights</h2><p>Subject to the applicable conditions, you may request access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing or data portability. You may object to processing based on legitimate interests. Where processing relies on consent, you may withdraw it for the future.</p><p>You may also complain to a data protection supervisory authority. For Baden-Württemberg, see the <a href=\\\"https://www.baden-wuerttemberg.datenschutz.de/\\\">state data protection authority</a>. Contact the controller above to exercise your rights.</p><h2>Reusing the starter kit</h2><p>This notice describes this demonstration, not every project built from the repository. If you reuse Craft Kit, adapt the notice to your controller details, hosting, enabled integrations and actual data-processing configuration.</p><p>Last updated: 13 November 2026.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 09:45:29','2026-11-15 14:14:40','dcff04d2-6277-4b20-8a2d-e8a0ac56c947'),(712,712,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"How the Craft Kit demo processes technical data, Datastar demo inputs, cookieless Matomo analytics and OpenStreetMap requests.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": []}',1,'2025-10-09 09:45:29','2026-11-13 15:54:27','832c50b2-74a5-4db7-a948-d9e7ba4d4905'),(723,723,1,'Search','search','search','{\"0335e22f-b3a6-4cf1-9c27-8843e48457b6\": \"Datastar Search — Lightweight Reactive Search for Craft CMS — A fast and lightweight search page for Craft CMS using Datastar. Real-time search, instant results, and no full-page reloads — built entirely in Twig.\", \"501b1b12-e462-43a8-b93e-55e9d3742ce8\": 0, \"fba4e9d8-e8fa-4067-b5f1-c9b9a2a562d1\": \"<h1>Search</h1><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A fast, lightweight search experience powered by Craft CMS and Datastar. This page demonstrates how to build reactive search interfaces directly in Twig — no heavy JavaScript framework required.</p><p>The Datastar Search Page is a practical example of how to implement instant, dynamic search functionality in Craft CMS. It uses Craft’s native search capabilities combined with Datastar’s reactive rendering to deliver fast and fluid results without page reloads.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 10:09:52','2026-06-09 08:51:33','5072f078-c07c-43b2-90e4-a11f68eb3878'),(724,724,1,'Search','search','search',NULL,1,'2025-10-09 10:09:52','2025-10-09 10:09:52','07da37ae-1769-496f-b7db-e9bb5bd7b01b'),(725,725,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Datastar Search — Lightweight Reactive Search for Craft CMS\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"A fast and lightweight search page for Craft CMS using Datastar. Real-time search, instant results, and no full-page reloads — built entirely in Twig.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": []}',1,'2025-10-09 10:14:06','2025-12-08 09:09:30','0b24b3f0-5b80-4e1b-a892-9d77a2ea0055'),(727,727,1,'Search','search','search','{\"fba4e9d8-e8fa-4067-b5f1-c9b9a2a562d1\": \"<h1>Search</h1>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 10:14:20','2025-10-09 10:14:20','14f05dde-3ad0-40dd-ac39-cd5961a71dd4'),(728,728,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-09 10:14:20','2025-10-09 10:14:20','f058a2de-6796-4b7f-8d1f-52a2e6393ff5'),(730,730,1,'Search','search','search','{\"fba4e9d8-e8fa-4067-b5f1-c9b9a2a562d1\": \"<h1>Search</h1><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A fast, lightweight search experience powered by Craft CMS and Datastar. This page demonstrates how to build reactive search interfaces directly in Twig — no heavy JavaScript framework required.</p><p>The Datastar Search Page is a practical example of how to implement instant, dynamic search functionality in Craft CMS. It uses Craft’s native search capabilities combined with Datastar’s reactive rendering to deliver fast and fluid results without page reloads.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 10:23:28','2025-10-09 10:23:28','2357f003-566c-4c9c-8878-78cbc09725c8'),(733,733,1,'Search','search','search','{\"fba4e9d8-e8fa-4067-b5f1-c9b9a2a562d1\": \"<h1>Search</h1><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A fast, lightweight search experience powered by Craft CMS and Datastar. This page demonstrates how to build reactive search interfaces directly in Twig — no heavy JavaScript framework required.</p><p>The Datastar Search Page is a practical example of how to implement instant, dynamic search functionality in Craft CMS. It uses Craft’s native search capabilities combined with Datastar’s reactive rendering to deliver fast and fluid results without page reloads.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 10:23:57','2025-10-09 10:23:57','0b29ee92-9761-4915-99cf-fca7c51a45c6'),(734,734,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Datastar Search — Lightweight Reactive Search for Craft CMS\", \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"A fast and lightweight search page for Craft CMS using Datastar. Real-time search, instant results, and no full-page reloads — built entirely in Twig.\"}',1,'2025-10-09 10:23:57','2025-10-09 10:23:57','4203f35c-4263-486a-b595-5dd04d59f7ff'),(750,750,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Craft CMS Boilerplate – Modern Starter Kit with Vite, Tailwind & Datastar\", \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"A modern Craft CMS boilerplate featuring Vite, Tailwind CSS, Vue 3, Datastar, and GraphQL. Built for developers and agencies looking for a fast, scalable, and beautifully structured starting point for new Craft projects.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": [700]}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','81d6644c-6007-4a61-8236-27501a5f92df'),(752,752,1,NULL,'__temp_xkxefblkbqrrpgdsmxpjqahpwwtxucyulfla',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','df175c3a-bedc-440a-907f-a2490f6346b9'),(753,753,1,NULL,'__temp_ymqpcozflkswyiztejqhscgrwkbbvylnvwoy',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:12@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Build flexible page layouts using Craft’s Matrix field. Each component can be placed freely within the custom Grid Layout system.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','9506760c-2c26-4e71-80cd-579b3e57fcc6'),(754,754,1,NULL,'__temp_rookcbakctclekveurvtcgllabmfytnayywb',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"✍️ CKEditor Builder\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Insert predefined components directly into CKEditor. A simple example of combining structured elements and rich text content.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','b3ea46d6-de27-4faf-853d-f3ee1e074121'),(755,755,1,NULL,'__temp_exydctshdtrxmqnzznfpmdmwtnijllasnzlm',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"⚡ Datastar Search\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:723@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Fast and lightweight search using Craft Datastar. Instant results, live updates, and minimal JavaScript.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','94ac525c-1107-4878-8775-d6527a8c5517'),(756,756,1,NULL,'__temp_wivzvacapfdmeujajaupvewukwdvqvhisguk',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"🚀 Blog (Datastar)\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>A dynamic blog built with Craft DataStar. Features live filtering, pagination, and instant content updates without page reloads.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','6832608a-6cb0-4ac4-bc2b-e6cb5b423d2f'),(757,757,1,NULL,'__temp_lwnertfphvvauwgyrfvklnfsixfpapkltjzf',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"🧩 Blog (Vue)\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:359@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>A Vue-based blog using GraphQL. Demonstrates reactive filtering, “load more” functionality, and category management via API.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','e46d04b6-7372-4cbe-936e-7a1b339cabf7'),(758,758,1,NULL,'__temp_uvnzbtbsulagvvlmhwivhpmohuohwpnvjcon',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"🧭 Grid Layout\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Layout\", \"value\": \"/layout\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Shows the responsive Grid Layout system used across all pages. Easily define full, content, feature, or popout columns.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-09 12:46:02','2025-10-09 12:46:02','235ec66f-4603-4a24-92e2-ce5790a32b8c'),(775,775,1,'Home','home','__home__','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"CraftCMS Lazy —\\nA simple Craft CMS Starter Kit\"}',1,'2025-10-13 09:26:54','2025-10-13 09:26:54','f5aeb841-4407-4fe4-9d07-7d7619c07f3f'),(776,776,1,NULL,'__temp_xmyryjgfvmihfecdlkmvkhurafqliwjajpcz',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A modern, production-ready Craft CMS Starter Kit with Vite, Tailwind, Vue Web Components, Datastar, GraphQL and DDEV — perfect for agencies and freelancers who want to build clean and fast Craft sites..</p><p>This starter kit helps developers quickly spin up clean and maintainable Craft CMS projects. It includes ready-made examples for Matrix Blocks, CKEditor integration, a Datastar-powered Search page, and both Datastar- and Vue-based blog listings.</p><p><strong>🧠 Built with modern tools and clean architecture</strong></p><ul><li>⚙️ <strong>Craft CMS 5</strong> – latest version with flexible content modeling</li><li>⚡ <strong>Vite</strong> – fast bundling and instant reloads</li><li>🧩 <strong>DDEV</strong> – reproducible local development environment</li><li>🚀 <strong>Datastar</strong> – lightweight, reactive frontend for dynamic UIs</li><li>🧱 <strong>Vue 3 (Web Components)</strong> – progressive enhancement with custom elements</li><li>🔗 <strong>GraphQL</strong> – structured data fetching directly from Craft</li><li>🎨 <strong>Tailwind CSS v4</strong> – utility-first styling with CSS variables</li><li>🎞️ <strong>Anime.js</strong> – smooth element animations and scroll-based transitions</li><li>🗃️ <strong>Craft eagerly() + render()</strong> – optimized queries, automatic block templates, and smart caching</li><li>🔌 <strong>Plugins:</strong> CKEditor, Datastar, Image Resizer, SEOMate, Vite</li></ul><p>💻 Feel free to explore, fork, or contribute — this starter kit is open source and available on <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">GitHub</a>.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-13 09:26:54','2025-10-13 09:26:54','628741a6-011c-4e56-bb08-4327168413d6'),(796,796,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','424ede7f-c052-438d-b172-074f9efc284e'),(797,797,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Matrix Builder – Modular Content Blocks for Craft CMS\", \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Explore how flexible content creation works in Craft CMS using Matrix fields. Each component is reusable, responsive, and fits seamlessly into the custom Grid Layout system.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": [470]}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','4249abde-90d3-418d-92af-387e8007d050'),(798,798,1,NULL,'__temp_igexmbvajwvcuuzsdrygzfnvhrvrckpdgpyk',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">The <strong>Matrix Builder</strong> is a visual demonstration of how Craft CMS handles flexible, component-based content through Matrix fields.</p><p>It shows how editors can create rich page layouts by combining different “blocks” — such as text, images, quotes, buttons, or call-to-action elements — without writing any code. Each block is powered by a reusable Twig component with consistent markup and a shared design system, making it easy for developers to maintain, extend, and customize.</p><p>What makes this setup especially powerful is that <strong>every component can be placed anywhere within the custom </strong><a href=\\\"/layout\\\"><strong>CSS Grid layout</strong></a>, using named grid areas like content, popout, feature, or full. This gives editors complete control over structure and visual hierarchy while developers retain full semantic and performance control.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','5c94a096-4d9b-4e7a-b0ac-f7c95b01fd7f'),(799,799,1,NULL,'__temp_dkucgpvpbmgwouxblhhoezbgricogtigdgeh',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": false, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [470]}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','9a60f5ca-79b2-4787-abd1-15380148c809'),(800,800,1,NULL,'__temp_lczjuokmzbhhbyxyrynxewsouacztdqeogei',NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','a81779a1-32a7-42e5-a5b2-2086621f6dca'),(801,801,1,NULL,'__temp_qrcmkinkbbxnuibhhyluprgddxbrnwukdrjd',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>The Matrix Builder is a flexible content module in Craft CMS that allows you to create structured layouts using reusable components. Instead of rigid templates, you can freely combine text, images, galleries, call-to-actions, or videos. This approach gives editors creative freedom while maintaining clean, semantic HTML and consistent design.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"🧱 What Is the Matrix Builder in Craft CMS?\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','dac9a841-44e6-4327-9835-91b3ca74f9f5'),(802,802,1,NULL,'__temp_fdmnmwnhizyqaowchspafavppvztbhftromn',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>The Matrix Builder comes with ready-to-use components like headline-text blocks, images, sliders, accordions, quotes, links, and FAQs. Each block is built on centralized Twig templates, making your content scalable, responsive, and easy to maintain — ideal for modern websites and professional content strategies.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"📦 What Components Are Included?\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','6de1b2e4-f607-4230-a4a9-707496773c26'),(803,803,1,NULL,'__temp_sqhkxwtlwqdgpomsyqfjgdeialsntxttdqnm',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Matrix-based editing separates content from layout, giving editors structured building blocks. This results in consistent design, better SEO performance, and more control over accessibility and UX. Unlike typical WYSIWYG editors, the output remains lightweight, semantic, and easy to optimize.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"🚀 Why Choose Matrix Over a Traditional WYSIWYG?\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','975f2bec-039c-40f5-b5e3-4d65d8503213'),(804,804,1,NULL,'__temp_iuqtjsmrlgyfgamoicbmshrwnihaozshbzmr',NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','4df095c0-874a-4209-9d08-2afd8c31d6bb'),(805,805,1,NULL,'__temp_dxtimhpfruderepiywupiwbzaabmxgnqgevz',NULL,'{\"2dba2ca7-6750-4abe-9d92-ec4e65d8329e\": false, \"35eccd8c-7a80-4452-8dfb-029ade24766e\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:197@1:url}\"}}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','d98f3d9b-e05b-4886-a87e-dcbe90fee867'),(806,806,1,NULL,'__temp_sadnfgcxlxzyfkuwekgeliwqwszcisshtpps',NULL,'{\"2dba2ca7-6750-4abe-9d92-ec4e65d8329e\": true, \"35eccd8c-7a80-4452-8dfb-029ade24766e\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','ebaee846-a217-4285-ac84-07527a3c491a'),(807,807,1,NULL,'__temp_dylfnxlitdhvawugsdazyilrjqksgobwewrz',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [28]}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','b1950fed-0791-487e-93cf-f9c52abafa34'),(808,808,1,NULL,'__temp_skgejxqlvzvxlvshaiwtkhzsdcucfrnrrbdi',NULL,'{\"b8d6efb4-2958-4af8-bc7d-70882b9d2432\": [28, 41, 42, 43]}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','9f3a4d00-8590-48f0-b970-084467cad13a'),(809,809,1,NULL,'__temp_ggcamffnpfxkkqkyiogvkbusxetubwjpugiu',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','833fec3f-1daf-4901-be19-8dc1084f3927'),(810,810,1,NULL,'__temp_vlktkftqsphxfjyndyemvdqeyyhcodychxau',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Dapibus Nullam Egestas Consectetur\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [28], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Aenean eu leo quam. Pellentesque ornare sem lacinia quam venenatis vestibulum. Fusce dapibus, tellus ac cursus commodo, tortor mauris condimentum nibh.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','595ecd7b-dd1e-49d2-89cd-e02cdaa2dba4'),(811,811,1,NULL,'__temp_vjcqenztenwqdnbjeaoufajpbezaedwnfdaw',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Purus Ligula Vehicula Tortor\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:197@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [41], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Nulla vitae elit libero, a pharetra augue. Vestibulum id ligula porta felis euismod semper.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','865bed73-9a64-4542-bae8-e4a561617e2c'),(812,812,1,NULL,'__temp_lxpgaomhbryfxiauurlxexhrqgqbctjrinec',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Mollis Vehicula Sem Consectetur\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [41], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Integer posuere erat a ante venenatis dapibus <strong>posuere</strong> velit aliquet. Praesent commodo cursus magna, vel scelerisque nisl consectetur et.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','a0eff70f-d4e9-4044-8ca0-1fdb79de933f'),(813,813,1,NULL,'__temp_ssedhvejnbomhxziekbsplayakexpmtvvapn',NULL,'{\"1d7830ee-7479-40b2-96b0-17200bd14633\": \"Cum sociis natoque penatibus et magnis dis parturient montes, nascetur ridiculus mus.\", \"2f0f4a25-fdf8-4cf1-a7c5-6591cf58478a\": true, \"60975007-2c9c-4def-920c-c569249360dc\": [43], \"8731b252-877d-4cfa-80b2-c380c4af26be\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"f1bae623-7325-44f0-9281-7ee78b45e5c8\": true, \"f919de8f-8fc8-4c89-b438-ccf0e409eb0d\": false}',1,'2025-10-15 12:59:15','2025-10-15 12:59:15','4f28761c-22b7-42f8-b1b1-e49abeb6ede8'),(816,816,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2025-10-15 13:00:37','2025-10-15 13:00:37','40305a4c-a4c2-4a8f-8039-f81a2d9f1bb0'),(817,817,1,NULL,'__temp_ssedhvejnbomhxziekbsplayakexpmtvvapn',NULL,'{\"1d7830ee-7479-40b2-96b0-17200bd14633\": \"Build Rich Text Content with Structure and Style\", \"2f0f4a25-fdf8-4cf1-a7c5-6591cf58478a\": true, \"60975007-2c9c-4def-920c-c569249360dc\": [43], \"8731b252-877d-4cfa-80b2-c380c4af26be\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"👉 Explore the CKEditor Builder\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"f1bae623-7325-44f0-9281-7ee78b45e5c8\": true, \"f919de8f-8fc8-4c89-b438-ccf0e409eb0d\": false}',1,'2025-10-15 13:00:37','2025-10-15 13:00:37','3c06244f-0b7c-4c35-bcb4-abac3b082133'),(823,823,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2025-10-15 13:02:31','2025-10-15 13:02:31','dce66a94-2acd-4682-beb1-e631fc642603'),(824,824,1,NULL,'__temp_ggcamffnpfxkkqkyiogvkbusxetubwjpugiu',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false}',1,'2025-10-15 13:02:31','2025-10-15 13:02:31','c53fc872-7a66-425e-b0d4-cada2e0c948b'),(825,825,1,NULL,'__temp_vlktkftqsphxfjyndyemvdqeyyhcodychxau',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"✍️ CKEditor Builder\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [28], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Insert predefined components directly into CKEditor. A simple example of combining structured elements and rich text content.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-15 13:02:31','2025-10-15 13:02:31','aa45fcce-feb3-4553-a0aa-5da5a670abd3'),(826,826,1,NULL,'__temp_vjcqenztenwqdnbjeaoufajpbezaedwnfdaw',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"🚀 Blog (Datastar)\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [41], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>A dynamic blog built with Craft DataStar. Features live filtering, pagination, and instant content updates without page reloads.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-15 13:02:31','2025-10-15 13:02:31','65a9f119-eae9-449c-ba4c-97d8f540bc34'),(827,827,1,NULL,'__temp_lxpgaomhbryfxiauurlxexhrqgqbctjrinec',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"🧭 Grid Layout\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"/layout\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [41], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Shows the responsive Grid Layout system used across all pages. Easily define full, content, feature, or popout columns.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-15 13:02:31','2025-10-15 13:02:31','b64ed2e8-e337-41fb-989a-7a7cca651aff'),(876,876,1,'Opinion','opinion',NULL,'{\"a8247aa8-49d4-46eb-9425-55d63c4de5ca\": \"#50b9a4\"}',1,'2025-10-21 08:57:07','2025-11-07 12:30:37','fbf68672-6da7-4ac4-b0ba-ab6514f69f3b'),(877,877,1,'Opinion','opinion',NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-21 08:57:09','2025-10-21 08:57:09','140c7c50-8ab3-4b8b-9824-1f9c19292862'),(878,878,1,'Souvik banerjee W Pr NEM 6dg unsplash',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-21 09:00:05','2025-10-21 09:00:05','697e26bf-485e-4bb8-9e44-1bc9e6cccac3'),(879,879,1,NULL,'__temp_epuxgsbappmctwahfdpzjemvchoaohitwwwg',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">For a custom, content-driven website, I want control over the content model, the markup and the way the interface behaves. Craft CMS gives me that foundation. Datastar makes it reactive without turning it into a separate frontend application.</p><h2>A content model built around the project</h2><p>Craft starts with sections, entry types, fields and relationships that you define. Editors work with the structure their content needs, rather than a theme\'s assumptions. Matrix handles page sections; CKEditor handles flowing text with embedded components.</p><p>WordPress can also support custom content models and carefully built frontends. My preference is about the starting point: Craft makes structured content and custom Twig templates central to the workflow.</p><h2>Own the HTML</h2><p>With Twig, the same project controls content queries, semantic markup, image output and accessible controls. There is no requirement to choose a theme or expose a JSON API before a page can exist.</p><p>That is a useful foundation for performance, but not a guarantee. Queries, eager loading, caching, image sizes and hosting still need attention.</p><h2>Add Datastar where the page needs to react</h2><p>A filter does not need a second application. Craft can render the results in Twig, and Datastar can request and morph those results into the page. Search, pagination and a task list follow the same pattern.</p><p>In Craft Kit, Datastar also controls the navigation dropdowns, mobile navigation and search panel. There is no Alpine, Vue or React layer coordinating that ordinary UI state. The same signal and attribute model covers local interactions and server requests.</p><h2>Choose the stack for the work</h2><p>WordPress remains a valid choice for teams invested in its ecosystem. Craft is the stack I choose when a project calls for a deliberate content architecture, a custom design and a frontend I can keep understandable.</p><p>The official <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/vs-wordpress\\\">Craft CMS and WordPress comparison</a> covers the differences in more detail. For an existing WordPress site, start with the <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/blog/migrating-from-wordpress\\\">migration guide</a> and audit the content before planning a rebuild.</p><h2>Try the approach, not just the argument</h2><p>Explore the <a href=\\\"{entry:258@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/blog}\\\">Datastar blog</a>, <a href=\\\"{entry:1029@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/map}\\\">map filters</a> and <a href=\\\"{entry:723@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/search}\\\">live search</a>. Then inspect the <a href=\\\"{entry:99@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/builder}\\\">Builder</a> to see how the content is composed.</p><p><a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">Download Craft Kit on GitHub</a> and use the templates as a starting point for your own Craft and Datastar project.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-21 09:00:53','2026-11-13 15:50:56','f7d1d692-4c20-4479-904a-59ee9a7bf802'),(880,880,1,'Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress','craft-vs-wordpress','blog/craft-vs-wordpress','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-04-29 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [876], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress\"}',1,'2025-10-21 09:00:53','2025-10-21 09:00:53','56d501be-fefb-47dd-9483-c4616c86f325'),(881,881,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"41d42c36-230e-4e28-96f8-8a4801e9694e\": \"<p>Tired of plugin chaos and theme bloat? Craft CMS might be the breath of fresh air you need.</p>\", \"914ae46d-5dd7-4afd-b5a3-32fbed3aecae\": [878]}',1,'2025-10-21 09:00:53','2025-10-21 09:00:53','70722f84-cdc4-42d5-a5fa-6a02584e01d2'),(882,882,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-21 09:00:53','2025-10-21 09:00:53','0e32dd55-6792-45dc-812f-32767cbf59f9'),(883,883,1,NULL,'__temp_epuxgsbappmctwahfdpzjemvchoaohitwwwg',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">For many agencies and developers, WordPress has been the go-to CMS for years. It’s familiar, has a massive ecosystem, and is well-known to clients.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">But <i>familiarity isn’t always the same as fit</i>.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Craft CMS isn’t trying to be WordPress — and that’s exactly why it’s winning the hearts of designers, developers, and clients who want clean, flexible sites without the plugin chaos.</p><h2><strong>Clean by Default</strong></h2><p>WordPress often starts out lean but quickly turns into a plugin maze. Craft CMS, on the other hand, comes with just what you need — nothing more, nothing less. No “Hello Dolly,” no page builder you didn’t ask for, no endless menu items.</p><p>👉 <strong>Result:</strong> Faster projects, fewer surprises, and cleaner codebases.</p><h2><strong>Developer First (But Friendly for Editors)</strong></h2><p>Craft is designed with developers in mind — structured content modeling, clean templating, and predictable behavior. But it also gives editors a <i>beautiful and intuitive</i> authoring experience. No clutter, no 30 different side panels. If you’ve ever tried to train a client in WordPress Gutenberg, you’ll know what I mean.</p><h2><strong>Performance Without a Fight</strong></h2><p>With WordPress, good performance often requires caching plugins, optimization tools, and server tweaks. Craft is fast out of the box — Twig templates, caching layers, and asset transforms are built in. That means fewer dependencies, less debugging, and a snappier experience overall.</p><h2><strong>Freedom for Designers</strong></h2><p>WordPress often bends you towards themes and blocks. Craft gives you a blank canvas. That’s why agencies love it — you can build <i>your</i> design system, not someone else’s. It’s like the difference between renting a furnished apartment and building your own loft.</p><h2><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2><p>WordPress isn’t bad — but Craft CMS is often a better fit for modern teams who want clarity, control, and clean output.</p><p>If you’re thinking about switching, Craft even provides a clear migration path from WordPress.  <br />👉 <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/blog/migrating-from-wordpress\\\">Official guide: Migrating from WordPress</a></p><p>✅ <strong>Tip:</strong> If you’re setting up Craft CMS for the first time, try starting from my a well-structured <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">starter kit</a>. It saves hours of setup time.</p><p> </p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\"> </p>\"}',1,'2025-10-21 09:00:53','2025-10-21 09:00:53','075a9245-45b0-444c-a037-384d14eda942'),(884,884,1,'Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress','craft-vs-wordpress','blog/craft-vs-wordpress','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-04-29 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [876], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress\"}',1,'2025-10-21 09:01:08','2025-10-21 09:01:08','3467b01f-c6e7-4cd5-87d0-d910f44c7bf7'),(886,886,1,'Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress','craft-vs-wordpress','blog/craft-vs-wordpress','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-10-20 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [876], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress\"}',1,'2025-10-21 09:01:36','2025-10-21 09:01:36','42bb6ea5-d4b8-4b3d-bb53-8d5b8b6ada65'),(892,892,1,'Development','development',NULL,'{\"a8247aa8-49d4-46eb-9425-55d63c4de5ca\": \"#bf6e6e\"}',1,'2025-10-21 09:16:22','2025-11-07 12:30:29','d4754597-0801-47cf-8de5-271482a68f08'),(893,893,1,'Development','development',NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-21 09:16:25','2025-10-21 09:16:25','0b3f6e41-b3a5-4835-9712-35dabb9271d1'),(925,925,1,'Brett jordan E1por S Gv JE unsplash',NULL,NULL,'{\"48d2238f-4200-4601-8702-9f2157892222\": \"Brett Jordan / Unsplash\", \"e30c17b9-ffa5-4343-99ee-0f780e5e0ed0\": \"In the beginning.\"}',1,'2025-10-21 11:55:24','2026-11-13 14:12:14','e98ec415-dc80-4957-b01a-4bc942f3cad1'),(935,935,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2025-10-21 11:57:14','2025-10-21 11:57:14','bf6ba0b4-18c5-447d-b1d1-22f0584d8a77'),(951,951,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"🧱 Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2025-10-21 12:04:39','2025-10-21 12:04:39','05de1faa-7f38-4374-ad37-a8aeab54b71d'),(972,972,1,'Mad geek love MKTZXUDQ5c8 unsplash',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-23 08:06:23','2025-10-23 08:06:23','85b2f095-7f8c-48a1-8b10-1ba5b47fab62'),(979,979,1,NULL,'__temp_jstciagbxuaohtngrbfunmncynfgajzhhnep',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">I used to reach for Craft, GraphQL and Vue whenever a website needed interactivity. For most content-driven projects, I now prefer Craft, Twig and Datastar. The reason is practical: I can deliver the same useful interactions with fewer layers to coordinate.</p><h2>What Vue and GraphQL solve</h2><p>A separate frontend application makes sense when it is genuinely an application: complex offline behavior, substantial browser-owned data, or several clients consuming the same API. Craft\'s GraphQL API can serve a web frontend, a mobile app and other integrations from one content model.</p><p>That is a different requirement from a website that needs search, filters and pagination. I do not want to introduce an API boundary solely to update a list of Craft entries.</p><h2>What the extra layer costs</h2><p>Craft generates a GraphQL schema from the content model and permissions; you do not have to invent that schema manually. You still need to maintain frontend queries, rendering components, loading states and error handling around the API.</p><p>For a single website, that can mean expressing the same content relationships in Craft, in API queries and in the frontend\'s rendering layer. Those boundaries can be valuable for an independent frontend team. In a small Craft team, I often find they add coordination without enough benefit.</p><h2>Let Craft render the response</h2><p>Craft already knows how to query entries, resolve relations, transform assets and render Twig. Datastar lets those templates remain the UI: an interaction requests an endpoint, the server returns HTML patches, and the browser updates the relevant elements.</p><p>The response can finish immediately. An SSE response does not require a permanent connection, and a live-search interaction does not require a dedicated streaming server.</p><p>Datastar signals handle transient browser state. Craft owns saved data, permissions and validation. The boundary is explicit without a separate frontend store or client-side router.</p><h2>One model for everyday interactions</h2><p>This site is a working example. The mobile menu, navigation dropdowns and search panel use Datastar, just like the blog filters, map filters and Todo List. There is no Alpine layer for the small interactions and another framework for the bigger ones.</p><p>Specialist tools still do specialist work: Leaflet draws the map, Embla handles the slider and GLightbox opens galleries. Datastar coordinates the ordinary UI and server-driven updates; it does not need to replace a mapping engine.</p><h2>When I would still choose Vue and GraphQL</h2><p>I would choose them when the product needs a separately deployed application, an API shared across several clients, or complex browser-side workflows that justify that architecture. This is not a claim that a server-rendered website can replace every application.</p><h2>See the smaller stack in practice</h2><p>Try the <a href=\\\"{entry:258@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/blog}\\\">filterable blog</a>, <a href=\\\"{entry:723@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/search}\\\">live search</a> and <a href=\\\"/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\\\">Todo List</a>. Each demonstrates a useful interaction while Craft remains responsible for the response.</p><p>For most Craft websites, that is the default I want: content in Craft, markup in Twig, reactivity in Datastar. <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">Craft Kit gives you the working starting point.</a></p>\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2026-11-13 15:50:56','64f67dc7-5c3f-462c-8e01-4858fb921668'),(982,982,1,NULL,'__temp_ztemfnobndtoeyiprvsiucxycbqsscckhhyt',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2><strong>⚡ Datastar + Twig Approach</strong></h2>\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','f7d8a54b-8b27-42e3-9a03-ddf52bc4339d'),(985,985,1,NULL,'__temp_cypbzsstsnbuyxakohhmvpjrxtfqzufmvbsg',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>When comparing both approaches, the contrast speaks for itself.</p><p>⚙️ <strong>Vue + GraphQL</strong> introduces multiple layers — components, queries, build steps, and state management — just to achieve basic interactivity.</p><p>And that’s only part of it. You also need to:</p><ul><li>Configure Vite and maintain a build pipeline</li><li>Define GraphQL schemas and set permissions</li><li>Handle authentication</li><li>Ship larger JavaScript bundles</li></ul><p>All of this adds weight to projects that often don’t need it.</p><p>🚀 <strong>Datastar</strong>, on the other hand, keeps everything close to the template.</p><p>It delivers reactivity and dynamic behavior without the complexity of a full frontend stack:</p><ul><li>No schema management</li><li>No complex routing</li><li>No hydration edge cases</li></ul><p>✨ And because Datastar also handles UI interactions like navigation, modals, or simple stateful components, I don’t even need Alpine.js anymore. One lightweight tool is enough.</p><p>✅ <strong>Lean. Fast. Maintainable.</strong></p><p>This setup fits most content-driven Craft CMS projects perfectly — modern interactivity without the frontend bloat.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','dfe4ecde-3aae-47e9-9bc6-54705bf00af3'),(986,986,1,'Why I Prefer Datastar Over Vue + GraphQL for Most Craft CMS Projects','why-i-prefer-datastar-over-vue-and-graphql','blog/why-i-prefer-datastar-over-vue-and-graphql','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-10-22 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [892], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why I Prefer Datastar Over Vue + GraphQL for Most Craft CMS Projects\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','32c41313-55c4-472f-9f64-f6fffb1b8bb2'),(987,987,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"41d42c36-230e-4e28-96f8-8a4801e9694e\": \"<p>Datastar gives me the speed and simplicity I need for most projects — without the overhead of a full frontend framework. Here’s why I often skip Vue + GraphQL.</p>\", \"914ae46d-5dd7-4afd-b5a3-32fbed3aecae\": [972]}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','b1927b1d-5a05-457a-a333-80330a9154f7'),(988,988,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Why I Prefer Datastar Over Vue + GraphQL for Most Craft CMS Projects\", \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Datastar gives me the speed and simplicity I need for most projects — without the overhead of a full frontend framework. Here’s why I often skip Vue + GraphQL.\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','a8c51b51-1f19-4824-b771-a73e61884ed8'),(989,989,1,NULL,'__temp_jstciagbxuaohtngrbfunmncynfgajzhhnep',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>When I first started working with Craft CMS, I loved pairing it with Vue and GraphQL. It felt powerful — almost limitless.</p><p>But over time, I realized something important: <strong>most projects don’t actually need a full frontend framework</strong>. What they need is something lean, reactive, and fast to build.</p><p>That’s where <a href=\\\"https://data-star.dev\\\"><strong>Datastar</strong></a> comes in — or more specifically, the <a href=\\\"https://plugins.craftcms.com/datastar\\\">Craft CMS Datastar plugin</a>.</p><p>Datastar lets me work directly in Twig, without juggling component states, hydration issues, or complicated build pipelines. It keeps my stack minimal — and my focus where it belongs: on the content and experience.</p><p>With Datastar, things stay refreshingly simple:</p><ul><li>✅ No build step for frontend state</li><li>🧭 No GraphQL boilerplate</li><li>🪶 No global stores or routing headaches</li></ul><p>I can sprinkle interactivity exactly where I need it — <strong>right inside my Twig templates</strong> — while keeping everything fast, reactive, and server-driven.</p><p>By contrast, working with Vue + GraphQL often meant:</p><ul><li>Defining and maintaining schemas and queries</li><li>Manually handling cache and reactivity</li><li>Debugging hydration issues between server and client</li></ul><p>With Datastar, I just add a few data- attributes — and I’m done.</p><p>My logic stays close to the markup. It scales surprisingly well. And the developer experience is honestly excellent.</p><p>Vue still has its place — for <strong>complex</strong>, highly dynamic UIs.</p><p>But for most <strong>content-heavy Craft CMS projects</strong>, Datastar is simply the faster, leaner, and more elegant solution.</p><h2><strong>🧱 Vue + GraphQL Approach</strong></h2>\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','68c1995d-09ad-45ec-8b4c-16afefb62e59'),(992,992,1,NULL,'__temp_ztemfnobndtoeyiprvsiucxycbqsscckhhyt',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2><strong>⚡ Datastar + Twig Approach</strong></h2>\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','8b1c07a4-e977-4be9-9708-3eb89f825f48'),(995,995,1,NULL,'__temp_cypbzsstsnbuyxakohhmvpjrxtfqzufmvbsg',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>When comparing both approaches, the contrast speaks for itself.</p><p>⚙️ <strong>Vue + GraphQL</strong> introduces multiple layers — components, queries, build steps, and state management — just to achieve basic interactivity.</p><p>And that’s only part of it. You also need to:</p><ul><li>Configure Vite and maintain a build pipeline</li><li>Define GraphQL schemas and set permissions</li><li>Handle authentication</li><li>Ship larger JavaScript bundles</li></ul><p>All of this adds weight to projects that often don’t need it.</p><p>🚀 <strong>Datastar</strong>, on the other hand, keeps everything close to the template.</p><p>It delivers reactivity and dynamic behavior without the complexity of a full frontend stack:</p><ul><li>No schema management</li><li>No complex routing</li><li>No hydration edge cases</li></ul><p>✨ And because Datastar also handles UI interactions like navigation, modals, or simple stateful components, I don’t even need Alpine.js anymore. One lightweight tool is enough.</p><p>✅ <strong>Lean. Fast. Maintainable.</strong></p><p>This setup fits most content-driven Craft CMS projects perfectly — modern interactivity without the frontend bloat.</p>\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:30','2025-10-23 08:22:30','f5cd80ac-1aa6-4cbd-95d4-cf739f99e405'),(996,996,1,'Why I Prefer Datastar Over Vue + GraphQL for Most Craft CMS Projects','why-i-prefer-datastar-over-vue-and-graphql','blog/why-i-prefer-datastar-over-vue-and-graphql','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-10-22 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [892], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why I Prefer Datastar Over Vue + GraphQL for Most Craft CMS Projects\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:22:32','2025-10-23 08:22:32','14a56e55-2999-4767-8b22-af3a306ffba0'),(999,999,1,'Why I Prefer Datastar Over Vue + GraphQL for Most Craft CMS Projects','why-i-prefer-datastar-over-vue-and-graphql','blog/why-i-prefer-datastar-over-vue-and-graphql','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-10-22 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [892], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why I Prefer Datastar Over Vue + GraphQL for Most Craft CMS Projects\"}',1,'2025-10-23 08:25:55','2025-10-23 08:25:55','94f10584-a34d-4d8e-8551-b90f1ef62f1b'),(1001,1001,1,'Showroom','layout',NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-23 08:33:28','2026-11-13 14:57:03','ad634ac0-3ecb-4a35-8b20-d7900caac6bd'),(1002,1002,1,'Layout','layout',NULL,NULL,1,'2025-10-23 08:33:35','2025-10-23 08:33:35','3b005a2b-726e-4b51-bf37-6d70a43fd2fe'),(1004,1004,1,'Grid','layout',NULL,'{\"5e2baca9-5c68-4147-b9e7-0df1a3d033d9\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Grid\", \"value\": \"/layout\"}}',1,'2025-10-23 08:33:52','2025-10-23 08:33:52','b2e11ed2-3c6f-4a01-9965-63a244ef9211'),(1014,1014,1,'GM 1500',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2025-11-04 13:26:17','2025-11-04 13:26:17','82b8b3ad-e047-4878-a1e5-d50034b3430e'),(1019,1019,1,'Home','home','__home__','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"CraftCMS Lazy —\\nA simple Craft CMS Starter Kit\"}',1,'2025-11-04 13:30:52','2025-11-04 13:30:52','bb241677-7c6d-4db5-b3e7-af9db8e27cbc'),(1020,1020,1,NULL,'__temp_xmyryjgfvmihfecdlkmvkhurafqliwjajpcz',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A modern, production-ready Craft CMS Starter Kit with Vite, Tailwind, Vue Web Components, Datastar, GraphQL and DDEV — perfect for agencies and freelancers who want to build clean and fast Craft sites..</p><p>This starter kit helps developers quickly spin up clean and maintainable Craft CMS projects. It includes ready-made examples for Matrix Blocks, CKEditor integration, a Datastar-powered Search page, and both Datastar- and Vue-based blog listings.</p><p><strong>🧠 Built with modern tools and clean architecture</strong></p><ul><li>⚙️ <strong>Craft CMS 5</strong> – latest version with flexible content modeling</li><li>⚡ <strong>Vite</strong> – fast bundling and instant reloads</li><li>🧩 <strong>DDEV</strong> – reproducible local development environment</li><li>🚀 <strong>Datastar</strong> – lightweight, reactive frontend for dynamic UIs</li><li>🧱 <strong>Vue 3 (Web Components)</strong> – progressive enhancement with custom elements</li><li>🔗 <strong>GraphQL</strong> – structured data fetching directly from Craft</li><li>🎨 <strong>Tailwind CSS v4</strong> – utility-first styling with CSS variables</li><li>🎞️ <strong>Anime.js</strong> – smooth element animations and scroll-based transitions</li><li>🗃️ <strong>Craft eagerly() + render()</strong> – optimized queries, automatic block templates, and smart caching</li><li><strong>🧾 SEO-Ready JSON-LD Organization Schema </strong>– structured data for Google Rich Results</li><li>🔍 <strong>SEO Meta, Open Graph &amp; Sitemap </strong>– powered by SEOMate for share-friendly pages</li><li>🔌 <strong>Plugins:</strong> CKEditor, Datastar, Image Resizer, SEOMate, Vite</li></ul><p>💻 Feel free to explore, fork, or contribute — this starter kit is open source and available on <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">GitHub</a>.</p>\"}',1,'2025-11-04 13:30:53','2025-11-04 13:30:53','7f0242b2-5ff0-419a-b893-bfa899ea80e4'),(1023,1023,1,'Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress','craft-vs-wordpress','blog/craft-vs-wordpress','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-10-20 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [876], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress\"}',1,'2025-11-05 07:50:19','2025-11-05 07:50:19','2855e028-b84e-4805-bd48-70e9ac0763f6'),(1024,1024,1,NULL,'__temp_epuxgsbappmctwahfdpzjemvchoaohitwwwg',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">For many agencies and developers, WordPress has been the go-to CMS for years. It’s familiar, has a massive ecosystem, and is well-known to clients.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">But <i>familiarity isn’t always the same as fit</i>.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Craft CMS isn’t trying to be WordPress — and that’s exactly why it’s winning the hearts of designers, developers, and clients who want clean, flexible sites without the plugin chaos.</p><h2><strong>Clean by Default</strong></h2><p>WordPress often starts out lean but quickly turns into a plugin maze. Craft CMS, on the other hand, comes with just what you need — nothing more, nothing less. No “Hello Dolly,” no page builder you didn’t ask for, no endless menu items.</p><p>👉 <strong>Result:</strong> Faster projects, fewer surprises, and cleaner codebases.</p><h2><strong>Developer First (But Friendly for Editors)</strong></h2><p>Craft is designed with developers in mind — structured content modeling, clean templating, and predictable behavior. But it also gives editors a <i>beautiful and intuitive</i> authoring experience. No clutter, no 30 different side panels. If you’ve ever tried to train a client in WordPress Gutenberg, you’ll know what I mean.</p><h2><strong>Performance Without a Fight</strong></h2><p>With WordPress, good performance often requires caching plugins, optimization tools, and server tweaks. Craft is fast out of the box — Twig templates, caching layers, and asset transforms are built in. That means fewer dependencies, less debugging, and a snappier experience overall.</p><h2><strong>Freedom for Designers</strong></h2><p>WordPress often bends you towards themes and blocks. Craft gives you a blank canvas. That’s why agencies love it — you can build <i>your</i> design system, not someone else’s. It’s like the difference between renting a furnished apartment and building your own loft.</p><h2><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2><p>WordPress isn’t bad — but Craft CMS is often a better fit for modern teams who want clarity, control, and clean output.</p><p>If you want a deeper breakdown of why teams move from WordPress to Craft — especially around performance, security, and content flexibility — the official comparison is worth a look:<br />👉 C<a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/vs-wordpress\\\">raft CMS vs WordPress</a></p><p>If you’re thinking about switching, Craft even provides a clear migration path from WordPress.  <br />👉 <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/blog/migrating-from-wordpress\\\">Official guide: Migrating from WordPress</a></p><p>✅ <strong>Tip:</strong> If you’re setting up Craft CMS for the first time, try starting from my a well-structured <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">starter kit</a>. It saves hours of setup time.</p><p> </p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\"> </p>\"}',1,'2025-11-05 07:50:19','2025-11-05 07:50:19','3f5557ef-6ae6-441a-97cb-dca79556c958'),(1027,1027,1,'Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress','craft-vs-wordpress','blog/craft-vs-wordpress','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-10-20 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [876], \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Why Craft CMS Might Be a Better Fit Than WordPress\"}',1,'2025-11-05 07:50:52','2025-11-05 07:50:52','75798977-8ff4-4a26-b889-edddafcfa3f4'),(1028,1028,1,NULL,'__temp_epuxgsbappmctwahfdpzjemvchoaohitwwwg',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">For many agencies and developers, WordPress has been the go-to CMS for years. It’s familiar, has a massive ecosystem, and is well-known to clients.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">But <i>familiarity isn’t always the same as fit</i>.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Craft CMS isn’t trying to be WordPress — and that’s exactly why it’s winning the hearts of designers, developers, and clients who want clean, flexible sites without the plugin chaos.</p><h2><strong>Clean by Default</strong></h2><p>WordPress often starts out lean but quickly turns into a plugin maze. Craft CMS, on the other hand, comes with just what you need — nothing more, nothing less. No “Hello Dolly,” no page builder you didn’t ask for, no endless menu items.</p><p>👉 <strong>Result:</strong> Faster projects, fewer surprises, and cleaner codebases.</p><h2><strong>Developer First (But Friendly for Editors)</strong></h2><p>Craft is designed with developers in mind — structured content modeling, clean templating, and predictable behavior. But it also gives editors a <i>beautiful and intuitive</i> authoring experience. No clutter, no 30 different side panels. If you’ve ever tried to train a client in WordPress Gutenberg, you’ll know what I mean.</p><h2><strong>Performance Without a Fight</strong></h2><p>With WordPress, good performance often requires caching plugins, optimization tools, and server tweaks. Craft is fast out of the box — Twig templates, caching layers, and asset transforms are built in. That means fewer dependencies, less debugging, and a snappier experience overall.</p><h2><strong>Freedom for Designers</strong></h2><p>WordPress often bends you towards themes and blocks. Craft gives you a blank canvas. That’s why agencies love it — you can build <i>your</i> design system, not someone else’s. It’s like the difference between renting a furnished apartment and building your own loft.</p><h2><strong>Conclusion</strong></h2><p>WordPress isn’t bad — but Craft CMS is often a better fit for modern teams who want clarity, control, and clean output.</p><p>If you want a deeper breakdown of why teams move from WordPress to Craft — especially around performance, security, and content flexibility — the official comparison is worth a look:<br />👉 <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/vs-wordpress\\\">Craft CMS vs WordPress</a></p><p>If you’re thinking about switching, Craft even provides a clear migration path from WordPress.  <br />👉 <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/blog/migrating-from-wordpress\\\">Official guide: Migrating from WordPress</a></p><p>✅ <strong>Tip:</strong> If you’re setting up Craft CMS for the first time, try starting from my a well-structured <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">starter kit</a>. It saves hours of setup time.</p><p> </p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\"> </p>\"}',1,'2025-11-05 07:50:52','2025-11-05 07:50:52','f536f390-2ff6-47e4-902a-74e56becbb8e'),(1029,1029,1,'Map','datastar-map','map','{\"0c03aeb7-3181-4eb2-93bf-4bba1f224c26\": \"Interactive Maps in Craft CMS — Datastar & Leaflet Demo — Dynamic markers, category filters, and clustering — powered by Craft CMS, Leaflet, and Datastar. A hypermedia-driven map built entirely in Twig, with the server as the single source of truth\", \"2b51574c-5057-4c70-9a63-3e3612eb11b0\": \"<h1><strong>Interactive Maps in Craft CMS — Datastar &amp; Leaflet Demo</strong></h1><p>Interactive, data-driven maps in Craft CMS — dynamic markers, category filters, and clustering, all rendered in Twig. Leaflet handles the map, Datastar manages reactivity over SSE. No JavaScript framework, no page reloads, no client-side state. Just  \\n  fast, server-rendered geodata — perfect for directories, location listings, or event maps.</p>\", \"9c489dde-d3e4-48c2-835e-1cd576c86441\": 0}',1,'2025-11-07 12:29:18','2026-04-20 15:16:10','1486f15a-d125-4512-8fd0-184417dec6c6'),(1030,1030,1,'Map','map','map',NULL,1,'2025-11-07 12:29:18','2025-11-07 12:29:18','0c73622c-6055-484c-878e-b01c3ad020c6'),(1031,1031,1,'Home','home','__home__','{\"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"CraftCMS Lazy —\\nA simple Craft CMS Starter Kit\"}',1,'2025-11-07 12:29:57','2025-11-07 12:29:57','ecb7de48-e7fe-4f67-b928-affe2df09679'),(1032,1032,1,NULL,'__temp_xmyryjgfvmihfecdlkmvkhurafqliwjajpcz',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A modern, production-ready Craft CMS Starter Kit with Vite, Tailwind, Vue Web Components, Datastar, GraphQL and DDEV — perfect for agencies and freelancers who want to build clean and fast Craft sites..</p><p>This starter kit helps developers quickly spin up clean and maintainable Craft CMS projects. It includes ready-made examples for Matrix Blocks, CKEditor integration, a Datastar-powered Search page, and both Datastar- and Vue-based blog listings.</p><p><strong>🧠 Built with modern tools and clean architecture</strong></p><ul><li>⚙️ <strong>Craft CMS 5</strong> – latest version with flexible content modeling</li><li>⚡ <strong>Vite</strong> – fast bundling and instant reloads</li><li>🧩 <strong>DDEV</strong> – reproducible local development environment</li><li>🚀 <strong>Datastar</strong> – lightweight, reactive frontend for dynamic UIs</li><li>🗺️ <strong>Leaflet</strong> – interactive, data-driven maps with clustering and live filtering</li><li>🧱 <strong>Vue 3 (Web Components)</strong> – progressive enhancement with custom elements</li><li>🔗 <strong>GraphQL</strong> – structured data fetching directly from Craft</li><li>🎨 <strong>Tailwind CSS v4</strong> – utility-first styling with CSS variables</li><li>🎞️ <strong>Anime.js</strong> – smooth element animations and scroll-based transitions</li><li>🗃️ <strong>Craft eagerly() + render()</strong> – optimized queries, automatic block templates, and smart caching</li><li><strong>🧾 SEO-Ready JSON-LD Organization Schema </strong>– structured data for Google Rich Results</li><li>🔍 <strong>SEO Meta, Open Graph &amp; Sitemap </strong>– powered by SEOMate for share-friendly pages</li><li>🔌 <strong>Plugins:</strong> CKEditor, Datastar, Image Resizer, SEOMate, Vite</li></ul><p>💻 Feel free to explore, fork, or contribute — this starter kit is open source and available on <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">GitHub</a>.</p>\"}',1,'2025-11-07 12:29:57','2025-11-07 12:29:57','75a7e947-fd25-4214-9571-6e67553fe07b'),(1034,1034,1,'Development','development',NULL,'{\"a8247aa8-49d4-46eb-9425-55d63c4de5ca\": \"#bf6e6e\"}',1,'2025-11-07 12:30:29','2025-11-07 12:30:29','3708bb40-f84b-4b48-8544-492c5a521dbf'),(1036,1036,1,'Opinion','opinion',NULL,'{\"a8247aa8-49d4-46eb-9425-55d63c4de5ca\": \"#50b9a4\"}',1,'2025-11-07 12:3