: \"Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2026-03-24 09:59:48','2026-03-24 09:59:48','fbaf30b2-f946-4d95-8966-e6b2805a0031'),(2068,2068,1,'Tailwind + Twig in the Zed Editor','tailwind-twig-and-the-zed-editor','blog/tailwind-twig-and-the-zed-editor','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2025-11-17 23:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [892], \"7f45d57a-6089-4476-9875-732dfa47a1a0\": {\"id\": 19, \"lat\": 53.550341, \"lng\": 10.000654, \"zoom\": 15, \"parts\": {\"arm\": \"Orion Arm\", \"city\": \"Hamburg\", \"group\": \"the Local Group\", \"state\": \"\", \"county\": \"\", \"galaxy\": \"Milky Way\", \"number\": \"\", \"planet\": \"Earth\", \"system\": \"the Solar System\", \"address\": \"\", \"cluster\": \"Virgo Cluster\", \"country\": \"Germany\", \"postcode\": \"\", \"supercluster\": \"Laniakea Supercluster\"}, \"address\": \"Hamburg, Germany\", \"fieldId\": 35, \"ownerId\": null, \"distance\": null, \"what3words\": null, \"ownerSiteId\": 1}, \"d74fbbee-f4c8-448b-b8fc-d5723a6d0f07\": 0, \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Tailwind + Twig in the Zed Editor\"}',1,'2026-03-26 16:41:55','2026-03-26 16:41:55','07a9dae5-e76a-4a0f-b823-09656706f819'),(2069,2069,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"41d42c36-230e-4e28-96f8-8a4801e9694e\": \"<p>Making Tailwind IntelliSense, Twig syntax &amp; Prettier all work together</p>\", \"914ae46d-5dd7-4afd-b5a3-32fbed3aecae\": [1196]}',1,'2026-03-26 16:41:55','2026-03-26 16:41:55','fc6b0840-e54a-4a97-89ed-1d5cd36919fd'),(2070,2070,1,NULL,'__temp_vzhwwxlrcexubrqwmorpeiowbdqyozhwoacz',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Working with <strong>Craft CMS</strong>, <strong>Twig templates</strong>, and <strong>Tailwind CSS</strong> inside <strong>Zed</strong> is amazing — <i>once everything works</i>.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Out of the box, Zed doesn’t fully understand Twig, and Tailwind IntelliSense won’t fire inside .twig files.</p><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Here’s the full guide to fixing that — including Twig syntax, Tailwind autocomplete, Emmet, and Prettier formatting.</p><h2><strong>Zed Extensions</strong></h2><p>Install these extensions in Zed:</p><ul><li><p><strong>Twig Extension</strong> → Syntax highlighting + LSP</p><p>👉 <i>Important:</i> <a href=\\\"https://github.com/YussufSassi/zed-twig\\\"><strong>Read the README</strong></a> to enable Emmet inside Twig</p></li><li><strong>Emmet</strong> → HTML/Twig abbreviation expansion</li></ul>\"}',1,'2026-03-26 16:41:55','2026-03-26 16:41:55','2b452cdb-4a89-4981-b5a4-ad2af25863fe'),(2071,2071,1,NULL,'__temp_qowybonnqcvzwobvxqfaucbcbwessmwuxurg',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2><strong>Node modules</strong></h2><p>To make Prettier format both Twig templates and Tailwind classes correctly, install:</p><ul><li><strong>prettier</strong></li><li><strong>prettier-plugin-tailwindcss</strong></li><li><strong>@zackad/prettier-plugin-twig</strong></li></ul><p> </p>\"}',1,'2026-03-26 16:41:55','2026-03-26 16:41:55','f391ddd8-17da-4ced-bd05-9bc9f17dabdf'),(2072,2072,1,NULL,'__temp_btrakhakhltdejmlxuspasfgovtunhqhugcp',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2><strong>🎉 Final result</strong></h2><p>With everything set up:</p><ul><li>Tailwind IntelliSense <strong>inside Twig</strong></li><li>Emmet expansions in Twig</li><li>Clean Twig formatting</li><li>Auto-sorted Tailwind classes</li><li>Full support for Craft CMS workflows</li></ul><p>Zed becomes a fast, lightweight dev environment for <strong>Craft CMS + Tailwind</strong>.</p>\"}',1,'2026-03-26 16:41:55','2026-03-26 16:41:55','fcfc1221-f434-4d3a-b4a0-ec6925d73897'),(2073,2073,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Tailwind + Twig in the Zed Editor\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Making Tailwind IntelliSense, Twig syntax & Prettier all work together\"}',1,'2026-03-26 16:41:55','2026-03-26 16:41:55','f666c60a-0328-4e13-8102-d72173d6328e'),(2074,2074,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-26 16:41:56','2026-03-26 16:41:56','c93c3bdc-3197-45ef-b841-338cfa2021fe'),(2075,2075,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-26 16:41:56','2026-03-26 16:41:56','66879a56-3f28-4301-8cf2-c06fe602647a'),(2076,2076,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-26 16:41:56','2026-03-26 16:41:56','088e1570-73b4-4341-9b74-2d9dac5ef23c'),(2078,2078,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Matrix Builder\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"Matrix Builder – Modular Content Blocks for Craft CMS — Explore how flexible content creation works in Craft CMS using Matrix fields. Each component is reusable, responsive, and fits seamlessly into the custom Grid Layout system.\"}',1,'2026-04-10 08:47:39','2026-04-10 08:47:39','f48f4bb5-6de7-40a5-b914-22471db430f7'),(2079,2079,1,'Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice','making-craft-cms-ai-ready-what-geo-actually-means-in-practice','blog/making-craft-cms-ai-ready-what-geo-actually-means-in-practice','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2026-04-09 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [892], \"7f45d57a-6089-4476-9875-732dfa47a1a0\": {\"id\": null, \"lat\": 51.2254018, \"lng\": 6.7763137, \"zoom\": 15, \"parts\": {\"arm\": \"Orion Arm\", \"city\": \"Dusseldorf\", \"group\": \"the Local Group\", \"state\": \"North Rhine-Westphalia\", \"county\": \"\", \"galaxy\": \"Milky Way\", \"number\": \"\", \"planet\": \"Earth\", \"system\": \"the Solar System\", \"address\": \"\", \"cluster\": \"Virgo Cluster\", \"country\": \"Germany\", \"postcode\": \"\", \"supercluster\": \"Laniakea Supercluster\"}, \"address\": \"Dusseldorf, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany\", \"fieldId\": 35, \"ownerId\": 2079, \"distance\": null, \"what3words\": null, \"ownerSiteId\": 1}, \"d74fbbee-f4c8-448b-b8fc-d5723a6d0f07\": 0, \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice\"}',1,'2026-04-10 08:47:59','2026-11-13 15:41:27','f92fcc66-38b2-4919-88fa-a46279570263'),(2080,2080,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"41d42c36-230e-4e28-96f8-8a4801e9694e\": \"<p>Make Craft content easier for AI tools to read with Markdown, clear structure and reusable SEO descriptions. A practical setup, without ranking promises.</p>\", \"914ae46d-5dd7-4afd-b5a3-32fbed3aecae\": [2691]}',1,'2026-04-10 08:48:00','2026-11-13 15:45:53','14ee2f2f-7609-4eba-a509-c0b8fb58f6a6'),(2081,2081,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Make Craft content easier for AI tools to read with Markdown, clear structure and reusable SEO descriptions. A practical setup, without ranking promises.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": [2691]}',1,'2026-04-10 08:48:00','2026-11-13 15:53:19','f11f0268-d383-4ca7-81ec-cec22c3b35ff'),(2082,2082,1,NULL,'__temp_wtragnbaiqmezzfuowubqopgdsfnzyxnmjgb',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Making a website useful to AI tools starts with the same work that helps people: clear content, meaningful headings and reliable links. Craft Kit adds machine-friendly output without maintaining a second copy of every article.</p><h2>Readable content comes first</h2><p>AI tools can process HTML, but a page may contain navigation, scripts and other material that obscures its main content. A well-structured Markdown representation can make that content easier to extract and work with.</p><p>Craft Kit uses the LLM Ready plugin to offer Markdown output. Clients that request <strong>Accept: text/markdown</strong> can receive a readable representation at the same page URL. Support for that request pattern varies between tools; it is not a promise that every crawler will use it.</p><h2>One content model, several representations</h2><p>The article remains editor-managed in Craft. Twig produces the website; machine-readable output is generated from the same source. There is no parallel documentation tree for editors to keep synchronized.</p><p>This matches the reason I use Datastar for the frontend: let Craft remain responsible for the content, and return the representation the interaction needs. HTML powers the visitor\'s interface; Markdown can serve a reading tool.</p><h2>What llms.txt can and cannot do</h2><p>An auto-generated <strong>llms.txt</strong> can act as a concise index for tools that choose to read it. It is not a replacement for a sitemap, robots directives, accessible HTML or good internal linking.</p><p>There is no ranking guarantee attached to publishing it. Adoption and crawler behavior change, so I would not build a marketing promise around it. I keep the index generated rather than asking editors to maintain another manual file.</p><h2>Reuse the descriptions you already write</h2><p>A useful SEO description can also summarize an article for a content index. Reusing it avoids another field that repeats the same editorial job. The important part is an accurate summary, not filling a special AI keyword slot.</p><h2>A practical checklist</h2><ol><li>Publish useful content with a clear heading structure.</li><li>Keep canonical URLs and internal links reliable.</li><li>Provide readable Markdown for clients that request it.</li><li>Generate an index from the existing content model.</li><li>Review the actual output instead of assuming a plugin guarantees visibility.</li></ol><p>For the reactive side of the same server-first approach, try the <a href=\\\"{entry:258@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/blog}\\\">Datastar blog</a> and <a href=\\\"{entry:723@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/search}\\\">live search</a>. Their content remains rendered by Craft rather than being hidden behind a separate frontend application.</p><p><a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">Explore Craft Kit on GitHub</a> to inspect the templates and configuration. Treat the AI-friendly output as a practical capability, not a guarantee of traffic, citations or rankings.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-10 08:48:06','2026-11-13 15:50:56','6a9ca5b4-9b35-41f5-9272-afc4c9c0b0bd'),(2083,2083,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-10 08:48:06','2026-04-10 08:48:06','d433ee6e-0553-4153-bfe5-2a5ebc4e0f39'),(2084,2084,1,'Nahrizul kadri O As F0 QMR Wl A unsplash',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-10 08:59:59','2026-04-10 08:59:59','5f0ef165-940d-4d1a-98af-44741760408d'),(2085,2085,1,'Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice','making-craft-cms-ai-ready-what-geo-actually-means-in-practice','blog/making-craft-cms-ai-ready-what-geo-actually-means-in-practice','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2026-04-09 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [892], \"7f45d57a-6089-4476-9875-732dfa47a1a0\": {\"id\": 53, \"lat\": 51.2254018, \"lng\": 6.7763137, \"zoom\": 15, \"parts\": {\"arm\": \"Orion Arm\", \"city\": \"Dusseldorf\", \"group\": \"the Local Group\", \"state\": \"North Rhine-Westphalia\", \"county\": \"\", \"galaxy\": \"Milky Way\", \"number\": \"\", \"planet\": \"Earth\", \"system\": \"the Solar System\", \"address\": \"\", \"cluster\": \"Virgo Cluster\", \"country\": \"Germany\", \"postcode\": \"\", \"supercluster\": \"Laniakea Supercluster\"}, \"address\": \"Dusseldorf, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany\", \"fieldId\": 35, \"ownerId\": null, \"distance\": null, \"what3words\": null, \"ownerSiteId\": 1}, \"8ea3656a-4096-4563-af60-555454f92e16\": \"Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice — GEO is full of hype. Here\'s what I actually implemented in Craft Kit  to make it AI-agent ready — what works, what doesn\'t, and what you  can safely ignore.\", \"d74fbbee-f4c8-448b-b8fc-d5723a6d0f07\": 0, \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice\"}',1,'2026-04-10 09:02:26','2026-04-10 09:02:26','3801cbb4-b756-44ec-87ac-07946ab2a9e1'),(2086,2086,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"41d42c36-230e-4e28-96f8-8a4801e9694e\": \"<p>GEO is the new SEO — but most of what you read about it is either theoretical or plain wrong. Here\'s what I actually implemented in Craft Kit, what works, and what you can safely ignore.</p>\", \"914ae46d-5dd7-4afd-b5a3-32fbed3aecae\": [2084]}',1,'2026-04-10 09:02:26','2026-04-10 09:02:26','b3ec314e-df3a-4a79-9bc9-fdafdec9f5ce'),(2087,2087,1,NULL,'__temp_wtragnbaiqmezzfuowubqopgdsfnzyxnmjgb',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Everyone\'s talking about Generative Engine Optimization. Most articles explain the same three concepts and call it a day. So instead of writing another overview, I want to share what I actually did to make Craft Kit AI-agent ready — and be honest about what matters and what doesn\'t.</p><h2>The one thing that actually works: serving Markdown</h2><p>LLMs understand text. Not HTML — text. A typical HTML page is full of navigation, scripts, SVGs, cookie banners, and a hundred other things an AI agent has to filter through just to get to your content. Markdown cuts all of that out.</p><p>The good news: there\'s already a standard for this. AI agents like Claude Code send an HTTP Accept header with text/markdown. If your server responds accordingly, the agent gets a clean Markdown version of your page — same URL, no separate route, no magic.</p><p>Craft Kit now supports this out of the box via the LLM Ready plugin. Every page automatically has a Markdown version, and the Accept header is handled for you. Token usage for agents drops significantly. Content is easier to process. Everyone wins.</p><h2>llms.txt — useful, but not what you think</h2><p>There\'s a lot of hype around llms.txt. The idea is simple: a file at your site root that acts as an AI-friendly sitemap, linking to Markdown versions of your pages with short descriptions.</p><p>Here\'s the honest reality: no major AI provider officially uses it. Google\'s John Mueller said it plainly in mid-2025 — no AI system currently reads llms.txt. An audit of 1,000 domains confirmed that LLM-specific bots like ClaudeBot or GPTBot don\'t fetch it at all.</p><p>That said, I kept it in Craft Kit — and here\'s why. The cost is near zero when it\'s auto-generated. For developer tooling and documentation sites like craft-kit.dev, it\'s the exact use case where it could eventually matter. And if adoption does pick up, you\'re already set.</p><p>What I\'d avoid: manually maintaining a llms.txt, treating it as an SEO lever, or including pages like Imprint and Privacy Policy in the index. None of that helps anyone.</p><h2>Recycling SEO fields for GEO</h2><p>One small practical win: the LLM Ready plugin lets you define which field to use as the description in your llms.txt entries. Instead of adding a new field, I pointed it at the existing SEO meta description. It\'s already written, already concise, and already describes the page accurately.</p><p>Less duplication, more signal.</p><h2>What I skipped</h2><p>A few things I looked at and decided against:</p><p><strong>&lt;script type=\\\"text/llms.txt\\\"&gt;</strong> — a Vercel proposal that embeds LLM-facing content directly in the HTML via an unknown script type. Clever idea, but browsers still load the full HTML and no AI provider actively reads it. Not worth the effort.</p><p><strong>A separate /docs section in Markdown</strong> — some sites maintain full parallel documentation in Markdown. For a demo project like Craft Kit this would be overkill. The per-page Markdown generation covers it.</p><h2>The short version</h2><p>If you want your Craft CMS site to be AI-agent ready:</p><ol><li>Serve Markdown on Accept: text/markdown — this is the only thing with real, confirmed adoption right now</li><li>Add a llms.txt as an auto-generated link index — low effort, no downside</li><li>Use your existing SEO descriptions as LLM descriptions</li><li>Keep focusing on good SEO and accessibility — if a screen reader struggles with your content, so will an AI</li></ol><p><strong>Craft Kit has all of this set up out of the box. One less thing to figure out.</strong></p>\"}',1,'2026-04-10 09:02:26','2026-04-10 09:02:26','ab4fdce1-761b-44f5-bb31-414fdc66c265'),(2088,2088,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-10 09:02:26','2026-04-10 09:02:26','b0fdbec3-be55-43bb-955b-134700fce1ef'),(2089,2089,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"GEO is full of hype. Here\'s what I actually implemented in Craft Kit  to make it AI-agent ready — what works, what doesn\'t, and what you  can safely ignore.\"}',1,'2026-04-10 09:02:26','2026-04-10 09:02:26','c3c96997-30d3-4879-96d8-8574caa30a10'),(2090,2090,1,'Making Craft CMS AI-Ready — What GEO Actually Means in Practice','making-craft-cms-ai-ready-what-geo-actually-means-in-practice','blog/making-craft-cms-ai-ready-what-geo-actually-means-in-practice','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2026-04-09 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [892], \"7f45d57a-6089-4476-9875-732dfa47a1a0\": {\"id\": 53, \"lat\": 51.2254018, \"lng\": 6.7763137, \"zoom\": 15, \"parts\": {\"arm\": \"Orion Arm\", \"city\": \"Dusseldorf\", \"group\": \"the Local Group\", \"state\": \"North Rhine-Westphalia\", \"county\": \"\", \"galaxy\": \"Milky Way\", \"number\": \"\", \"planet\": \"Earth\", \"system\": \"the Solar System\", \"address\": \"\", \"cluster\": \"Virgo Cluster\", \"country\": \"Germany\", \"postcode\": \"\", \"supercluster\": \"Laniakea Supercluster\"}, \"address\": \"Dusseldorf, North Rhine-Westphalia, Germany\", \"fieldId\": 35, \"ownerId\": null, \"distance\": null, \"what3words\": null, \"ownerSiteId\": 1}, \"8ea36