t-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">No headless. No JavaScript framework. Just a clean, fast, production-ready foundation.</p>\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:05:02','2026-04-24 09:05:02','82ed9672-2a55-4e3a-a3fb-a9f6250875e7'),(2267,2267,1,'Lighthouse',NULL,NULL,'{\"e30c17b9-ffa5-4343-99ee-0f780e5e0ed0\": \"craft-kit.dev — 100/100 across all Lighthouse categories. No optimization pass required.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:19:57','2026-04-24 10:29:32','7d35691c-6d09-427d-8f9e-e5bbdcde42a8'),(2268,2268,1,NULL,'__temp_tjghqsvjgikvfdrdidfeseyugvzrcuhuvdbq',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [2267]}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:31','2026-04-24 10:16:50','9689b1be-cee6-4936-a567-ebaf571f057a'),(2269,2269,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:20:31','2026-04-24 09:20:31','fdde5db2-53fc-452b-a63f-8423fa6c41b7'),(2270,2270,1,NULL,'__temp_smioappptayceknmwyajesgotnfvyuynwqsc',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','5f3bb36f-fc29-401a-b70a-353d5f5b46d5'),(2271,2271,1,NULL,'__temp_rfpzhuavpwnodthqdldvgcwrjjverleqvhiv',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Craft CMS live search with Datastar\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:723@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Instant filtering, server side</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 10:16:50','2ce94ec2-6ab4-4cfe-99a0-83b7dd78426e'),(2272,2272,1,NULL,'__temp_gqijinpoaxfblxwszfodbcbygfkheupzzmiu',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Craft CMS blog listing with Datastar\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>paginated, filtered, reactive</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 10:16:50','20422ac1-04a4-4ba8-8c2c-a70d4b1a2945'),(2273,2273,1,NULL,'__temp_exakmyjhftiekvarjwtneocfrkitaunruopc',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Craft CMS. todo list with Datastar\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Todos\", \"value\": \"https://craft-kit.dev/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Full CRUD, no JS framework</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 10:16:50','f688f87b-04b2-44b6-bdf8-ae274d66fced'),(2274,2274,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','8c790774-ca94-42a3-b017-5cc4908bc0fe'),(2275,2275,1,NULL,'__temp_kxwhfgistwnjjblgiuvkzaeavgpetxpswgzl',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Examples you can follow</h2><p>The demos show individual patterns you can inspect and adapt:</p><ul><li><a href=\\\"/blog\\\">Blog</a> — filter posts and load more results.</li><li><a href=\\\"/map\\\">Map</a> — filter locations and display them on an interactive map.</li><li><a href=\\\"/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\\\">Todo List</a> — add, complete and delete tasks.</li><li><a href=\\\"/search\\\">Search</a> — update results as you type.</li></ul><p>The <a href=\\\"/builder\\\">Builder demo</a> compares reusable page blocks in Matrix with components embedded in CKEditor. Both use the same Twig templates with rendering suited to their context.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-11-13 15:00:24','2ee1575f-3b45-4bf0-bf67-37b9a36f590f'),(2276,2276,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','c9bd9f51-d836-4544-b1e7-6d5580dafdfd'),(2277,2277,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">No headless. No JavaScript framework. Just a clean, fast, production-ready foundation.</p>\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','fc491f8b-00b9-41f8-bb4f-2168cb241fad'),(2278,2278,1,NULL,'__temp_gyydugypgvjiequfbxcuomsbyqstomnyqdeo',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>Most agency stacks are overbuilt. A React frontend talking to a headless CMS through a GraphQL API — deployed across three services, maintained by a team of specialists, and introduced to a client who just wants to update a text block.</p><p>Craft Kit is the alternative. A single, opinionated starter kit for Craft CMS 5 that ships with everything a modern project needs and nothing it doesn\'t.</p><blockquote><p>Craft Kit is a scaffold, not a theme. It gives you a structured starting point with established patterns and sane defaults — then gets out of the way. Every part of it is meant to be adapted, extended, or replaced to fit the project at hand.</p></blockquote><h2>Why Craft CMS?</h2><p>Craft is one of the few CMS platforms that gets content modeling right. Fields, sections, entry types, Matrix blocks — the authoring experience is flexible enough for complex projects and simple enough that clients actually use it without training. It doesn\'t force a data structure on you. You build exactly what the project needs.</p><p>And the platform is moving in the right direction. Craft 6, due in late 2026, is being built as a Laravel package — meaning it can be dropped into any existing Laravel application and treated as a first-class dependency. The full Laravel ecosystem becomes available: packages, middleware, tooling, and a talent pool that\'s orders of magnitude larger than any niche PHP framework. For agencies evaluating long-term platform risk, that matters.</p><p>Craft 5 is now an LTS release, with five years of support guaranteed after Craft 6 ships. There is no pressure to migrate before you\'re ready.</p><h2>Why not headless?</h2><p>Headless architecture makes sense for a specific set of problems: native mobile apps consuming the same API, highly distributed content teams, microsecond performance SLAs at massive scale. For most agency projects, it introduces complexity without solving anything the client actually asked for.</p><p>The Hypermedia approach — server-rendered HTML, enriched where needed with lightweight interactivity — delivers the same results with a fraction of the moving parts. Craft CMS handles content modeling and rendering. Twig handles templating. Datastar handles the reactive bits. That\'s the whole stack.</p><blockquote><p>Same UX. Faster development. Fewer dependencies. Easier onboarding for the next developer on the project.</p></blockquote><h2><strong>100 across the board</strong></h2><p>The demo site runs 100 across the board — not as a benchmark exercise, but as a direct consequence of the architecture. Server-rendered HTML is fast. Semantic markup is accessible. Clean output is indexable.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','c04f7e52-b6a3-4ff3-8b17-fa065d156734'),(2279,2279,1,NULL,'__temp_tjghqsvjgikvfdrdidfeseyugvzrcuhuvdbq',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": false, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [2267]}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','de054afa-2793-493c-ab4e-d3eb1e8e6661'),(2280,2280,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','2797f24c-6ceb-4891-8939-7f1a4f29ee41'),(2281,2281,1,NULL,'__temp_qyczkdevkhsquglcuaumrjenkyenhcmoklto',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>These scores hold without any special optimization pass. They are the baseline, not the goal.</p><h2>The stack</h2><p><strong>Craft CMS 5, Twig, Datastar, Vite, Tailwind CSS, DDEV, SEOMate</strong><br /><strong>— and nothing else.</strong></p><p>Every tool has a reason to be here. DDEV ensures every developer on the team gets the same local environment on day one. Vite handles asset bundling with instant HMR. SEOMate covers Open Graph, meta, and sitemaps without configuration overhead. Datastar replaces the need for a JavaScript framework wherever reactivity is required.</p><p>What is not in the stack is just as deliberate: no React, no Vue, no Next.js, no GraphQL, no separate API layer.</p><h2>Datastar demos — real-world patterns</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with working examples of the most common reactive UI patterns, built with Datastar and server-rendered Twig. No JavaScript build step. No component library. No state management library.</p><p>These are demos, not finished components. The point is to show the pattern clearly so you can adapt it to what the project actually needs.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','68586402-30c1-44af-a7d1-606c81e8f4e6'),(2282,2282,1,NULL,'__temp_smioappptayceknmwyajesgotnfvyuynwqsc',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','54790aec-90b1-4f3f-a414-c7aa0e38f9e4'),(2283,2283,1,NULL,'__temp_rfpzhuavpwnodthqdldvgcwrjjverleqvhiv',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Live search\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:723@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Instant filtering, server side</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','23d8ca21-5bcb-4a81-b203-e02b82cb41ee'),(2284,2284,1,NULL,'__temp_gqijinpoaxfblxwszfodbcbygfkheupzzmiu',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Blog listing\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>paginated, filtered, reactive</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','f004fdd4-c04a-4a8e-8f91-f81f723dc2cc'),(2285,2285,1,NULL,'__temp_exakmyjhftiekvarjwtneocfrkitaunruopc',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Todo list\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Todos\", \"value\": \"https://craft-kit.dev/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Full CRUD, no JS framework</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','50c118f3-bfcd-4341-bdcb-8f4821e7db8c'),(2286,2286,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','1c03f093-de66-4d39-8ed2-f71bbf208e9a'),(2287,2287,1,NULL,'__temp_kxwhfgistwnjjblgiuvkzaeavgpetxpswgzl',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>LLM-ready out of the box</h2><p>Craft Kit includes the LLM Ready Plugin. Append .md to any entry URL and the page renders as clean Markdown — structured, readable, and machine-consumable without additional templates or configuration.</p><p>AI crawlers index it cleanly. LLMs can summarize it accurately. And it costs nothing at runtime.</p><h2>AI-assisted development setup</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with a complete Claude Code configuration so AI-assisted development works on day one:</p><p>CLAUDE.md gives Claude the full project context — stack, architecture, conventions, folder structure. .claudeignore keeps it focused on relevant files. .mcp.json connects Claude Code to the Craft MCP Plugin for direct access to the running Craft installation. A Datastar skill set — attribute reference, SSE patterns, and philosophy docs — is included as a Claude skill folder.</p><p>A developer unfamiliar with Craft or Datastar can be productive from the first session.</p><h2>Who this is for</h2><p>Craft Kit is for agencies and freelancers who want to deliver fast, accessible, maintainable sites without managing a distributed frontend infrastructure. It is for CTOs who are tired of explaining why a brochure site needs three separate deployment pipelines. And it is for developers who would rather write templates than configure build systems.</p><p>It is not a theme, a page builder, or a finished product. It is a starting point with the hard decisions already made — so the first week of a project is spent building, not configuring.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','a0188f26-46ec-4d02-ae03-565aaa072368'),(2288,2288,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:20:32','2026-04-24 09:20:32','f6cf6592-c426-4680-bddb-463d134f7b88'),(2292,2292,1,'LLM Ready',NULL,NULL,'{\"e30c17b9-ffa5-4343-99ee-0f780e5e0ed0\": \"LLMs love it. AI crawlers index it. Zero extra configuration.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:21:51','2026-04-24 10:02:29','4a3d2a05-c953-4037-adaa-157338d79b3f'),(2299,2299,1,NULL,'__temp_mcqntodppnalncdqjrkpjoazvzfioslijscq',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [2292]}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 10:16:50','95446ead-8bf6-4990-8252-d9ff4dc0bdba'),(2300,2300,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','81c61fdb-f0ca-4a79-8478-0b939417f721'),(2301,2301,1,NULL,'__temp_fmvvromaplrawkitxcmsakwluxoxwurrixal',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>AI-assisted development setup</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with a complete Claude Code configuration so AI-assisted development works on day one.</p><p> CLAUDE.md gives Claude the full project context — stack, architecture, conventions, folder structure. .claudeignore keeps it focused on relevant files. .mcp.json connects Claude Code to the Craft MCP Plugin for direct access to the running Craft installation. A Datastar skill set — attribute reference, SSE patterns, and philosophy docs — is included as a Claude skill folder.</p><blockquote><p>A developer unfamiliar with Craft or Datastar can be productive from the first session.<br />The setup does the explaining.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 10:16:50','c4153b42-df4b-44ec-9dc2-070a2a0c7eba'),(2302,2302,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','1fd2797d-e83b-4571-b7db-9ff9d0272df0'),(2303,2303,1,NULL,'__temp_vfxmybeygkhtkxuwzrcpcxjpmzuvcfsiufat',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Make it your own</h2><p>Clone the repository, follow the setup in the README and explore the templates alongside the demos. Keep the patterns that help and remove what your project does not need.</p><p>The example design and content are a starting point, not a requirement. Bring your own content model, styling and project-specific features.</p><p><a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">View the project on GitHub</a></p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-11-13 13:39:29','35621541-d5e4-4968-87a4-0f87ffd6cba3'),(2304,2304,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','97b9dba7-15fe-4495-8f42-7cd5d4752c38'),(2305,2305,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">No headless. No JavaScript framework. Just a clean, fast, production-ready foundation.</p>\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','eca1d4b5-9019-4e2b-b850-44331ce314f5'),(2306,2306,1,NULL,'__temp_kxwhfgistwnjjblgiuvkzaeavgpetxpswgzl',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>LLM-ready out of the box</h2><p>Craft Kit includes the LLM Ready Plugin. Append .md to any entry URL and the page renders as clean Markdown — structured, readable, and machine-consumable without additional templates or configuration.</p><p>AI crawlers index it cleanly. LLMs can summarize it accurately. And it costs nothing at runtime.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','d10ac36a-7bba-41ac-811f-7d821713abde'),(2307,2307,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','8ed71755-7626-4d11-8e93-76083577cf13'),(2308,2308,1,NULL,'__temp_mcqntodppnalncdqjrkpjoazvzfioslijscq',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": false, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [2292]}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','8a5ea008-7220-450c-84c3-ec8506234780'),(2309,2309,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','77f8eae6-fe08-4585-ae41-eaa1d3da9d88'),(2310,2310,1,NULL,'__temp_fmvvromaplrawkitxcmsakwluxoxwurrixal',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>AI-assisted development setup</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with a complete Claude Code configuration so AI-assisted development works on day one:</p><p>CLAUDE.md gives Claude the full project context — stack, architecture, conventions, folder structure. .claudeignore keeps it focused on relevant files. .mcp.json connects Claude Code to the Craft MCP Plugin for direct access to the running Craft installation. A Datastar skill set — attribute reference, SSE patterns, and philosophy docs — is included as a Claude skill folder.</p><p>A developer unfamiliar with Craft or Datastar can be productive from the first session.</p><h2>Who this is for</h2><p>Craft Kit is for agencies and freelancers who want to deliver fast, accessible, maintainable sites without managing a distributed frontend infrastructure. It is for CTOs who are tired of explaining why a brochure site needs three separate deployment pipelines. And it is for developers who would rather write templates than configure build systems.</p><p>It is not a theme, a page builder, or a finished product. It is a starting point with the hard decisions already made — so the first week of a project is spent building, not configuring.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','e46135be-1127-4d24-b69f-32a302dfaea4'),(2311,2311,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','ca023bca-bf9a-41ed-b7cc-8c020c5d6ec7'),(2312,2312,1,NULL,'__temp_vfxmybeygkhtkxuwzrcpcxjpmzuvcfsiufat',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>Craft Kit is available on <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">github</a>. If you are evaluating it for an agency project or want to talk through whether this architecture fits your stack, <a href=\\\"https://webworker.me/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">get in touch</a>.</p><p>Questions about the Hypermedia approach, Datastar integration, or how to migrate an existing Craft project — happy to discuss any of it.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','eb4c7273-a7ce-45f2-bfea-d50167385683'),(2313,2313,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:26:15','2026-04-24 09:26:15','d6b71fd5-f726-4ecd-ba4b-78cdd34922c5'),(2314,2314,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">No headless. No JavaScript framework. Just a clean, fast, production-ready foundation.</p>\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:26:31','2026-04-24 09:26:31','63afca0e-3015-47c7-875f-b79c186ac216'),(2315,2315,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">No headless. No JavaScript framework. Just a clean, fast, production-ready foundation.</p>\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:28:37','2026-04-24 09:28:37','8a5389c3-e23d-46ec-9155-3f1b54634843'),(2320,2320,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:38:06','2026-04-24 09:38:06','8fcda36b-8cee-441f-83f5-10afe67f69a5'),(2321,2321,1,NULL,'__temp_gyydugypgvjiequfbxcuomsbyqstomnyqdeo',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">WordPress is a plugin problem. TYPO3 is a configuration problem. Headless is a complexity problem. They\'re different symptoms of the same mistake: the wrong tool for the job.</p><p>Every agency has the same story. Too many moving parts, too much time configuring, too little time building. The stack is different. The problem is the same.</p><p>Craft CMS is the answer most agencies haven\'t tried yet.</p><blockquote><p>Craft Kit is a scaffold, not a theme. It gives you a structured starting point with established patterns and sane defaults — then gets out of the way. Every part of it is meant to be adapted, extended, or replaced to fit the project at hand.</p></blockquote><h2>Who this is for</h2><p>Craft Kit is for agencies and freelancers who want to deliver fast, accessible, maintainable sites without managing a distributed frontend infrastructure. It is for CTOs who are tired of explaining why a brochure site needs three separate deployment pipelines. And it is for developers who would rather write templates than configure build systems.</p><p>It is not a theme, a page builder, or a finished product. It is a starting point with the hard decisions already made — so the first week of a project is spent building, not configuring.</p><h2>Why Craft CMS?</h2><p>Craft is one of the few CMS platforms that gets content modeling right. Fields, sections, entry types, Matrix blocks — the authoring experience is flexible enough for complex projects and simple enough that clients actually use it without training. It doesn\'t force a data structure on you. You build exactly what the project needs.</p><p>And the platform is moving in the right direction. Craft 6, due in late 2026, is being built as a Laravel package — meaning it can be dropped into any existing Laravel application and treated as a first-class dependency. The full Laravel ecosystem becomes available: packages, middleware, tooling, and a talent pool that\'s orders of magnitude larger than any niche PHP framework. For agencies evaluating long-term platform risk, that matters.</p><p>Craft 5 is now an LTS release, with five years of support guaranteed after Craft 6 ships. There is no pressure to migrate before you\'re ready.</p><h2>Why not headless?</h2><p>Headless architecture makes sense for a specific set of problems: native mobile apps consuming the same API, highly distributed content teams, microsecond performance SLAs at massive scale. For most agency projects, it introduces complexity without solving anything the client actually asked for.</p><p>The Hypermedia approach — server-rendered HTML, enriched where needed with lightweight interactivity — delivers the same results with a fraction of the moving parts. Craft CMS handles content modeling and rendering. Twig handles templating. Datastar handles the reactive bits. That\'s the whole stack.</p><blockquote><p>Same UX. Faster development. Fewer dependencies. Easier onboarding for the next developer on the project.</p></blockquote><h2><strong>100 across the board</strong></h2><p>The demo site runs 100 across the board — not as a benchmark exercise, but as a direct consequence of the architecture. Server-rendered HTML is fast. Semantic markup is accessible. Clean output is indexable.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:38:06','2026-04-24 09:38:06','a6c65a21-f2eb-481c-9cd8-71c3b90c7720'),(2322,2322,1,NULL,'__temp_fmvvromaplrawkitxcmsakwluxoxwurrixal',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>AI-assisted development setup</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with a complete Claude Code configuration so AI-assisted development works on day one:</p><p>CLAUDE.md gives Claude the full project context — stack, architecture, conventions, folder structure. .claudeignore keeps it focused on relevant files. .mcp.json connects Claude Code to the Craft MCP Plugin for direct access to the running Craft installation. A Datastar skill set — attribute reference, SSE patterns, and philosophy docs — is included as a Claude skill folder.</p><p>A developer unfamiliar with Craft or Datastar can be productive from the first session.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:38:06','2026-04-24 09:38:06','8979e5ea-879c-4ead-91c5-67b2ff975346'),(2323,2323,1,NULL,'__temp_vfxmybeygkhtkxuwzrcpcxjpmzuvcfsiufat',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<hr /><p>Craft Kit is available on <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">github</a>. If you are evaluating it for an agency project or want to talk through whether this architecture fits your stack, <a href=\\\"https://webworker.me/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">get in touch</a>.</p><p>Questions about the Hypermedia approach, Datastar integration, or how to migrate an existing Craft project — happy to discuss any of it.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:38:06','2026-04-24 09:38:06','273118cc-beda-4ae7-96c0-b6b81f061474'),(2339,2339,1,NULL,'__temp_tywyazieygvtllwbymokluxxbsgguvtbfvol',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A starting point for Craft CMS, not a finished website.</p><p>Craft Kit is a starter kit you can download from GitHub and adapt to your own projects. It combines a configured development environment with working examples of content blocks and Datastar interactions.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-11-13 13:39:29','2db7c577-4c1f-467e-90de-79e3cb181d58'),(2340,2340,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','9dd79aa3-d238-4e47-865a-8063b2c5e54e'),(2341,2341,1,NULL,'__temp_ljsfgmcbtabnrdytpaurjxjojzdppgjbsjzd',NULL,'{\"d04bc466-1b82-4e88-ba5a-d772666f5e29\": \"Less stack. More product.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','410e264d-4572-45e6-a6ff-909a91d42312'),(2342,2342,1,NULL,'__temp_qpmjvvmaqtrewwofnxzrlzpiwgrwnystgpgt',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"👥\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Smaller teams, same output\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"One developer can own the full stack. No separate frontend and backend specialists required.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','d67e6808-fab8-4b02-b8dc-9fcffe836230'),(2343,2343,1,NULL,'__temp_isdbfyfehxyknnlmbgifkesqxvgfxslfmqvo',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🚀\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"No DevOps overhead\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"One stack, one deployment. No pipeline between your CMS, your API, and your frontend.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','3d9e1789-10a1-4416-a021-204a9bf9e6fd'),(2344,2344,1,NULL,'__temp_uyaubxedqbwkzynnyccygcthkbdlxlprckdw',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"⚡\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Faster onboarding\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"New developers are productive from day one. Twig is readable. The structure is obvious. No framework to learn first.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','0b8a9658-011c-4aa9-bfe0-fcb365676078'),(2345,2345,1,NULL,'__temp_ywzunbwknwgwtnspsbfjsprndzucdpuxnwgt',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🔧\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Lower maintenance cost\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Fewer moving parts means fewer things to break, fewer dependencies to update, and fewer midnight alerts.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','34a5854e-c124-4e2a-a5d9-30ab5bdf963b'),(2346,2346,1,NULL,'__temp_xcorpmrrkzdbmjxejadaqrloumfxfbxsdnoa',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🤝\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"One team, one codebase\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"No frontend/backend split. No handoff friction. The whole project lives in one place, owned by one team.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','7a8356fe-b4c2-4f2e-b5a1-a7d476ec9f62'),(2347,2347,1,NULL,'__temp_lhnsndxhgzvscmicwaaqisxaawcxvaeccfez',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🛡️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"A platform with a roadmap\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Craft 5 is LTS — five years of support after Craft 6 ships. Craft 6 brings Laravel under the hood. The platform is going somewhere.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','003417f2-4472-45a5-b4fb-788e2cecbb6f'),(2348,2348,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','334cfcda-f5df-4464-a22e-cf21b76f8bb3'),(2349,2349,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','8d4b4826-a0e4-4a2f-a32c-65ca87c1d9bf'),(2350,2350,1,NULL,'__temp_tywyazieygvtllwbymokluxxbsgguvtbfvol',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">WordPress is a plugin problem. TYPO3 is a configuration problem. Headless is a complexity problem. They\'re different symptoms of the same mistake: the wrong tool for the job.</p><p>Every agency has the same story. Too many moving parts, too much time configuring, too little time building. The stack is different. The problem is the same.</p><p><strong>Craft CMS is the answer most agencies haven\'t tried yet.</strong></p><blockquote><p>Craft Kit is a scaffold, not a theme. It gives you a structured starting point with established patterns and sane defaults — then gets out of the way. Every part of it is meant to be adapted, extended, or replaced to fit the project at hand.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','6777735b-d4b9-45b9-b1ba-32bf9a2e91ac'),(2351,2351,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','136be735-84a7-49b8-9b26-8f14b29331e2'),(2352,2352,1,NULL,'__temp_ljsfgmcbtabnrdytpaurjxjojzdppgjbsjzd',NULL,'{\"d04bc466-1b82-4e88-ba5a-d772666f5e29\": \"Less stack. More product.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','b558d86c-7df3-4ccd-9a15-092dae62127c'),(2353,2353,1,NULL,'__temp_qpmjvvmaqtrewwofnxzrlzpiwgrwnystgpgt',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"👥\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Smaller teams, same output\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"One developer can own the full stack. No separate frontend and backend specialists required.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','3a90799b-c443-4de8-80c4-fe1c8377cdef'),(2354,2354,1,NULL,'__temp_isdbfyfehxyknnlmbgifkesqxvgfxslfmqvo',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🚀\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"No DevOps overhead\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"One stack, one deployment. No pipeline between your CMS, your API, and your frontend.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','f369ba72-67f1-418e-a819-dfd8c14951fa'),(2355,2355,1,NULL,'__temp_uyaubxedqbwkzynnyccygcthkbdlxlprckdw',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"⚡\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Faster onboarding\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"New developers are productive from day one. Twig is readable. The structure is obvious. No framework to learn first.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','a4c3f6ab-8142-4c17-b7a5-2b8c065c9a18'),(2356,2356,1,NULL,'__temp_ywzunbwknwgwtnspsbfjsprndzucdpuxnwgt',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🔧\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Lower maintenance cost\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Fewer moving parts means fewer things to break, fewer dependencies to update, and fewer midnight alerts.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','66e4a6b8-90a9-447a-b3de-931368573b60'),(2357,2357,1,NULL,'__temp_xcorpmrrkzdbmjxejadaqrloumfxfbxsdnoa',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🤝\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"One team, one codebase\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"No frontend/backend split. No handoff friction. The whole project lives in one place, owned by one team.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','66e0b5a1-cf39-4b73-aba8-d37d1d2cf4f2'),(2358,2358,1,NULL,'__temp_lhnsndxhgzvscmicwaaqisxaawcxvaeccfez',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🛡️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"A platform with a roadmap\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Craft 5 is LTS — five years of support after Craft 6 ships. Craft 6 brings Laravel under the hood. The platform is going somewhere.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','02180017-cd08-4ff8-9453-24463536f035'),(2359,2359,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','2055eb1b-378e-4444-9c9f-42248aa9aec2'),(2360,2360,1,NULL,'__temp_gyydugypgvjiequfbxcuomsbyqstomnyqdeo',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Who this is for</h2><p>Craft Kit is for agencies and freelancers who want to deliver fast, accessible, maintainable sites without managing a distributed frontend infrastructure. It is for CTOs who are tired of explaining why a brochure site needs three separate deployment pipelines. And it is for developers who would rather write templates than configure build systems.</p><p>It is not a theme, a page builder, or a finished product. It is a starting point with the hard decisions already made — so the first week of a project is spent building, not configuring.</p><h2>Why Craft CMS?</h2><p>Craft is one of the few CMS platforms that gets content modeling right. Fields, sections, entry types, Matrix blocks — the authoring experience is flexible enough for complex projects and simple enough that clients actually use it without training. It doesn\'t force a data structure on you. You build exactly what the project needs.</p><p>And the platform is moving in the right direction. Craft 6, due in late 2026, is being built as a Laravel package — meaning it can be dropped into any existing Laravel application and treated as a first-class dependency. The full Laravel ecosystem becomes available: packages, middleware, tooling, and a talent pool that\'s orders of magnitude larger than any niche PHP framework. For agencies evaluating long-term platform risk, that matters.</p><p>Craft 5 is now an LTS release, with five years of support guaranteed after Craft 6 ships. There is no pressure to migrate before you\'re ready.</p><h2>Why not headless?</h2><p>Headless architecture makes sense for a specific set of problems: native mobile apps consuming the same API, highly distributed content teams, microsecond performance SLAs at massive scale. For most agency projects, it introduces complexity without solving anything the client actually asked for.</p><p>The Hypermedia approach — server-rendered HTML, enriched where needed with lightweight interactivity — delivers the same results with a fraction of the moving parts. Craft CMS handles content modeling and rendering. Twig handles templating. Datastar handles the reactive bits. That\'s the whole stack.</p><blockquote><p>Same UX. Faster development. Fewer dependencies. Easier onboarding for the next developer on the project.</p></blockquote><h2><strong>100 across the board</strong></h2><p>The demo site runs 100 across the board — not as a benchmark exercise, but as a direct consequence of the architecture. Server-rendered HTML is fast. Semantic markup is accessible. Clean output is indexable.</p><p>These scores hold without any special optimization pass. They are the baseline, not the goal.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','6d729c0b-bccc-4487-b88e-0df834a91e90'),(2361,2361,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','ca3ef8a8-22ca-4c62-874e-b2cd0628eaba'),(2362,2362,1,NULL,'__temp_qyczkdevkhsquglcuaumrjenkyenhcmoklto',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>The stack</h2><p><strong>Craft CMS 5, Twig, Datastar, Vite, Tailwind CSS, DDEV, SEOMate</strong><br /><strong>— and nothing else.</strong></p><p>Every tool has a reason to be here. DDEV ensures every developer on the team gets the same local environment on day one. Vite handles asset bundling with instant HMR. SEOMate covers Open Graph, meta, and sitemaps without configuration overhead. Datastar replaces the need for a JavaScript framework wherever reactivity is required.</p><p>What is not in the stack is just as deliberate: no React, no Vue, no Next.js, no GraphQL, no separate API layer.</p><h2>Datastar demos — real-world patterns</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with working examples of the most common reactive UI patterns, built with Datastar and server-rendered Twig. No JavaScript build step. No component library. No state management library.</p><p>These are demos, not finished components. The point is to show the pattern clearly so you can adapt it to what the project actually needs.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','bb8d25d6-73e4-4cab-a06f-a4e256cf9d11'),(2363,2363,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 09:49:37','2026-04-24 09:49:37','7dfb9ec0-aa99-4610-a858-c857f07a6452'),(2364,2364,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:49:42','2026-04-24 09:49:42','a53f94b4-7332-43fc-a513-5a5f737ec504'),(2365,2365,1,'Why Craft Kit','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','the-craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies-actually-need','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\"}',1,'2026-04-24 09:53:19','2026-04-24 09:53:19','175c4281-a671-4555-a273-e3f84d33ac01'),(2370,2370,1,'Why Craft Kit','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit for Agencies — Ship Faster, Maintain Less — Tired of WordPress plugins, TYPO3 complexity, or headless overhead? This production-ready Craft CMS scaffold helps agencies ship faster with less stack drama.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:00:15','2026-04-24 10:00:15','8965721d-f02f-4be1-86f7-94758ee1a73d'),(2371,2371,1,NULL,'__temp_vfxmybeygkhtkxuwzrcpcxjpmzuvcfsiufat',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Ship on time</h2><p>Your next project starts in a few weeks. How many developers does it need? How long until the first deployment? If the answer is uncomfortable — it\'s time to look at the stack.</p><p>Craft CMS doesn\'t just simplify the architecture. It puts deadlines back in reach and keeps maintenance predictable. Smaller teams, faster builds, less time firefighting. Ship on time. Stay on top of it.</p><hr /><p>Craft Kit is available on <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">github</a>. If you are evaluating it for an agency project or want to talk through whether this architecture fits your stack, <a href=\\\"https://webworker.me/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">get in touch</a>.</p><p>Questions about the Hypermedia approach, Datastar integration, or how to migrate an existing Craft project — happy to discuss any of it.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:00:15','2026-04-24 10:00:15','26633ce5-8a03-40ce-910e-8f7ebc6ff6ef'),(2372,2372,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-24 10:00:15','2026-04-24 10:00:15','b0da4ad7-43b9-4cca-92e8-e7af575e5ddd'),(2373,2373,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit for Agencies — Ship Faster, Maintain Less\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Tired of WordPress plugins, TYPO3 complexity, or headless overhead? This production-ready Craft CMS scaffold helps agencies ship faster with less stack drama.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:00:15','2026-04-24 10:00:15','08912460-dd9a-4da5-9378-40c15a4cadf9'),(2387,2387,1,'Why Craft Kit','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit for Agencies — Ship Faster, Maintain Less — Tired of WordPress plugins, TYPO3 complexity, or headless overhead? This production-ready Craft CMS scaffold helps agencies ship faster with less stack drama.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','ee6e0162-dbec-418d-aaab-3f76d5063815'),(2388,2388,1,NULL,'__temp_tywyazieygvtllwbymokluxxbsgguvtbfvol',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">WordPress is a plugin problem. TYPO3 is a configuration problem. Headless is a complexity problem. They\'re different symptoms of the same mistake: the wrong tool for the job.</p><p>Every agency has the same story. Too many moving parts, too much time configuring, too little time building. The stack is different. The problem is the same.</p><p><strong>Craft CMS is the answer most agencies haven\'t tried yet. Craft Kit is a production-ready Craft CMS starter kit that gives your team a clean foundation — without the overhead of a headless setup, a JavaScript framework, or a plugin ecosystem held together with hope.</strong></p><blockquote><p>Craft Kit is a scaffold, not a theme. It gives you a structured starting point with established patterns and sane defaults — then gets out of the way. Every part of it is meant to be adapted, extended, or replaced to fit the project at hand.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','0ecc1211-53ae-4cf3-8d58-f5a790405ef7'),(2389,2389,1,NULL,'__temp_gyydugypgvjiequfbxcuomsbyqstomnyqdeo',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Who this is for</h2><p>Craft Kit is for agencies and freelancers who want to deliver fast, accessible, maintainable sites without managing a distributed frontend infrastructure. It is for CTOs who are tired of explaining why a brochure site needs three separate deployment pipelines. And it is for developers who would rather write templates than configure build systems.</p><p>It is not a theme, a page builder, or a finished product. It is a starting point with the hard decisions already made — so the first week of a project is spent building, not configuring.</p><h2>Why Craft CMS?</h2><p>Craft is one of the few CMS platforms that gets content modeling right. Fields, sections, entry types, Matrix blocks — the authoring experience is flexible enough for complex projects and simple enough that clients actually use it without training. It doesn\'t force a data structure on you. You build exactly what the project needs.</p><p>For agencies coming from WordPress or TYPO3, Craft is the upgrade that doesn\'t feel like a compromise — cleaner content modeling, no plugin bloat, and a codebase you can actually own.</p><p>And the platform is moving in the right direction. Craft 6, due in late 2026, is being built as a Laravel package — meaning it can be dropped into any existing Laravel application and treated as a first-class dependency. The full Laravel ecosystem becomes available: packages, middleware, tooling, and a talent pool that\'s orders of magnitude larger than any niche PHP framework. For agencies evaluating long-term platform risk, that matters.</p><p>Craft 5 is now an LTS release, with five years of support guaranteed after Craft 6 ships. There is no pressure to migrate before you\'re ready.</p><blockquote><p>The CMS your editors will actually use.<br />The platform your developers won\'t want to leave.</p></blockquote><h2>Why not headless?</h2><p>Headless architecture makes sense for a specific set of problems: native mobile apps consuming the same API, highly distributed content teams, microsecond performance SLAs at massive scale. For most agency projects, it introduces complexity without solving anything the client actually asked for.</p><p>The Hypermedia approach — server-rendered HTML, enriched where needed with lightweight interactivity — delivers the same results with a fraction of the moving parts. Craft CMS handles content modeling and rendering. Twig handles templating. Datastar handles the reactive bits. That\'s the whole stack.</p><blockquote><p>Same UX. Faster development. Fewer dependencies.<br />Easier onboarding for the next developer on the project.</p></blockquote><h2><strong>100 across the board</strong></h2><p>The demo site runs 100 across the board — not as a benchmark exercise, but as a direct consequence of the architecture. Server-rendered HTML is fast. Semantic markup is accessible. Clean output is indexable.</p><blockquote><p>These scores hold without any special optimization pass.<br />They are the baseline, not the goal.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','78368da8-4515-4433-9e1d-f11928f56c91'),(2390,2390,1,NULL,'__temp_tjghqsvjgikvfdrdidfeseyugvzrcuhuvdbq',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [2267]}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','4eecca3c-4789-4324-baa0-0b7f16d05845'),(2391,2391,1,NULL,'__temp_qyczkdevkhsquglcuaumrjenkyenhcmoklto',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>The stack</h2><p><strong>Craft CMS 5, Twig, Datastar, Vite, Tailwind CSS, DDEV, SEOMate</strong><br /><strong>— and nothing else.</strong></p><p>Every tool has a reason to be here. DDEV ensures every developer on the team gets the same local environment on day one. Vite handles asset bundling with instant HMR. SEOMate covers Open Graph, meta, and sitemaps without configuration overhead. Datastar replaces the need for a JavaScript framework wherever reactivity is required.</p><p>What is not in the stack is just as deliberate: no React, no Vue, no Next.js, no GraphQL, no separate API layer.</p><blockquote><p>Every tool chosen on merit. Every tool you can replace.<br />Nothing you can\'t explain to a client.</p></blockquote><h2>Datastar demos — real-world patterns</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with working examples of the most common reactive UI patterns, built with Datastar and server-rendered Twig. No JavaScript build step. No component library. No state management library.</p><p>These are demos, not finished components. The point is to show the pattern clearly so you can adapt it to what the project actually needs.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','1bfbda1c-d9ae-4e57-a152-02c2fa9d5585'),(2392,2392,1,NULL,'__temp_smioappptayceknmwyajesgotnfvyuynwqsc',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','7fe891dc-37f9-466b-bfd8-4388eca47d62'),(2393,2393,1,NULL,'__temp_rfpzhuavpwnodthqdldvgcwrjjverleqvhiv',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Craft CMS live search with Datastar\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:723@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Instant filtering, server side</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','67cd47b3-058b-4912-b839-e3e17af4f580'),(2394,2394,1,NULL,'__temp_gqijinpoaxfblxwszfodbcbygfkheupzzmiu',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Craft CMS blog listing with Datastar\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>paginated, filtered, reactive</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','771e2812-18e7-45b2-a199-e95bd508a721'),(2395,2395,1,NULL,'__temp_exakmyjhftiekvarjwtneocfrkitaunruopc',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Craft CMS. todo list with Datastar\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Todos\", \"value\": \"https://craft-kit.dev/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Full CRUD, no JS framework</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','35ac88c7-e02c-4653-8ce0-c4eac488b63b'),(2396,2396,1,NULL,'__temp_kxwhfgistwnjjblgiuvkzaeavgpetxpswgzl',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>LLM-ready out of the box</h2><p>Craft Kit includes the LLM Ready Plugin. Append .md to any entry URL and the page renders as clean Markdown — structured, readable, and machine-consumable without additional templates or configuration.</p><blockquote><p>AI crawlers index it cleanly. LLMs summarize it accurately. Your content is machine-readable by default — no extra tooling, no extra cost.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','bae5f6a3-5d16-47d9-8396-2a2e20792ebb'),(2397,2397,1,NULL,'__temp_mcqntodppnalncdqjrkpjoazvzfioslijscq',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [2292]}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','d5e6ee06-2902-418a-886c-e2acb54c1a0f'),(2398,2398,1,NULL,'__temp_fmvvromaplrawkitxcmsakwluxoxwurrixal',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>AI-assisted development setup</h2><p>Craft Kit ships with a complete Claude Code configuration so AI-assisted development works on day one.</p><p> CLAUDE.md gives Claude the full project context — stack, architecture, conventions, folder structure. .claudeignore keeps it focused on relevant files. .mcp.json connects Claude Code to the Craft MCP Plugin for direct access to the running Craft installation. A Datastar skill set — attribute reference, SSE patterns, and philosophy docs — is included as a Claude skill folder.</p><blockquote><p>A developer unfamiliar with Craft or Datastar can be productive from the first session.<br />The setup does the explaining.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','6db01772-3b32-489e-8cc4-606c644e7c89'),(2399,2399,1,NULL,'__temp_vfxmybeygkhtkxuwzrcpcxjpmzuvcfsiufat',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Ship on time</h2><p>Your next project starts in a few weeks. How many developers does it need? How long until the first deployment? If the answer is uncomfortable — it\'s time to look at the stack.</p><p>Craft CMS doesn\'t just simplify the architecture. It puts deadlines back in reach and keeps maintenance predictable. Smaller teams, faster builds, less time firefighting. Ship on time. Stay on top of it.</p><p>The web was Hypermedia before we called it that. A URL returns HTML. The browser renders it. That\'s still the fastest, most accessible, most maintainable architecture there is. We just forgot.</p><blockquote><p>Every JavaScript framework was built to solve a problem that server-rendered HTML doesn\'t have.</p></blockquote><hr /><p>Craft Kit is available on <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">github</a>. If you are evaluating it for an agency project or want to talk through whether this architecture fits your stack, <a href=\\\"https://webworker.me/\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\">get in touch</a>.</p><p>Questions about the Hypermedia approach, Datastar integration, or how to migrate an existing Craft project — happy to discuss any of it.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:50','2026-04-24 10:16:50','f922b909-aeea-450c-bc53-c8ca92ceac4d'),(2400,2400,1,'Why Craft Kit','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit for Agencies — Ship Faster, Maintain Less — Tired of WordPress plugins, TYPO3 complexity, or headless overhead? This production-ready Craft CMS scaffold helps agencies ship faster with less stack drama.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:16:54','2026-04-24 10:16:54','5a63beb7-9381-4253-9a74-3d6d5e19f5db'),(2403,2403,1,'Why Craft Kit','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit for Agencies — Ship Faster, Maintain Less — Tired of WordPress plugins, TYPO3 complexity, or headless overhead? This production-ready Craft CMS scaffold helps agencies ship faster with less stack drama.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:20:06','2026-04-24 10:20:06','209a3acf-8827-4c30-9285-89986fec80ad'),(2404,2404,1,NULL,'__temp_gyydugypgvjiequfbxcuomsbyqstomnyqdeo',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Why Craft CMS?</h2><p>Craft is one of the few CMS platforms that gets content modeling right. Fields, sections, entry types, Matrix blocks — the authoring experience is flexible enough for complex projects and simple enough that clients actually use it without training. It doesn\'t force a data structure on you. You build exactly what the project needs.</p><p>For agencies coming from WordPress or TYPO3, Craft is the upgrade that doesn\'t feel like a compromise — cleaner content modeling, no plugin bloat, and a codebase you can actually own.</p><p>And the platform is moving in the right direction. Craft 6, due in late 2026, is being built as a Laravel package — meaning it can be dropped into any existing Laravel application and treated as a first-class dependency. The full Laravel ecosystem becomes available: packages, middleware, tooling, and a talent pool that\'s orders of magnitude larger than any niche PHP framework. For agencies evaluating long-term platform risk, that matters.</p><p>Craft 5 is now an LTS release, with five years of support guaranteed after Craft 6 ships. There is no pressure to migrate before you\'re ready.</p><blockquote><p>The CMS your editors will actually use.<br />The platform your developers won\'t want to leave.</p></blockquote><h2>Why not headless?</h2><p>Headless architecture makes sense for a specific set of problems: native mobile apps consuming the same API, highly distributed content teams, microsecond performance SLAs at massive scale. For most agency projects, it introduces complexity without solving anything the client actually asked for.</p><p>The Hypermedia approach — server-rendered HTML, enriched where needed with lightweight interactivity — delivers the same results with a fraction of the moving parts. Craft CMS handles content modeling and rendering. Twig handles templating. Datastar handles the reactive bits. That\'s the whole stack.</p><blockquote><p>Same UX. Faster development. Fewer dependencies.<br />Easier onboarding for the next developer on the project.</p></blockquote><h2><strong>100 across the board</strong></h2><p>The demo site runs 100 across the board — not as a benchmark exercise, but as a direct consequence of the architecture. Server-rendered HTML is fast. Semantic markup is accessible. Clean output is indexable.</p><blockquote><p>These scores hold without any special optimization pass.<br />They are the baseline, not the goal.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:20:06','2026-04-24 10:20:06','748f05cd-aca3-45b3-8c28-fe29cde35a7a'),(2406,2406,1,'Why Craft Kit','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','craft-cms-starter-kit-agencies','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"The Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Actually Need\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit for Agencies — Ship Faster, Maintain Less — Tired of WordPress plugins, TYPO3 complexity, or headless overhead? This production-ready Craft CMS scaffold helps agencies ship faster with less stack drama.\"}',1,'2026-04-24 10:26:30','2026-04-24 10:26:30','ada743fc-64f3-4625-a14b-7bb02d9d67bf'),(2408,2408,1,'Todo List','todolist',NULL,'{\"5e2baca9-5c68-4147-b9e7-0df1a3d033d9\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Todo List\", \"value\": \"/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\"}}',1,'2026-04-24 10:27:52','2026-04-24 10:27:52','9bb3aa66-0ca0-4dfe-802d-25b52cf1a2be'),(2409,2409,1,'Why Craft Kit','why-craft-kit',NULL,'{\"5e2baca9-5c68-4147-b9e7-0df1a3d033d9\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:2221@1:url}\"}}',1,'2026-04-24 10:28:17','2026-04-24 10:28:33','cd9c32c0-acf5-4636-888f-ba5352c7ac2e'),(2410,2410,1,'Why Craft Kit','why-craft-kit',NULL,'{\"5e2baca9-5c68-4147-b9e7-0df1a3d033d9\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:2221@1:url}\"}}',1,'2026-04-24 10:28:30','2026-04-24 10:28:30','99d7ba76-fce4-42db-a60a-2723fe9f43a2'),(2411,2411,1,'Craft CMS is Becoming a Laravel Package','craft-cms-6-laravel','blog/craft-cms-6-laravel','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2026-04-27 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [268], \"7f45d57a-6089-4476-9875-732dfa47a1a0\": {\"id\": null, \"lat\": 52.5173885, \"lng\": 13.3951309, \"zoom\": 15, \"parts\": {\"arm\": \"Orion Arm\", \"city\": \"Berlin\", \"group\": \"the Local Group\", \"state\": \"\", \"county\": \"\", \"galaxy\": \"Milky Way\", \"number\": \"\", \"planet\": \"Earth\", \"system\": \"the Solar System\", \"address\": \"\", \"cluster\": \"Virgo Cluster\", \"country\": \"Germany\", \"postcode\": \"\", \"supercluster\": \"Laniakea Supercluster\"}, \"address\": \"Berlin, Germany\", \"fieldId\": 35, \"ownerId\": 2411, \"distance\": null, \"what3words\": null, \"ownerSiteId\": 1}, \"d74fbbee-f4c8-448b-b8fc-d5723a6d0f07\": 0, \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Craft CMS is Becoming a Laravel Package. Here is What That Means for You.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:03:38','2026-11-13 15:41:27','708bb858-aa30-41fc-b834-69540e765755'),(2412,2412,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"41d42c36-230e-4e28-96f8-8a4801e9694e\": \"<p>Craft CMS is moving towards Laravel. Learn what the announced direction means for your projects, which details need checking and why clean Twig still matters.</p>\", \"914ae46d-5dd7-4afd-b5a3-32fbed3aecae\": [2692]}',1,'2026-04-28 11:03:38','2026-11-13 15:45:53','c40181d2-d4d5-4b7f-a692-1826fb9f4fc6'),(2413,2413,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Craft CMS 6 and Laravel — What Craft Developers Need to Know\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Craft CMS is moving towards Laravel. Learn what the announced direction means for your projects, which details need checking and why clean Twig still matters.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": [2692]}',1,'2026-04-28 11:03:38','2026-11-13 15:53:19','e2845e06-7482-4f3c-a9e9-8427e0947532'),(2414,2414,1,NULL,'__temp_dyzuagdpzcywlcsglsgmpeqdpnpfrabvemcr',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Pixel &amp; Tonic announced that Craft CMS 6 will move from Yii 2 to Laravel. For Craft developers, the interesting question is what that foundation changes — and what should remain familiar.</p><p>This article summarizes the announced direction, not the current release status. Craft Kit currently runs on Craft CMS 5. Check the <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/blog/laravel\\\">official Laravel announcement</a> and <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/knowledge-base/supported-versions\\\">supported versions</a> before planning a production upgrade.</p><h2>Why the framework matters</h2><p>The underlying framework supplies infrastructure for requests, services, commands and integrations. Laravel has an established ecosystem that Craft can build on. That creates opportunities, but does not mean every Laravel package or hosting tool automatically works with every Craft project.</p><p>Pixel &amp; Tonic described the transition as mostly a port rather than a wholesale rewrite of Craft\'s architecture. The stated aim is to keep extending the CMS familiar while changing the foundation underneath it.</p><h2>What to evaluate</h2><p>The useful questions are concrete: how custom modules boot, which APIs change, which plugin versions support the release, and what the chosen hosting environment requires. Test those against your own project rather than treating a framework name as a migration plan.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:04:13','2026-11-13 15:52:10','446ca1bc-d520-440f-8ca3-3c1920e3adf0'),(2415,2415,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:04:13','2026-04-28 11:04:13','6ef8e415-65eb-4313-a00f-3f3a55970dd1'),(2416,2416,1,NULL,'__temp_sopumlbdlehymcbywkjddpeesvdxwbpmyyfk',NULL,'{\"d04bc466-1b82-4e88-ba5a-d772666f5e29\": \"What the framework change means\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:08:07','2026-11-13 15:52:11','0e0fe7d6-f2c6-43a5-b705-952a22e0a211'),(2417,2417,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:08:07','2026-04-28 11:08:07','3afe0137-65de-4d34-80bd-9a76d7a582ec'),(2418,2418,1,NULL,'__temp_xbvlvqleuhqvydemtghsrjrebykqhzaowjoi',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"⚙️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Framework foundation\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Laravel becomes the underlying framework in the announced Craft 6 direction. Evaluate framework-level changes against the actual release documentation.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:08:18','2026-11-13 15:52:11','42306636-a6d6-4f26-ab9c-cb22a990d7b4'),(2419,2419,1,NULL,'__temp_kaimyratqfzqrmtbxhxenksinmpblxjxuymk',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🗃️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Plugin compatibility\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"The announced Yii 2 adapter aims to reduce migration work. Plugin support and custom-module compatibility still need project-specific testing.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:08:33','2026-11-13 15:52:11','d01377a0-67f4-40fb-b7ed-64ed3ec1ab07'),(2420,2420,1,NULL,'__temp_bbkovqgbxkjoobgnlbxannpponulgjkudqod',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📦\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"A broader ecosystem\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Laravel offers a large package ecosystem. Choose integrations for a real requirement and verify compatibility rather than assuming every package is a drop-in.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:08:52','2026-11-13 15:52:11','8b45dbe6-a16c-4b1e-9ef0-a5329e45bda2'),(2421,2421,1,NULL,'__temp_zikohidxtyytfoxulbdnscurbazqhjrzmvau',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🚀\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Familiar content architecture\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"The announcement emphasizes a port of the existing architecture. Structured content and deliberate template boundaries remain useful investments.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:09:11','2026-11-13 15:52:11','962cccff-361d-4f3d-bde7-8693c245112c'),(2422,2422,1,NULL,'__temp_dvircpqzyvmogztggiuadssoggqpyqhvhwfg',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📊\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"A tested upgrade path\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Rehearse upgrades on a local copy, check Project Config and migrations, and verify queues, assets and custom code before touching production.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:09:34','2026-11-13 15:52:11','331b6fae-da9c-45c6-940c-05e96efdb06a'),(2423,2423,1,NULL,'__temp_vnivgvksezxshwprmuwpolueoshfceqnoopx',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🛠️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Current release guidance\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Use official release notes and support dates for planning. A roadmap describes an intention; it is not confirmation that a feature has shipped.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:09:52','2026-11-13 15:52:11','e45f736e-997b-439b-b83e-97516fedcbf2'),(2424,2424,1,NULL,'__temp_daocwrgiaptvxcfgnjafqyvxvvooqagobrms',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>What happens to existing projects</h2><p>The announcement includes a Yii 2 adapter intended to reduce compatibility work for Craft 5 plugins and modules. That is an aid to migration, not a guarantee that every custom integration will run unchanged. Check support from each plugin author and test the actual upgrade.</p><p>Craft 5 is an LTS release. Pixel &amp; Tonic announced support for five years after Craft 6\'s full release; use the <a href=\\\"https://craftcms.com/knowledge-base/supported-versions\\\">official support policy</a> for current dates rather than calculating them from an old roadmap.</p><h2>What editors can look forward to</h2><p>Pixel &amp; Tonic also announced editorial features for Craft 6. Treat the list below as announced plans; check the release notes for what is available in a particular version.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:11:02','2026-11-13 15:52:11','9e4a9b98-4039-4a6b-84c2-6c872d24c6a9'),(2425,2425,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:11:02','2026-04-28 11:11:02','e5e67dde-d40a-4cf6-9dad-2733f3fb2c7e'),(2426,2426,1,NULL,'__temp_lqwrfrtjyioxrehlxfhluumivnrvpkgqfrcw',NULL,'{\"d04bc466-1b82-4e88-ba5a-d772666f5e29\": \"Announced editorial features\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:13:35','2026-11-13 15:52:11','198b2f1f-7028-455e-aebb-6c2628e5e2e7'),(2427,2427,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:13:35','2026-04-28 11:13:35','b8438d0b-4e99-4d1e-ae52-31d16bfe23de'),(2428,2428,1,NULL,'__temp_yypbfzsagpbfklflctpkpchweyezdiuowapm',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"✅\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Approval workflows\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Announced governance features would let teams define how content moves through review and publication. Verify availability in the version you choose.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:13:39','2026-11-13 15:52:11','8edb9abd-aa54-4832-a5ed-d75508015d22'),(2429,2429,1,NULL,'__temp_fevpxsvfnavmrzqqfuklzbelfudcsxtmrqsx',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"💬\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Edit-page comments\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Feedback directly on an entry edit page is part of the announced editorial direction, keeping discussion close to the content it concerns.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:13:52','2026-11-13 15:52:11','8e00ae51-b4ee-47f4-8ae5-b94522d676f4'),(2430,2430,1,NULL,'__temp_biwjmbvbgpgialmddcccczhnqnjjmrediczs',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📋\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Element activity logs\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"The announced activity timeline is intended to make changes to an element easier to follow, including who changed what and when.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:14:08','2026-11-13 15:52:11','9e42c98d-1dc3-4c02-a8e6-b89a9399c26c'),(2431,2431,1,NULL,'__temp_ypuyxwhfugyjxcjizashheeojuvutjwnnfue',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📅\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Content releases\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Publishing related entries and drafts together, manually or on a schedule, is one of the announced improvements for coordinated launches.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:14:29','2026-11-13 15:52:11','3ba5ed5c-d547-4e1b-85c9-1ffa48609f51'),(2432,2432,1,NULL,'__temp_uflbgcwhxputwgsgexaegqeotkzofmghxvrb',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Roadmaps are not release guarantees</h2><p>The original announcement targeted a 2026 beta and full release. Schedules and implementation details can change. Confirm the current release, migration guidance and plugin compatibility directly with Craft before setting a client deadline.</p><h2>What this means for Craft Kit and Datastar</h2><p>The architectural reason for Datastar does not depend on Laravel: Craft renders HTML, and Datastar coordinates reactive browser state and server-driven updates. A backend framework change is not a reason to introduce a separate frontend application.</p><p>Craft Kit demonstrates that approach today on Craft 5. Its navigation dropdowns, search panel, blog filters and Todo List use Datastar rather than Alpine or another general-purpose frontend framework.</p><p>Try the <a href=\\\"{entry:258@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/blog}\\\">blog</a>, <a href=\\\"{entry:723@1:url||https://craftcms-lazy.ddev.site/search}\\\">search</a> and <a href=\\\"/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\\\">Todo List</a>, or <a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">inspect the starter kit on GitHub</a>. Build a clean content model and well-defined template boundaries now; assess any future framework migration against the actual released APIs.</p>\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:15:21','2026-11-13 15:52:11','9c6b4bf5-432a-4373-881a-45b1f5c3da70'),(2433,2433,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:15:21','2026-04-28 11:15:21','cc3817ef-31f8-47b6-96b8-99cfa71a4e2e'),(2434,2434,1,'Markus winkler q Pj V8 Xa XPTQ unsplash',NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:23:42','2026-04-28 11:23:42','65db8257-f980-452e-947d-e1de1286e3cf'),(2435,2435,1,NULL,'__temp_xaygllieqyndoyvhtocnpvadjmpxecbkomtm',NULL,'{\"1d7830ee-7479-40b2-96b0-17200bd14633\": \"Read the official announcement\", \"8731b252-877d-4cfa-80b2-c380c4af26be\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"value\": \"https://craftcms.com/blog/laravel\", \"target\": \"_blank\"}}',1,'2026-04-28 11:24:30','2026-04-28 11:25:52','b6b5955f-05fe-4114-b928-720b51c8ea5d'),(2436,2436,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:24:30','2026-04-28 11:24:30','e98b06e1-37a7-454f-9db6-bbad4e0b7fc9'),(2437,2437,1,'Craft CMS is Becoming a Laravel Package','craft-cms-6-laravel','blog/craft-cms-6-laravel','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2026-04-27 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [268], \"7f45d57a-6089-4476-9875-732dfa47a1a0\": {\"id\": 54, \"lat\": 52.5173885, \"lng\": 13.3951309, \"zoom\": 15, \"parts\": {\"arm\": \"Orion Arm\", \"city\": \"Berlin\", \"group\": \"the Local Group\", \"state\": \"\", \"county\": \"\", \"galaxy\": \"Milky Way\", \"number\": \"\", \"planet\": \"Earth\", \"system\": \"the Solar System\", \"address\": \"\", \"cluster\": \"Virgo Cluster\", \"country\": \"Germany\", \"postcode\": \"\", \"supercluster\": \"Laniakea Supercluster\"}, \"address\": \"Berlin, Germany\", \"fieldId\": 35, \"ownerId\": null, \"distance\": null, \"what3words\": null, \"ownerSiteId\": 1}, \"8ea3656a-4096-4563-af60-555454f92e16\": \"Craft CMS 6 and Laravel — What Craft Developers Need to Know — Craft CMS 6 is switching from Yii 2 to Laravel. What changes, what stays, and what Craft developers should do now. Full breakdown based on Dot All 2025 announcements.\", \"d74fbbee-f4c8-448b-b8fc-d5723a6d0f07\": 0, \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Craft CMS is Becoming a Laravel Package. Here is What That Means for You.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','9c73f4c2-6d1e-4290-98c9-03b38618a979'),(2438,2438,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"41d42c36-230e-4e28-96f8-8a4801e9694e\": \"<p>Craft 6 runs on Laravel. Everything you need to know before it ships.</p>\", \"914ae46d-5dd7-4afd-b5a3-32fbed3aecae\": [2434]}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','7a5f8e99-6f7b-4be5-a516-932af7421586'),(2439,2439,1,NULL,'__temp_dyzuagdpzcywlcsglsgmpeqdpnpfrabvemcr',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Craft 6 switches from Yii 2 to Laravel. If you have never touched Laravel, this is the moment to pay attention.</p><p>At Dot All 2025 in Lisbon, Pixel &amp; Tonic announced that Craft CMS 6 will be built on Laravel — the most widely used PHP framework in the world. This is not a cosmetic update. It is a fundamental shift in how Craft works under the hood, and it changes what you have access to as a developer.</p><p>If you have been building with Craft for years and never needed Laravel, that is completely fine. But understanding what this change brings — and what it does not break — is worth your time.</p><blockquote><p>Craft 6 is still in development. Beta is planned for Q3 2026, general availability Q4 2026. Everything here is based on official announcements. Implementation details may evolve.</p></blockquote><h2>Why Laravel?</h2><p>Craft has been running on Yii 2 since Craft 3. Yii 2 is a solid framework — but it is a niche one. The developer pool is small, the ecosystem is limited, and the tooling has not kept pace with what modern PHP development expects.</p><p><strong>Laravel is a different story entirely.</strong></p><p>Laravel has 70% market share among PHP developers. Over 25,000 Composer packages. A GitHub community four times the size of Yii 2. For Craft developers, that means a vastly larger ecosystem, better tooling, and a much bigger pool of developers who already know the underlying framework.</p><p>For Craft developers, this means access to a vastly larger ecosystem, better tooling, and — if your agency hires — a much larger pool of developers who already know the underlying framework.</p><blockquote><p>Craft is not abandoning what makes it Craft. It is adopting the infrastructure that lets it go further.</p></blockquote><h2>What you get access to</h2><p>Once Craft 6 runs on Laravel, the full Laravel toolchain becomes available in your Craft project — not as third-party integrations, but as native capabilities.</p><blockquote><p>You are not learning a new CMS. You are getting a much larger toolbox for the one you already use.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','9c8d4a29-0461-44b3-86b6-6d7a3584b111'),(2440,2440,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','b7d75542-d607-4042-88ba-eea84ee75638'),(2441,2441,1,NULL,'__temp_sopumlbdlehymcbywkjddpeesvdxwbpmyyfk',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','230543db-0de8-427e-a72d-0d66dd574135'),(2442,2442,1,NULL,'__temp_xbvlvqleuhqvydemtghsrjrebykqhzaowjoi',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"⚙️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Artisan CLI\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"All Craft commands run via php artisan. Custom commands, generators, and task automation — the way Laravel developers already work.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','67cf53be-419f-4908-b7b3-5a7a694b6edd'),(2443,2443,1,NULL,'__temp_kaimyratqfzqrmtbxhxenksinmpblxjxuymk',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🗃️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Eloquent ORM\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Laravel\'s database layer is available alongside Craft\'s native element queries. Custom data models without fighting the framework.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','0950b138-85b0-405c-951e-5bf6681ba803'),(2444,2444,1,NULL,'__temp_bbkovqgbxkjoobgnlbxannpponulgjkudqod',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📦\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"25,000+ Composer packages\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Any Laravel-compatible package drops straight into your Craft project. Payments, notifications, PDF generation — already solved.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','d4184ab1-2cfc-41c4-9640-d6371080a335'),(2445,2445,1,NULL,'__temp_zikohidxtyytfoxulbdnscurbazqhjrzmvau',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🚀\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Laravel Octane\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"In-memory application server. Extreme performance gains without changing your application code.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','0e758be6-a0f8-4694-bf49-b5927f9928e0'),(2446,2446,1,NULL,'__temp_dvircpqzyvmogztggiuadssoggqpyqhvhwfg',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📊\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Laravel Horizon\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Professional queue monitoring. Scheduled publishing, asset processing, email — all visible, all manageable.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','9b5d2153-b6f5-4706-98c6-e9e0aa0017f4'),(2447,2447,1,NULL,'__temp_vnivgvksezxshwprmuwpolueoshfceqnoopx',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🛠️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Laravel Forge / Vapor\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Deployment pipelines you may already be using. Craft now fits into them natively.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','e71b14c3-179e-4431-953e-b7bdcfd2f3a3'),(2448,2448,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','f2961806-7fb2-4458-9af9-bc4bec26c950'),(2449,2449,1,NULL,'__temp_daocwrgiaptvxcfgnjafqyvxvvooqagobrms',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>What happens to your existing projects</h2><p>Craft 5 becomes an official LTS release the moment Craft 6 ships. That means five full years of security updates and critical bug fixes — no forced migration, no deadline pressure.</p><p>For plugins, Pixel &amp; Tonic is shipping a Yii 2 adapter. Most existing Craft plugins will run on Craft 6 without code changes. The upgrade path is designed to be gradual, not a cliff.</p><blockquote><p>Craft 2 to Craft 3 was painful. Pixel &amp; Tonic learned from it. This migration is built differently.</p></blockquote><h2>What is new for content editors</h2><p>The Laravel migration is not the only story. Craft 6 also ships a set of long-overdue editorial features that make the control panel meaningfully better for the people using it every day.</p><blockquote><p>Features your clients have been asking for since Craft 3. They are finally first-class.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','7be7c710-e5c9-4fd0-a125-1f1740d2662a'),(2450,2450,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','5b8ad3d8-c5f7-41fd-8a4f-b7cc5d87be12'),(2451,2451,1,NULL,'__temp_lqwrfrtjyioxrehlxfhluumivnrvpkgqfrcw',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','7dbfeb05-efd0-4608-a77f-1b22243ec900'),(2452,2452,1,NULL,'__temp_yypbfzsagpbfklflctpkpchweyezdiuowapm',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"✅\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Content Approval Workflows\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Built-in approval processes for content publication. Custom rules, precise control, no plugin required.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','a175b74d-cbbe-4c27-a7bf-c67bc6d1a97d'),(2453,2453,1,NULL,'__temp_fevpxsvfnavmrzqqfuklzbelfudcsxtmrqsx',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"💬\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Commenting on Entry Edit Pages\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Editors can leave feedback directly on the editing screen. No more back-channel Slack threads about a headline.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','bbf8a612-e89b-40b0-8613-9a2ab7cd9934'),(2454,2454,1,NULL,'__temp_biwjmbvbgpgialmddcccczhnqnjjmrediczs',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📋\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Activity Logs\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"A full changelog for every content element. Who changed what, and when.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','0322864b-e288-498b-8df6-aa348ca12c9e'),(2455,2455,1,NULL,'__temp_ypuyxwhfugyjxcjizashheeojuvutjwnnfue',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"📅\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Content Releases\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Coordinate the publication of multiple entries at once. Campaign launches, site relaunches — handled.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','d967afba-ce7d-430b-b6e7-6c77d6872991'),(2456,2456,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','aa13e121-d6db-48d3-851a-74fa43c601c4'),(2457,2457,1,NULL,'__temp_uflbgcwhxputwgsgexaegqeotkzofmghxvrb',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>The timeline</h2><ul><li>Q1 2026 → Laravel migration complete, first alpha released</li><li>Q3 2026 Beta → approximately three months, open testing</li><li>Q4 2026 → General availability</li><li>2027–2031 Craft 5 LTS → security and critical updates</li></ul><h2>What to do now</h2><p>If you are on Craft 5, stay there. It is stable, it is LTS, and there is no reason to rush. Use the time to get comfortable with Laravel basics — Artisan, Eloquent, the service container. None of it is complicated if you already understand PHP, and all of it will make you a more capable Craft developer when Craft 6 lands.</p><p>If you are starting a new project today, Craft 5 is still the right choice. The architecture you build now — clean templates, proper element types, structured content — will carry forward cleanly.</p><blockquote><p>The best time to learn Laravel basics is before you need them. That time is now.</p></blockquote>\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','af655864-37f1-421f-b71f-13a94832230f'),(2458,2458,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','d91efcf6-2802-4a12-86d4-c15963ec5ed2'),(2459,2459,1,NULL,'__temp_xaygllieqyndoyvhtocnpvadjmpxecbkomtm',NULL,'{\"1d7830ee-7479-40b2-96b0-17200bd14633\": \"Read the official announcement\", \"8731b252-877d-4cfa-80b2-c380c4af26be\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"value\": \"https://craftcms.com/blog/laravel\", \"target\": \"_blank\"}}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','67fd8b66-8b6a-4fe0-b4d4-54ba3eb37c59'),(2460,2460,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','a96b6ec9-37b3-4824-9e35-9dbe1ac57d7f'),(2461,2461,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Craft CMS 6 and Laravel — What Craft Developers Need to Know\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Craft CMS 6 is switching from Yii 2 to Laravel. What changes, what stays, and what Craft developers should do now. Full breakdown based on Dot All 2025 announcements.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:31','2026-04-28 11:26:31','a2020b04-2fcb-492e-8b3a-d34a8c271c98'),(2462,2462,1,'Craft CMS is Becoming a Laravel Package','craft-cms-6-laravel','blog/craft-cms-6-laravel','{\"6268711e-041f-4ba2-ac1f-69075f35f133\": {\"date\": \"2026-04-27 22:00:00\"}, \"6ebd48e4-16ae-438b-88db-b7c32dac5dbd\": [268], \"7f45d57a-6089-4476-9875-732dfa47a1a0\": {\"id\": 54, \"lat\": 52.5173885, \"lng\": 13.3951309, \"zoom\": 15, \"parts\": {\"arm\": \"Orion Arm\", \"city\": \"Berlin\", \"group\": \"the Local Group\", \"state\": \"\", \"county\": \"\", \"galaxy\": \"Milky Way\", \"number\": \"\", \"planet\": \"Earth\", \"system\": \"the Solar System\", \"address\": \"\", \"cluster\": \"Virgo Cluster\", \"country\": \"Germany\", \"postcode\": \"\", \"supercluster\": \"Laniakea Supercluster\"}, \"address\": \"Berlin, Germany\", \"fieldId\": 35, \"ownerId\": null, \"distance\": null, \"what3words\": null, \"ownerSiteId\": 1}, \"8ea3656a-4096-4563-af60-555454f92e16\": \"Craft CMS 6 and Laravel — What Craft Developers Need to Know — Craft CMS 6 is switching from Yii 2 to Laravel. What changes, what stays, and what Craft developers should do now. Full breakdown based on Dot All 2025 announcements.\", \"d74fbbee-f4c8-448b-b8fc-d5723a6d0f07\": 0, \"f333c3f6-b95e-4720-8b85-bac84b0fd6bf\": \"Craft CMS is Becoming a Laravel Package. Here is What That Means for You.\"}',1,'2026-04-28 11:26:35','2026-04-28 11:26:35','a848de7f-ef97-4d54-9451-f7ad9dac6764'),(2463,2463,1,'Home','home','__home__','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Craft Kit —\\nThe Craft CMS Starter Kit Agencies Build On\", \"c0b7cbea-b2bc-4f4c-88f4-8117f3000cb9\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit with Datastar & Hypermedia — A production-ready Craft CMS 5 boilerplate — Vite, Tailwind, Datastar and DDEV preconfigured. Hypermedia-first, server-rendered, no JavaScript frameworks.\"}',1,'2026-06-09 08:51:33','2026-06-09 08:51:33','4dbe5c8f-78e8-4e1b-b105-e8f046de6ca4'),(2464,2464,1,'Map','datastar-map','map','{\"0c03aeb7-3181-4eb2-93bf-4bba1f224c26\": \"Interactive Maps in Craft CMS — Datastar & Leaflet Demo — Dynamic markers, category filters, and clustering — powered by Craft CMS, Leaflet, and Datastar. A hypermedia-driven map built entirely in Twig, with the server as the single source of truth\", \"2b51574c-5057-4c70-9a63-3e3612eb11b0\": \"<h1><strong>Interactive Maps in Craft CMS — Datastar &amp; Leaflet Demo</strong></h1><p>Interactive, data-driven maps in Craft CMS — dynamic markers, category filters, and clustering, all rendered in Twig. Leaflet handles the map, Datastar manages reactivity over SSE. No JavaScript framework, no page reloads, no client-side state. Just  \\n  fast, server-rendered geodata — perfect for directories, location listings, or event maps.</p>\", \"9c489dde-d3e4-48c2-835e-1cd576c86441\": 0}',1,'2026-06-09 08:51:33','2026-06-09 08:51:33','9bc83c50-afdd-4039-a006-406c422afe02'),(2465,2465,1,'Search','search','search','{\"0335e22f-b3a6-4cf1-9c27-8843e48457b6\": \"Datastar Search — Lightweight Reactive Search for Craft CMS — A fast and lightweight search page for Craft CMS using Datastar. Real-time search, instant results, and no full-page reloads — built entirely in Twig.\", \"501b1b12-e462-43a8-b93e-55e9d3742ce8\": 0, \"fba4e9d8-e8fa-4067-b5f1-c9b9a2a562d1\": \"<h1>Search</h1><p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A fast, lightweight search experience powered by Craft CMS and Datastar. This page demonstrates how to build reactive search interfaces directly in Twig — no heavy JavaScript framework required.</p><p>The Datastar Search Page is a practical example of how to implement instant, dynamic search functionality in Craft CMS. It uses Craft’s native search capabilities combined with Datastar’s reactive rendering to deliver fast and fluid results without page reloads.</p>\"}',1,'2026-06-09 08:51:33','2026-06-09 08:51:33','b9a3677d-079d-4413-bf88-6ad1ea8ecdc9'),(2466,2466,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Datastar Search — Lightweight Reactive Search for Craft CMS\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"A fast and lightweight search page for Craft CMS using Datastar. Real-time search, instant results, and no full-page reloads — built entirely in Twig.\"}',1,'2026-06-09 08:51:33','2026-06-09 08:51:33','8555e405-e2a9-45e2-afe1-6f38b5f973eb'),(2470,2470,1,'Builder','layout',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-11-13 13:16:00','2026-11-13 13:16:00','6c649696-f419-433b-9d8c-e5cdd9e8153d'),(2471,2471,1,'Home','home','__home__','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Craft Kit\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','0f1d2877-b4d9-4de9-ac0a-2f044fdda04f'),(2472,2472,1,NULL,'__temp_xmyryjgfvmihfecdlkmvkhurafqliwjajpcz',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A Craft CMS starter kit with working examples.</p><p>Start with Craft CMS 5, Twig, Tailwind CSS, Vite and DDEV already configured. Explore reactive interfaces with Datastar and reusable content blocks with Matrix and CKEditor.</p><p><a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">View on GitHub</a></p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','8413bbf1-df6d-4fcf-881b-8aa3f0b7ec72'),(2473,2473,1,NULL,'__temp_xkxefblkbqrrpgdsmxpjqahpwwtxucyulfla',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false, \"61e6d6af-7f1b-4d26-aee8-03abb530b6eb\": \"Explore the examples\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','614ae784-2f5d-4154-8257-67f9a483f601'),(2474,2474,1,NULL,'__temp_wivzvacapfdmeujajaupvewukwdvqvhisguk',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Blog\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Datastar Blog\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Filter posts and load more results with server-rendered HTML and Datastar.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','96625dd1-b1f3-487d-8f23-49cd49605cd8'),(2475,2475,1,NULL,'__temp_lwnertfphvvauwgyrfvklnfsixfpapkltjzf',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Map\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Datastar Map\", \"value\": \"{entry:1029@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Explore locations with live filtering, map markers and clustering.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','96c4b4b1-f7a7-4e48-8662-dbd9cc6bb900'),(2476,2476,1,NULL,'__temp_uvnzbtbsulagvvlmhwivhpmohuohwpnvjcon',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Todo List\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Datastar Todo List\", \"value\": \"/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Add, complete and delete tasks with Datastar and server-sent events.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','b36b0b4c-d0b7-4433-ba30-8e07eca940a0'),(2477,2477,1,NULL,'__temp_exydctshdtrxmqnzznfpmdmwtnijllasnzlm',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Search\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Datastar Search\", \"value\": \"{entry:723@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Search Craft content and update results as you type.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','c8bbc879-cc12-488a-ab68-597c1d904516'),(2478,2478,1,NULL,'__temp_ymqpcozflkswyiztejqhscgrwkbbvylnvwoy',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Matrix Builder\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:12@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Build pages from reusable content blocks, each rendered through its own Twig template.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','43efaa1d-94cb-48a7-916a-b51c0b522e74'),(2479,2479,1,NULL,'__temp_rookcbakctclekveurvtcgllabmfytnayywb',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"CKEditor Builder\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"CKEditor Builder\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Combine rich text and reusable components in a single editor field.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','e587a90c-1da0-4bdf-a583-174577a0e508'),(2480,2480,1,NULL,'__temp_cuuymclhjswekobraeoddxtrgwnaxsmmljiw',NULL,'{\"1d7830ee-7479-40b2-96b0-17200bd14633\": \"Use it as your starting point.\", \"4f0be684-f690-4928-92e0-e614fd7efe16\": \"<p>Download the starter kit, explore the templates and adapt it to your next project.</p>\", \"8731b252-877d-4cfa-80b2-c380c4af26be\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"👉 Get the Starter Kit on github\", \"value\": \"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\", \"target\": \"_blank\"}}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','853ad59e-ff32-4483-b2ed-a79fff494766'),(2481,2481,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Craft CMS Starter Kit with Datastar Examples\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"A Craft CMS 5 starter kit with Twig, Tailwind, Vite and DDEV. Explore Datastar examples for blogs, maps, todos and search, plus Matrix and CKEditor builders.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": [700]}',1,'2026-11-13 13:34:21','2026-11-13 13:34:21','b3edbff8-6518-4bf5-a8db-43feaebb3aa2'),(2482,2482,1,'Why Craft Kit','why-craft-kit','why-craft-kit','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Why Craft Kit?\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:39:29','2026-11-13 13:39:29','cd0d9c9e-0bd6-42f6-899f-17a9d7003a8a'),(2483,2483,1,NULL,'__temp_tywyazieygvtllwbymokluxxbsgguvtbfvol',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">A starting point for Craft CMS, not a finished website.</p><p>Craft Kit is a starter kit you can download from GitHub and adapt to your own projects. It combines a configured development environment with working examples of content blocks and Datastar interactions.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:39:29','2026-11-13 13:39:29','0735b5af-f185-45b6-a2d8-0ef3cfee0265'),(2484,2484,1,NULL,'__temp_gyydugypgvjiequfbxcuomsbyqstomnyqdeo',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Server-rendered by default</h2><p>Craft manages the content, Twig renders the pages, and Datastar updates the parts that need to react. Search results, filtered listings and small interactions stay close to the templates instead of moving into a separate frontend application.</p><p>Use HTML and CSS for the basics, then add the tools an interaction actually needs. The map uses Leaflet, the slider uses Embla, and Datastar connects reactive interfaces to server-rendered HTML.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:39:29','2026-11-13 13:39:29','55b652fe-4ee0-46b5-9600-aa0e8f0319ea'),(2485,2485,1,NULL,'__temp_qyczkdevkhsquglcuaumrjenkyenhcmoklto',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>What is already configured</h2><ul><li><strong>Craft CMS 5 and Twig</strong> for content modeling and page templates.</li><li><strong>Datastar</strong> for reactive updates with HTML over server-sent events.</li><li><strong>Tailwind CSS and Vite</strong> for styling, development and asset builds.</li><li><strong>DDEV</strong> for a repeatable local development environment.</li><li><strong>SEOMate and LLM Ready</strong> for metadata, sitemaps and Markdown versions of entry pages.</li></ul>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:39:29','2026-11-13 13:39:29','9b64df9c-4fa7-4eaa-9f83-260c969e92a3'),(2486,2486,1,NULL,'__temp_kxwhfgistwnjjblgiuvkzaeavgpetxpswgzl',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Examples you can follow</h2><p>The demos show individual patterns you can inspect and adapt:</p><ul><li><a href=\\\"/blog-hypermedia-datastar\\\">Blog</a> — filter posts and load more results.</li><li><a href=\\\"/map\\\">Map</a> — filter locations and display them on an interactive map.</li><li><a href=\\\"/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\\\">Todo List</a> — add, complete and delete tasks.</li><li><a href=\\\"/search\\\">Search</a> — update results as you type.</li></ul><p>The <a href=\\\"/matrix-builder\\\">Matrix Builder</a> demonstrates reusable page blocks. The <a href=\\\"/cke-builder\\\">CKEditor Builder</a> shows how those components can sit inside rich text. Both use the same block templates with rendering suited to their context.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:39:29','2026-11-13 13:39:29','edf3b09c-2773-416e-9e16-8051ed5b6ebc'),(2487,2487,1,NULL,'__temp_vfxmybeygkhtkxuwzrcpcxjpmzuvcfsiufat',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<h2>Make it your own</h2><p>Clone the repository, follow the setup in the README and explore the templates alongside the demos. Keep the patterns that help and remove what your project does not need.</p><p>The example design and content are a starting point, not a requirement. Bring your own content model, styling and project-specific features.</p><p><a href=\\\"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\\\">View the project on GitHub</a></p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:39:29','2026-11-13 13:39:29','b3ace422-757d-42c9-af60-82e4fa849ee4'),(2488,2488,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Why Craft Kit? A Practical Craft CMS Starter Kit\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Explore the approach behind Craft Kit: server-rendered Twig, Datastar interactions, reusable content blocks and a configured Craft CMS 5 development setup.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 13:39:29','2026-11-13 13:39:29','f8fcfdf9-5dbe-4d93-aa40-65156cb6997f'),(2489,2489,1,'Blog','blog','blog','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Datastar Blog\", \"981facbf-3e2f-4e4b-9f37-d1b8629dd72b\": \"<p>A blog listing built with Craft CMS, Twig and Datastar. Filter posts by category and load more results without a full page reload.</p><p>Choose a category or use “Load more” to try it. Datastar sends the request; Craft returns the updated HTML.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:03:02','2026-11-13 14:03:02','29c20331-ed0b-4ab3-a25a-cf681e34f2ad'),(2490,2490,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Datastar Blog Demo for Craft CMS\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Explore category filtering and load-more pagination with Craft CMS, Twig and Datastar. A working example included in the Craft Kit starter kit.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:03:02','2026-11-13 14:03:02','34f4f827-a582-494a-89a6-6a0c4008ef37'),(2491,2491,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>The illustrations were created for Craft Kit with an image-generation model. AI-generated assets are marked by the shared image component.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 15:53:18','13a5fc78-f775-445f-a92f-e0449d19cf45'),(2492,2492,1,'Matrix Builder','matrix-builder','matrix-builder','{\"1a9a9160-4064-4d41-b55f-e820ab14f99c\": 0, \"872f39e9-c6e7-4db6-9915-33944177d829\": \"Matrix Builder\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','9d1e271d-89ec-459a-aac2-a072512306c8'),(2493,2493,1,NULL,'__temp_igexmbvajwvcuuzsdrygzfnvhrvrckpdgpyk',NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Build a page from reusable content blocks.</p><p>With Craft’s Matrix field, editors add, arrange and edit blocks in the control panel. Each block has its own fields and Twig template. A shared content container keeps the page aligned; the outer wrapper handles backgrounds and spacing.</p><p>This page demonstrates text, media, accordions, buttons, cards, a slider, a gallery and a call to action. Open the accordion below to see how each block works, or compare the same components in the <a href=\\\"/cke-builder\\\">CKEditor Builder</a>.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','e4e2f790-2691-4880-9690-937827ead85c'),(2494,2494,1,NULL,'__temp_dkucgpvpbmgwouxblhhoezbgricogtigdgeh',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [470]}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','45cff693-9edb-44c3-9758-4d767c7dfb4c'),(2495,2495,1,NULL,'__temp_lczjuokmzbhhbyxyrynxewsouacztdqeogei',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','021c67b7-80dc-4794-ab20-4000c8c38af9'),(2496,2496,1,NULL,'__temp_qrcmkinkbbxnuibhhyluprgddxbrnwukdrjd',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>A Matrix field holds a sequence of entries with different types. Here, those types represent page blocks. Editors choose a block, fill in its fields and move it into place. Twig renders each entry through its block template.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"How does the Matrix Builder work?\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','a58e9026-73e1-40e8-a94c-ff5d6f028478'),(2497,2497,1,NULL,'__temp_fdmnmwnhizyqaowchspafavppvztbhftromn',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Use a text block for headings, paragraphs, lists and links. This introduction is a text block. Rich text stays editable in Craft while its presentation comes from the shared typography styles.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Text\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','2ef70ca4-0491-4225-a6ab-1660270b4747'),(2498,2498,1,NULL,'__temp_sqhkxwtlwqdgpomsyqfjgdeialsntxttdqnm',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>A media block displays an image, video or audio asset, with an optional caption. The image example below uses responsive image transforms and includes a photographer credit.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-media\\\">View the media block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Media\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','e429de91-6b52-4bac-8e3e-0bd265dbd917'),(2499,2499,1,NULL,'__temp_ntbjjsmqcppzkuxbwwdjsdffobfuzhywcuuu',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Group links to entries or external URLs in a button block. The example links to other demos in this starter kit.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-buttons\\\">View the button block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Buttons\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','a5435070-829b-4543-bd18-da0cda7331a7'),(2500,2500,1,NULL,'__temp_zddmiezhcowhvvycomtuzzqdacozlmohhvhm',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Each card combines a headline and teaser with an optional image and link. Add and reorder the nested card entries inside the block.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-cards\\\">View the card block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Cards\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','446fa0fa-8d78-4e03-96f1-a53718b829ff'),(2501,2501,1,NULL,'__temp_cmrnwpfqtqzgswipneamgkxvibjomlcrazfw',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>You are using an accordion block now. Each item has a heading, rich text and an initial open or closed state. Use it for FAQs or supporting details that readers can expand when needed.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Accordions\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','b85c4a1f-d426-4c27-b73c-e0fae02cd5b8'),(2502,2502,1,NULL,'__temp_arkvvvzawwxwegqkblwutjidbidtphinbouf',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Select and arrange several images in one block. The page shows a preview grid; opening an image launches the lightbox with the full selection.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-gallery\\\">View the gallery block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Gallery\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','61819a23-3de0-465c-89c0-88d5224c24a4'),(2503,2503,1,NULL,'__temp_mzavqhbrjmontcfxiyhhjalhelokfemkpbii',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>The slider presents nested card entries in an Embla carousel. Use the arrow buttons or drag the cards to browse. This example uses cards without images.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-slider\\\">View the slider block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Slider\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','1752ee3f-d628-4ba7-8403-6217ea7adbb7'),(2504,2504,1,NULL,'__temp_vdlnoxztodxfkbntzlzcmancspfjwhzxfinn',NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>A call-to-action block combines a headline, optional text and a link. Use it to give a section a clear next step.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-cta\\\">View the call-to-action block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Call to action\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','df3836bd-9195-4fc8-b566-23c732919483'),(2505,2505,1,NULL,'__temp_dylfnxlitdhvawugsdazyilrjqksgobwewrz',NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [1804]}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','3938aef8-d41b-4033-857d-1bb466e5e12e'),(2506,2506,1,NULL,'__temp_ggcamffnpfxkkqkyiogvkbusxetubwjpugiu',NULL,'{\"0f59f188-6699-4347-a393-7cc6ddd680fc\": false, \"61e6d6af-7f1b-4d26-aee8-03abb530b6eb\": \"Cards: image, text and link\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','61680ce9-0890-4b1b-91ae-ead3a227f24d'),(2507,2507,1,NULL,'__temp_vlktkftqsphxfjyndyemvdqeyyhcodychxau',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"CKEditor Builder\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [487], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>See the same reusable components embedded in a rich-text field, rather than arranged as separate page blocks.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','ee40c93e-c3b2-4559-be55-52412d19cea0'),(2508,2508,1,NULL,'__temp_vjcqenztenwqdnbjeaoufajpbezaedwnfdaw',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Datastar Blog\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [1123], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Filter posts by category and load more results with server-rendered Twig and Datastar.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','f7d115e7-8521-4d85-a7f0-2dae3358458e'),(2509,2509,1,NULL,'__temp_lxpgaomhbryfxiauurlxexhrqgqbctjrinec',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Datastar Map\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:1029@1:url}\"}, \"e07011df-84b0-4504-8c98-7af8c534248c\": [1821], \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Explore a location listing connected to a Leaflet map, with filters, markers and clustering.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','fa354e9e-8cf0-42df-972e-2393e5a7c1cd'),(2510,2510,1,NULL,'__temp_awiesparhzqylaqztqrjxfevvsldtjdnyvjr',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','15a8f1ee-85df-44be-885e-8c75b1e6e295'),(2511,2511,1,NULL,'__temp_ylemifpwvuyctlwdehmbulafpegthmaqheca',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Datastar Blog\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:258@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Try category filtering and load-more pagination without a full page reload.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','19ddc2bf-26f1-471c-9996-d9fdc6ecb94f'),(2512,2512,1,NULL,'__temp_ehhrklzrainhieblfenjrffadyetuiiwpiaw',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Datastar Map\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:1029@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Filter locations and explore them on an interactive Leaflet map.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','122af16f-6fd1-4a4f-897a-0a35d48b6218'),(2513,2513,1,NULL,'__temp_eotiwlzzapgiwvhsiznjjmbidgcqrwhvozbg',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Datastar Search\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:723@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Search Craft content and update the results as you type.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','d402b195-be8b-4497-a941-48d2d32b484d'),(2514,2514,1,NULL,'__temp_iwehllemswxtjrechvbuvprnzpooxrcjktcd',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"CKEditor Builder\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"label\": \"Read more\", \"value\": \"{entry:99@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Combine editable rich text and reusable components in one field.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','13015656-c0ae-4b50-8d9e-288752643b39'),(2515,2515,1,NULL,'__temp_wbtjljkqhjgsihsgyveoixvllsfpsotuzhom',NULL,'{\"4ca0b060-ab25-4210-ba7a-04339db07b5d\": \"Why Craft Kit?\", \"b68b894d-8c8e-4fc8-af1c-45b45dfc82d5\": {\"type\": \"entry\", \"value\": \"{entry:2221@1:url}\"}, \"e3da269c-60c2-4d60-9a98-718ef293562c\": \"<p>Read about the starter kit’s approach, toolchain and reusable examples.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','18a198dd-1b09-4623-aa6d-bcfef1594260'),(2516,2516,1,NULL,'__temp_skgejxqlvzvxlvshaiwtkhzsdcucfrnrrbdi',NULL,'{\"b8d6efb4-2958-4af8-bc7d-70882b9d2432\": [1123, 925, 1804, 1821]}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','8217950b-6239-4fc6-8e62-5e22b06f45f9'),(2517,2517,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p>Demo photos: <a href=\\\"https://unsplash.com/photos/gcsNOsPEXfs\\\">Planning an interface</a> by Firmbee.com; <a href=\\\"https://unsplash.com/photos/E1por_SGvJE\\\">In the beginning</a> and <a href=\\\"https://unsplash.com/photos/ofpr9Cw8Rj8\\\">Keep things simple</a> by Brett Jordan; <a href=\\\"https://unsplash.com/photos/5Xwaj9gaR0g\\\">Workspace</a> by Martin Shreder. All four are free to use under the <a href=\\\"https://unsplash.com/license\\\">Unsplash License</a>.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','b96733f5-4341-4fe7-abb6-98cc47e4d609'),(2518,2518,1,NULL,'__temp_ytlqvepnrrvzzijpzczplwjclwcwaqybepii',NULL,'{\"d04bc466-1b82-4e88-ba5a-d772666f5e29\": \"How blocks fit together\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','8250ea2d-9426-442a-98e8-678bfb66ae9d'),(2519,2519,1,NULL,'__temp_byyiuytdbvnwsmzimfsebiqdnzynujrhalzm',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"⚡\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Defined fields\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Each block type has fields suited to its content, such as text, images or links.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','3f30d96c-e5ce-4655-8616-c83697a8a83e'),(2520,2520,1,NULL,'__temp_xejdvhpirncibaqcjdqghzofxkhsrxkkvbkd',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🧱\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Shared templates\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"One Twig template per block keeps its markup in one place.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','bd736f9a-d5b5-4bca-8426-d60c590714fd'),(2521,2521,1,NULL,'__temp_mpgssyzsvuhztrarldwkqfguvlbbgpppkcme',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🎨\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"A shared container\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Content uses one width; the outer wrapper controls backgrounds and spacing.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','1510d2b1-ab62-43d0-b7c7-9ecb0295bb08'),(2522,2522,1,NULL,'__temp_gratvrcwhvabevkjqznzllzrqezofyatpbpb',NULL,'{\"3e5af703-8dda-4b8d-90ec-c328be3aa431\": \"🛠️\", \"487cc30b-61c6-421d-b453-84857b9cae46\": \"Editor-controlled order\", \"a88d2904-f0c9-447c-87ac-4dbd0d25d7d7\": \"Arrange the available blocks in Craft without changing the page template.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','08b5999e-3f8f-4c80-b031-37b97c3e3f93'),(2523,2523,1,NULL,'__temp_ssedhvejnbomhxziekbsplayakexpmtvvapn',NULL,'{\"1d7830ee-7479-40b2-96b0-17200bd14633\": \"Build your own page.\", \"4f0be684-f690-4928-92e0-e614fd7efe16\": \"<p>Start with the example blocks, adapt their fields and templates, and give them your own design. The starter kit and demo templates are available on GitHub.</p>\", \"8731b252-877d-4cfa-80b2-c380c4af26be\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"👉 Download Craft Kit\", \"value\": \"https://github.com/handplant/craftcms-lazy-starter-kit\"}}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','13191804-2184-474e-9ba2-ee5f56f3b76d'),(2524,2524,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"9bd2388d-d293-4f1b-8283-61a80c29e4ac\": \"Matrix Builder Demo for Craft CMS\", \"e3b0b587-97fc-47a0-a491-7e55f71b27ad\": false, \"f9112d3e-b4f8-4c57-bbba-1c369f98698d\": \"Explore reusable Craft CMS Matrix blocks: text, media, cards, galleries, sliders and calls to action. See how editable content becomes server-rendered Twig.\", \"fb364fbf-e22b-4dbe-8570-724df7c5e068\": [470]}',1,'2026-11-13 14:13:20','2026-11-13 14:13:20','3f7e3c41-8dbf-4095-8474-b2a8a5f3b7ff'),(2525,2525,1,'Matrix — modular page blocks',NULL,NULL,'{\"48d2238f-4200-4601-8702-9f2157892222\": \"AI-generated illustration for Craft Kit\", \"5ab4cacf-3877-4008-802e-aa67b2627478\": true, \"e30c17b9-ffa5-4343-99ee-0f780e5e0ed0\": \"Reusable blocks, arranged as a page.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:49:05','2026-11-13 14:49:05','e3b059b5-3fd9-4cff-b638-5a4e21a9e1c0'),(2526,2526,1,'CKEditor — components in the flow',NULL,NULL,'{\"48d2238f-4200-4601-8702-9f2157892222\": \"AI-generated illustration for Craft Kit\", \"5ab4cacf-3877-4008-802e-aa67b2627478\": true, \"e30c17b9-ffa5-4343-99ee-0f780e5e0ed0\": \"Components embedded in the flow of a story.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:49:42','2026-11-13 14:49:42','19add2ee-15c8-432a-9f56-15ff3416caaf'),(2527,2527,1,'Reusable content cards',NULL,NULL,'{\"48d2238f-4200-4601-8702-9f2157892222\": \"AI-generated illustration for Craft Kit\", \"5ab4cacf-3877-4008-802e-aa67b2627478\": true, \"e30c17b9-ffa5-4343-99ee-0f780e5e0ed0\": \"Different pieces, one consistent system.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:49:42','2026-11-13 14:49:42','eacb4529-b841-480f-b98f-32e5c040c835'),(2528,2528,1,'Expandable accordion',NULL,NULL,'{\"48d2238f-4200-4601-8702-9f2157892222\": \"AI-generated illustration for Craft Kit\", \"5ab4cacf-3877-4008-802e-aa67b2627478\": true, \"e30c17b9-ffa5-4343-99ee-0f780e5e0ed0\": \"A structure that opens when you need more detail.\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:49:42','2026-11-13 14:49:42','6bd0ba7a-06e5-4218-ae23-c94a2b7f5183'),(2530,2530,1,'Todos','todolist',NULL,'{\"5e2baca9-5c68-4147-b9e7-0df1a3d033d9\": {\"type\": \"url\", \"label\": \"Todos\", \"value\": \"/hypermedia-todolist-craft-cms-datastar\"}}',1,'2026-11-13 14:56:04','2026-11-13 14:56:04','87bd2342-d2ed-4e6b-95c4-fbdf2955d2a7'),(2532,2532,1,'Showroom','layout',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-11-13 14:57:03','2026-11-13 14:57:03','1f8e69f2-73af-4fc3-bd17-fc2c66474e2d'),(2533,2533,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"54ea783f-26e8-4a98-a119-9a041012aa68\": \"<p class=\\\"ui-teaser\\\">Two ways to compose content. The same reusable Twig components.</p><p>Build pages from separate Matrix blocks, or embed those components in the flow of a CKEditor field. This demo shows both approaches side by side.</p><p><a href=\\\"#matrix\\\">Explore Matrix</a> · <a href=\\\"#ckeditor\\\">Explore CKEditor</a></p><h2>Matrix: build the page</h2><p>Each block is an entry with its own fields and Twig template. Add, arrange and edit blocks in Craft; a shared content container keeps the page aligned while each wrapper controls backgrounds and spacing.</p>\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','6a26429e-d910-44dd-8263-9c4c6d6ba4e0'),(2534,2534,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"2865337a-17be-4f7e-abb6-f993a4223470\": \"matrix\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','481d248c-f0e7-45f6-86aa-f93b64001160'),(2535,2535,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"26b82635-94fe-4602-bc9b-85d9440f803d\": true, \"293325f0-efb5-4532-bed8-8ece59244dd0\": [470]}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','047f1dd3-ce1f-4083-b9f3-a3d9c991a7b3'),(2536,2536,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"2865337a-17be-4f7e-abb6-f993a4223470\": \"matrix-editor\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','5ee4a06f-baa6-4136-9679-530662a3c5b5'),(2537,2537,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','069822fc-fe74-442f-97e8-60cc1539bc07'),(2538,2538,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>A Matrix field holds a sequence of entries with different types. Here, those types represent page blocks. Editors choose a block, fill in its fields and move it into place. Twig renders each entry through its block template.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"How does the Matrix Builder work?\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','7f0b2dd1-8b54-4690-8c3b-5bc33b41a1aa'),(2539,2539,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Use a text block for headings, paragraphs, lists and links. This introduction is a text block. Rich text stays editable in Craft while its presentation comes from the shared typography styles.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Text\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','86ab3272-bff2-478b-bcaf-3a241d553f76'),(2540,2540,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>A media block displays an image, video or audio asset, with an optional caption. The image example below uses responsive image transforms and includes a photographer credit.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-media\\\">View the media block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Media\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','390a09ee-ae1e-4a5a-8d8d-e27ee9dc7a18'),(2541,2541,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Group links to entries or external URLs in a button block. The example links to other demos in this starter kit.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-buttons\\\">View the button block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Buttons\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','ba981465-e053-47b8-8194-f2c49bd95bf7'),(2542,2542,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Each card combines a headline and teaser with an optional image and link. Add and reorder the nested card entries inside the block.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-cards\\\">View the card block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Cards\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','cc90a0bf-334e-4e50-a831-427bd0297f0b'),(2543,2543,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>You are using an accordion block now. Each item has a heading, rich text and an initial open or closed state. Use it for FAQs or supporting details that readers can expand when needed.</p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Accordions\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','2700ec68-4e93-4c71-996a-3b73989f2215'),(2544,2544,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>Select and arrange several images in one block. The page shows a preview grid; opening an image launches the lightbox with the full selection.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-gallery\\\">View the gallery block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Gallery\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','d59862e0-be56-46d8-9bdd-350f70e423bd'),(2545,2545,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>The slider presents nested card entries in an Embla carousel. Use the arrow buttons or drag the cards to browse. This example uses cards without images.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-slider\\\">View the slider block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Slider\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','d1180e75-fc69-43e4-b619-9b4181be8f8c'),(2546,2546,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"1914e261-c0f4-4bd8-ba28-a8d24eb68efc\": false, \"2f81e9a4-b86d-4811-acbc-2c63e797e15b\": \"<p>A call-to-action block combines a headline, optional text and a link. Use it to give a section a clear next step.</p><p><a href=\\\"#block-cta\\\">View the call-to-action block</a></p>\", \"f5b31de1-27bd-4d5b-b4f2-d55ac6415806\": \"Call to action\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','de5588b8-57e8-4858-b306-31b2829a5f78'),(2547,2547,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'{\"2865337a-17be-4f7e-abb6-f993a4223470\": \"block accordion\"}',1,'2026-11-13 14:59:03','2026-11-13 14:59:03','764464ec-2560-471c-bd