th an ai badge the editor screenshots show the craft kit demo installation images are served locally no unsplash images are used last updated 13 november 2026 '),(705,'field',27,1,''),(705,'slug',0,1,' imprint '),(705,'title',0,1,' imprint '),(706,'slug',0,1,''),(711,'field',8,1,' privacy policy '),(711,'field',18,1,' craft kit is a public demonstration of a craft cms starter kit and its datastar examples it also presents my work as an independent developer this notice explains how personal data is processed when you visit or use the demos controller and contact andi grether badstr 22c 79379 mullheim germany webworker ag gmail com website delivery and server logs when you request a page or an asset the hosting system processes technical information such as your ip address request url time of access browser information and response status these data are needed to deliver the website diagnose problems and protect it from abuse logs are retained only as long as needed for these purposes or to investigate security incidents subject to applicable retention obligations the legal basis for operating and securing the website is our legitimate interest under article 6 1 f gdpr datastar interactions search and the todo list datastar is served from this website navigation controls search filters and the demo forms send requests to this website when a server response is needed search terms and submitted demo values are processed to provide the requested result they can also form part of the requested url and technical access logs the todo list stores tasks in your server side session a necessary session cookie can associate your browser with that session security cookies may also be used for request protection the demo does not create a permanent personal task account do not enter sensitive or confidential information into it essential session and security storage is used to provide the function you request not for advertising the applicable basis is article 6 1 f gdpr and for strictly necessary device storage or access section 25 2 tdddg cookieless matomo analytics the public website uses a self hosted matomo installation at p e8qn5a project space to understand use of the demo the tracker is configured with cookies disabled it records page views and link interactions the demos also send event categories such as adding or completing a task and opening the bitcoin data panel the task text is not included in those custom event calls analytics can process the visited url referrer time of access browser and device information and the ip address received by the analytics server cookieless tracking is still data processing ip masking and retention are controlled in the matomo server configuration disabling cookies alone is not a guarantee of anonymity the purpose is to improve the demonstration and understand which examples are useful based on our legitimate interest under article 6 1 f gdpr you may object to processing based on legitimate interests by contacting the controller if a particular analytics configuration requires consent it must be assessed separately the absence of cookies does not decide that question by itself openstreetmap on the map demo opening the map demo loads map tiles directly from openstreetmap tile servers these requests transmit technical connection data including your ip address and the requested tile urls to the map service this is separate from the locally served leaflet code used to display the map the map is provided to demonstrate location filtering details about the services data processing are available in the openstreetmap foundation privacy policy other pages do not need to load those map tiles ai generated content all editorial texts and illustrations on this demo website were generated or revised using artificial intelligence actual screenshots of the craft control panel are not ai generated generated illustrations are identified by an ai badge ai assisted content may contain errors it is provided to demonstrate the starter kit and does not replace independent professional advice simply viewing the texts and images does not send your data to an ai service images fonts and frontend assets the demo images fonts and application ui scripts are served from this website the matomo analytics script is loaded separately from the analytics host described above the editorial illustrations were created for craft kit and are marked with an ai badge viewing them does not send an image generation request or visitor data to an ai image service unsplash images and remote font services are not used server side data sources and external links the github repository statistics and binance btc usdt ticker are fetched by the websites server the demo does not send your search terms or task text to those services and your browser does not need to contact their apis to display the results links to github linkedin documentation and external articles take you to other websites when you follow them their operators then process data under their own privacy policies contact by email if you send an email your message and contact details are processed to answer your inquiry this includes processing by the email service providers involved in delivery the legal basis is article 6 1 b gdpr for contract related inquiries or article 6 1 f gdpr for other correspondence messages are deleted when no longer needed unless legal retention obligations apply your rights subject to the applicable conditions you may request access rectification erasure restriction of processing or data portability you may object to processing based on legitimate interests where processing relies on consent you may withdraw it for the future you may also complain to a data protection supervisory authority for baden wurttemberg see the state data protection authority contact the controller above to exercise your rights reusing the starter kit this notice describes this demonstration not every project built from the repository if you reuse craft kit adapt the notice to your controller details hosting enabled integrations and actual data processing configuration last updated 13 november 2026 '),(711,'field',27,1,' how the craft kit demo processes technical data datastar demo inputs cookieless matomo analytics and openstreetmap requests '),(711,'slug',0,1,' privacy policy '),(711,'title',0,1,' privacy policy '),(712,'field',4,1,' how the craft kit demo processes technical data datastar demo inputs cookieless matomo analytics and openstreetmap requests '),(712,'slug',0,1,''),(723,'field',18,1,' search a fast lightweight search experience powered by craft cms and datastar this page demonstrates how to build reactive search interfaces directly in twig no heavy javascript framework required the datastar search page is a practical example of how to implement instant dynamic search functionality in craft cms it uses crafts native search capabilities combined with datastars reactive rendering to deliver fast and fluid results without page reloads '),(723,'field',27,1,' datastar search lightweight reactive search for craft cms a fast and lightweight search page for craft cms using datastar real time search instant results and no full page reloads built entirely in twig '),(723,'slug',0,1,' search '),(723,'title',0,1,' search '),(725,'slug',0,1,''),(876,'slug',0,1,' opinion '),(876,'title',0,1,' opinion '),(878,'alt',0,1,''),(878,'extension',0,1,' jpg '),(878,'filename',0,1,' souvik banerjee wprnem 6dg unsplash jpg '),(878,'kind',0,1,' image '),(878,'slug',0,1,''),(878,'title',0,1,' souvik banerjee w pr nem 6dg unsplash '),(879,'field',20,1,' for a custom content driven website i want control over the content model the markup and the way the interface behaves craft cms gives me that foundation datastar makes it reactive without turning it into a separate frontend application a content model built around the project craft starts with sections entry types fields and relationships that you define editors work with the structure their content needs rather than a themes assumptions matrix handles page sections ckeditor handles flowing text with embedded components wordpress can also support custom content models and carefully built frontends my preference is about the starting point craft makes structured content and custom twig templates central to the workflow own the html with twig the same project controls content queries semantic markup image output and accessible controls there is no requirement to choose a theme or expose a json api before a page can exist that is a useful foundation for performance but not a guarantee queries eager loading caching image sizes and hosting still need attention add datastar where the page needs to react a filter does not need a second application craft can render the results in twig and datastar can request and morph those results into the page search pagination and a task list follow the same pattern in craft kit datastar also controls the navigation dropdowns mobile navigation and search panel there is no alpine vue or react layer coordinating that ordinary ui state the same signal and attribute model covers local interactions and server requests choose the stack for the work wordpress remains a valid choice for teams invested in its ecosystem craft is the stack i choose when a project calls for a deliberate content architecture a custom design and a frontend i can keep understandable the official craft cms and wordpress comparison covers the differences in more detail for an existing wordpress site start with the migration guide and audit the content before planning a rebuild try the approach not just the argument explore the datastar blog map filters and live search then inspect the builder to see how the content is composed download craft kit on github and use the templates as a starting point for your own craft and datastar project '),(879,'slug',0,1,' temp epuxgsbappmctwahfdpzjemvchoaohitwwwg '),(879,'title',0,1,''),(892,'slug',0,1,' development '),(892,'title',0,1,' development '),(925,'alt',0,1,' wooden letter tiles spelling in the beginning on a white background '),(925,'extension',0,1,' jpg '),(925,'field',4,1,' in the beginning brett jordan unsplash '),(925,'filename',0,1,' brett jordan e1por sgvje unsplash jpg '),(925,'kind',0,1,' image '),(925,'slug',0,1,''),(925,'title',0,1,' brett jordan e1por s gv je unsplash '),(972,'alt',0,1,''),(972,'extension',0,1,' jpg '),(972,'filename',0,1,' mad geek love mktzxudq5c8 unsplash jpg '),(972,'kind',0,1,' image '),(972,'slug',0,1,''),(972,'title',0,1,' mad geek love mktzxudq5c8 unsplash '),(979,'field',20,1,' i used to reach for craft graphql and vue whenever a website needed interactivity for most content driven projects i now prefer craft twig and datastar the reason is practical i can deliver the same useful interactions with fewer layers to coordinate what vue and graphql solve a separate frontend application makes sense when it is genuinely an application complex offline behavior substantial browser owned data or several clients consuming the same api crafts graphql api can serve a web frontend a mobile app and other integrations from one content model that is a different requirement from a website that needs search filters and pagination i do not want to introduce an api boundary solely to update a list of craft entries what the extra layer costs craft generates a graphql schema from the content model and permissions you do not have to invent that schema manually you still need to maintain frontend queries rendering components loading states and error handling around the api for a single website that can mean expressing the same content relationships in craft in api queries and in the frontends rendering layer those boundaries can be valuable for an independent frontend team in a small craft team i often find they add coordination without enough benefit let craft render the response craft already knows how to query entries resolve relations transform assets and render twig datastar lets those templates remain the ui an interaction requests an endpoint the server returns html patches and the browser updates the relevant elements the response can finish immediately an sse response does not require a permanent connection and a live search interaction does not require a dedicated streaming server datastar signals handle transient browser state craft owns saved data permissions and validation the boundary is explicit without a separate frontend store or client side router one model for everyday interactions this site is a working example the mobile menu navigation dropdowns and search panel use datastar just like the blog filters map filters and todo list there is no alpine layer for the small interactions and another framework for the bigger ones specialist tools still do specialist work leaflet draws the map embla handles the slider and glightbox opens galleries datastar coordinates the ordinary ui and server driven updates it does not need to replace a mapping engine when i would still choose vue and graphql i would choose them when the product needs a separately deployed application an api shared across several clients or complex browser side workflows that justify that architecture this is not a claim that a server rendered website can replace every application see the smaller stack in practice try the filterable blog live search and todo list each demonstrates a useful interaction while craft remains responsible for the response for most craft websites that is the default i want content in craft markup in twig reactivity in datastar craft kit gives you the working starting point '),(979,'slug',0,1,' temp jstciagbxuaohtngrbfunmncynfgajzhhnep '),(979,'title',0,1,''),(982,'field',20,1,' ⚡ datastar twig approach '),(982,'slug',0,1,' temp ztemfnobndtoeyiprvsiucxycbqsscckhhyt '),(982,'title',0,1,''),(985,'field',20,1,' when comparing both approaches the contrast speaks for itself ⚙️ vue graphql introduces multiple layers components queries build steps and state management just to achieve basic interactivity and thats only part of it you also need to configure vite and maintain a build pipeline define graphql schemas and set permissions handle authentication ship larger javascript bundles all of this adds weight to projects that often dont need it datastar on the other hand keeps everything close to the template it delivers reactivity and dynamic behavior without the complexity of a full frontend stack no schema management no complex routing no hydration edge cases ✨ and because datastar also handles ui interactions like navigation modals or simple stateful components i dont even need alpine js anymore one lightweight tool is enough ✅ lean fast maintainable this setup fits most content driven craft cms projects perfectly modern interactivity without the frontend bloat '),(985,'slug',0,1,' temp cypbzsstsnbuyxakohhmvpjrxtfqzufmvbsg '),(985,'title',0,1,''),(1001,'slug',0,1,' layout '),(1001,'title',0,1,' showroom '),(1014,'alt',0,1,''),(1014,'extension',0,1,' svg '),(1014,'filename',0,1,' gm 1500 svg '),(1014,'kind',0,1,' image '),(1014,'slug',0,1,''),(1014,'title',0,1,' gm 1500 '),(1029,'field',18,1,' interactive maps in craft cms datastar leaflet demo interactive data driven maps in craft cms dynamic markers category filters and clustering all rendered in twig leaflet handles the map datastar manages reactivity over sse no javascript framework no page reloads no client side state just fast server rendered geodata perfect for directories location listings or event maps '),(1029,'field',27,1,' interactive maps in craft cms datastar leaflet demo dynamic markers category filters and clustering powered by craft cms leaflet and datastar a hypermedia driven map built entirely in twig with the server as the single source of truth '),(1029,'slug',0,1,' datastar map '),(1029,'title',0,1,' map '),(1084,'field',4,1,' interactive maps in craft cms datastar leaflet demo dynamic markers category filters and clustering powered by craft cms leaflet and datastar a hypermedia driven map built entirely in twig with the server as the single source of truth '),(1084,'slug',0,1,''),(1099,'slug',0,1,' map '),(1099,'title',0,1,' map '),(1101,'field',8,1,' how craft cms helps businesses scale their content operations by appfoster '),(1101,'field',10,1,' community '),(1101,'field',17,1,''),(1101,'field',27,1,' how craft cms helps businesses scale their content operations by appfoster appfoster looks at scaling content operations with craft cms structured models reusable content and editorial workflows that can grow with the business '),(1101,'field',28,1,' appfoster looks at scaling content operations with craft cms structured models reusable content and editorial workflows that can grow with the business '),(1101,'field',35,1,' 9131 keele street vaughan york region golden horseshoe ontario l4k 5b4 canada '),(1101,'slug',0,1,' how craft cms helps businesses scale their content operations by appfoster '),(1101,'title',0,1,' how craft cms helps businesses scale their content operations by appfoster '),(1102,'field',11,1,' appfoster looks at scaling content operations with craft cms structured models reusable content and editorial workflows that can grow with the business '),(1102,'slug',0,1,''),(1103,'field',4,1,' how craft cms helps businesses scale their content operations by appfoster appfoster looks at scaling content operations with craft cms structured models reusable content and editorial workflows that can grow with the business '),(1103,'slug',0,1,''),(1107,'field',8,1,' ⚡ bitcoin the open protocol for value '),(1107,'field',10,1,' opinion '),(1107,'field',17,1,''),(1107,'field',19,1,' bitcoin is no longer just a speculative asset its an open decentralized protocol much like the internet itself except instead of moving data it moves value instantly globally and without permission why it matters todays financial system runs on trust in institutions bitcoin replaces that trust with math and code the rules are transparent and no one can change them not banks not governments not developers 21 million bitcoin no more no less ever energy security misconceptions yes bitcoin uses energy but that energy secures the network making it the most resilient computing system on the planet it has been running for over 15 years without interruption no hacks no bailouts no downtime the real innovation bitcoin isnt crypto its the opposite its simple minimal and stable by design no founders no marketing department just open source code and a global network of users keeping it alive its a protocol not a product final thought whether you see it as a store of value digital cash or an idea bitcoin is about freedom transparency and self sovereignty its not about getting rich its about getting free '),(1107,'field',27,1,' bitcoin the open protocol for value bitcoin is an open protocol for transferring value explore the idea of shared rules and a decentralized network then try the datastar powered price demo '),(1107,'field',28,1,' bitcoin is an open protocol for transferring value explore the idea of shared rules and a decentralized network then try the datastar powered price demo '),(1107,'field',35,1,' frankfurt hesse germany '),(1107,'slug',0,1,' bitcoin the open protocol for value '),(1107,'title',0,1,' bitcoin the open protocol for value '),(1108,'field',11,1,' bitcoin is an open protocol for transferring value explore the idea of shared rules and a decentralized network then try the datastar powered price demo '),(1108,'slug',0,1,''),(1109,'field',4,1,' bitcoin the open protocol for value bitcoin is an open protocol for transferring value explore the idea of shared rules and a decentralized network then try the datastar powered price demo '),(1109,'slug',0,1,''),(1110,'field',20,1,' bitcoin is an open protocol for transferring value what interests me is the architecture public rules independently operated nodes and a network that does not depend on one applications database shared rules independently checked participants can run software that verifies transactions and blocks against the protocols rules control is distributed across a network rather than assigned to a single bank or platform the current consensus rules limit issuance to approximately 21 million bitcoin those rules are maintained through software and network agreement not an administrator changing a balance in a central system security has costs and limits proof of work consumes energy to make rewriting transaction history expensive that does not remove every risk wallets can be compromised services can fail and transactions require care confirmation times and fees also vary bitcoin is neither an instant payment guarantee nor a promise of financial returns this article is a technical introduction not investment advice why there is a bitcoin panel in craft kit the small bitcoin button in this sites navigation is also a datastar example open it and craft fetches the btc usdt ticker from binance on the server renders the result in twig and sends an html update to the browser while the panel is open datastar runs the refresh countdown and requests an update roughly every ten seconds when it is closed the interval does not request ticker updates the open state countdown and request indicator all use datastar signals and attributes the visitors browser talks to this website not directly to binance market data is illustrative and may be delayed or unavailable it is not an execution price the useful takeaway a live data panel does not need a separate frontend application the same server rendered pattern powers the blog filters search and todo list explore the craft kit source on github to see the datastar attributes and twig endpoints behind the panel '),(1110,'slug',0,1,' temp xywfexnhyxzniuroeiuvyfhpbiwlqqqfblwo '),(1110,'title',0,1,''),(1111,'alt',0,1,''),(1111,'extension',0,1,' jpg '),(1111,'filename',0,1,' michael fortsch a