,'field',4,1,' ️ editor controlled order '),(1964,'field',8,1,' arrange the available blocks in craft without changing the page template '),(1964,'slug',0,1,' temp gratvrcwhvabevkjqznzllzrqezofyatpbpb '),(1964,'title',0,1,''),(1965,'slug',0,1,''),(1981,'field',8,1,' features '),(1981,'field',40,1,' ⚡ hypermedia first no javascript frameworks datastar handles reactivity via sse server stays the source of truth matrix content builder flexible page layouts with reusable blocks mix and match sections without touching code tailwind css utility first styling with css custom properties oklch colors and zero config overhead ️ production ready setup vite ddev and craft cms 5 pre configured and ready to build on from day one '),(1981,'slug',0,1,' temp chcdsoceehskmeaejhnlktaqyzrhotbhartq '),(1981,'title',0,1,''),(1982,'field',4,1,' ⚡ hypermedia first '),(1982,'field',8,1,' no javascript frameworks datastar handles reactivity via sse server stays the source of truth '),(1982,'slug',0,1,' temp czygtbsyuidoyzfduojpxacmabomyhyfusmo '),(1982,'title',0,1,''),(1983,'field',4,1,' matrix content builder '),(1983,'field',8,1,' flexible page layouts with reusable blocks mix and match sections without touching code '),(1983,'slug',0,1,' temp joouhcsjsjtgnbykeslaxjxihitgofcxfqdh '),(1983,'title',0,1,''),(1984,'field',4,1,' tailwind css '),(1984,'field',8,1,' utility first styling with css custom properties oklch colors and zero config overhead '),(1984,'slug',0,1,' temp kdsyjobebvafutnkaslbujacqfitmyudocaf '),(1984,'title',0,1,''),(1985,'field',4,1,' ️ production ready setup '),(1985,'field',8,1,' vite ddev and craft cms 5 pre configured and ready to build on from day one '),(1985,'slug',0,1,' temp rgwiaskotmziwuwmpkaaajtrvmopmynhchpv '),(1985,'title',0,1,''),(1986,'slug',0,1,''),(1999,'slug',0,1,''),(2000,'slug',0,1,''),(2001,'slug',0,1,''),(2019,'field',8,1,' use it as your starting point '),(2019,'field',11,1,' download the starter kit explore the templates and adapt it to your next project '),(2019,'slug',0,1,' temp cuuymclhjswekobraeoddxtrgwnaxsmmljiw '),(2019,'title',0,1,''),(2020,'slug',0,1,''),(2050,'slug',0,1,' todolist '),(2050,'title',0,1,' todos '),(2074,'slug',0,1,''),(2075,'slug',0,1,''),(2076,'slug',0,1,''),(2079,'field',8,1,' making craft cms ai ready what geo actually means in practice '),(2079,'field',10,1,' development '),(2079,'field',17,1,''),(2079,'field',19,1,' everyones talking about generative engine optimization most articles explain the same three concepts and call it a day so instead of writing another overview i want to share what i actually did to make craft kit ai agent ready and be honest about what matters and what doesnt the one thing that actually works serving markdown llms understand text not html text a typical html page is full of navigation scripts svgs cookie banners and a hundred other things an ai agent has to filter through just to get to your content markdown cuts all of that out the good news theres already a standard for this ai agents like claude code send an http accept header with text markdown if your server responds accordingly the agent gets a clean markdown version of your page same url no separate route no magic craft kit now supports this out of the box via the llm ready plugin every page automatically has a markdown version and the accept header is handled for you token usage for agents drops significantly content is easier to process everyone wins llms txt useful but not what you think theres a lot of hype around llms txt the idea is simple a file at your site root that acts as an ai friendly sitemap linking to markdown versions of your pages with short descriptions heres the honest reality no major ai provider officially uses it googles john mueller said it plainly in mid 2025 no ai system currently reads llms txt an audit of 1 000 domains confirmed that llm specific bots like claudebot or gptbot dont fetch it at all that said i kept it in craft kit and heres why the cost is near zero when its auto generated for developer tooling and documentation sites like craft kit dev its the exact use case where it could eventually matter and if adoption does pick up youre already set what id avoid manually maintaining a llms txt treating it as an seo lever or including pages like imprint and privacy policy in the index none of that helps anyone recycling seo fields for geo one small practical win the llm ready plugin lets you define which field to use as the description in your llms txt entries instead of adding a new field i pointed it at the existing seo meta description its already written already concise and already describes the page accurately less duplication more signal what i skipped a few things i looked at and decided against script type= text llms txt a vercel proposal that embeds llm facing content directly in the html via an unknown script type clever idea but browsers still load the full html and no ai provider actively reads it not worth the effort a separate docs section in markdown some sites maintain full parallel documentation in markdown for a demo project like craft kit this would be overkill the per page markdown generation covers it the short version if you want your craft cms site to be ai agent ready serve markdown on accept text markdown this is the only thing with real confirmed adoption right now add a llms txt as an auto generated link index low effort no downside use your existing seo descriptions as llm descriptions keep focusing on good seo and accessibility if a screen reader struggles with your content so will an ai craft kit has all of this set up out of the box one less thing to figure out '),(2079,'field',27,1,' making craft cms ai ready what geo actually means in practice make craft content easier for ai tools to read with markdown clear structure and reusable seo descriptions a practical setup without ranking promises '),(2079,'field',28,1,' make craft content easier for ai tools to read with markdown clear structure and reusable seo descriptions a practical setup without ranking promises '),(2079,'field',35,1,' dusseldorf north rhine westphalia germany '),(2079,'slug',0,1,' making craft cms ai ready what geo actually means in practice '),(2079,'title',0,1,' making craft cms ai ready what geo actually means in practice '),(2080,'field',11,1,' make craft content easier for ai tools to read with markdown clear structure and reusable seo descriptions a practical setup without ranking promises '),(2080,'slug',0,1,''),(2081,'field',4,1,' making craft cms ai ready what geo actually means in practice make craft content easier for ai tools to read with markdown clear structure and reusable seo descriptions a practical setup without ranking promises '),(2081,'slug',0,1,''),(2082,'field',20,1,' making a website useful to ai tools starts with the same work that helps people clear content meaningful headings and reliable links craft kit adds machine friendly output without maintaining a second copy of every article readable content comes first ai tools can process html but a page may contain navigation scripts and other material that obscures its main content a well structured markdown representation can make that content easier to extract and work with craft kit uses the llm ready plugin to offer markdown output clients that request accept text markdown can receive a readable representation at the same page url support for that request pattern varies between tools it is not a promise that every crawler will use it one content model several representations the article remains editor managed in craft twig produces the website machine readable output is generated from the same source there is no parallel documentation tree for editors to keep synchronized this matches the reason i use datastar for the frontend let craft remain responsible for the content and return the representation the interaction needs html powers the visitors interface markdown can serve a reading tool what llms txt can and cannot do an auto generated llms txt can act as a concise index for tools that choose to read it it is not a replacement for a sitemap robots directives accessible html or good internal linking there is no ranking guarantee attached to publishing it adoption and crawler behavior change so i would not build a marketing promise around it i keep the index generated rather than asking editors to maintain another manual file reuse the descriptions you already write a useful seo description can also summarize an article for a content index reusing it avoids another field that repeats the same editorial job the important part is an accurate summary not filling a special ai keyword slot a practical checklist publish useful content with a clear heading structure keep canonical urls and internal links reliable provide readable markdown for clients that request it generate an index from the existing content model review the actual output instead of assuming a plugin guarantees visibility for the reactive side of the same server first approach try the datastar blog and live search their content remains rendered by craft rather than being hidden behind a separate frontend application explore craft kit on github to inspect the templates and configuration treat the ai friendly output as a practical capability not a guarantee of traffic citations or rankings '),(2082,'slug',0,1,' temp wtragnbaiqmezzfuowubqopgdsfnzyxnmjgb '),(2082,'title',0,1,''),(2083,'slug',0,1,''),(2084,'alt',0,1,''),(2084,'extension',0,1,' jpg '),(2084,'filename',0,1,' nahrizul kadri oasf0qmrwla unsplash jpg '),(2084,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2084,'slug',0,1,''),(2084,'title',0,1,' nahrizul kadri o as f0 qmr wl a unsplash '),(2172,'field',4,1,' ai ready '),(2172,'field',8,1,' structured llms txt and markdown exports so ai coding tools understand your project from day one '),(2172,'slug',0,1,' temp psgpkklclxxxapxjchpyvphpydmdrkfbbdtu '),(2172,'title',0,1,''),(2173,'field',4,1,' ♿ accessible by default '),(2173,'field'