kit '),(2685,'filename',0,1,' blog bitcoin protocol png '),(2685,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2685,'slug',0,1,''),(2685,'title',0,1,' bitcoin an open network for value '),(2686,'alt',0,1,' ivory architectural panels joined by an orange dovetail in a graphite frame beside simple drafting tools '),(2686,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2686,'field',4,1,' quality comes from how the pieces fit together ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2686,'filename',0,1,' blog team craftsmanship png '),(2686,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2686,'slug',0,1,''),(2686,'title',0,1,' craft cms shared craftsmanship '),(2687,'alt',0,1,' an open ivory folio on a graphite plinth with orange and ivory material strips held by a fine alignment guide '),(2687,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2687,'field',4,1,' templates styles and formatting in alignment ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2687,'filename',0,1,' blog twig tailwind zed png '),(2687,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2687,'slug',0,1,''),(2687,'title',0,1,' twig tailwind and zed tools in alignment '),(2688,'alt',0,1,' one orange conduit passes through three ivory panels beside two separate channels joined by small bridges '),(2688,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2688,'field',4,1,' different ways to coordinate a reactive interface ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2688,'filename',0,1,' blog datastar alpine htmx png '),(2688,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2688,'slug',0,1,''),(2688,'title',0,1,' datastar and alpine with htmx coordinating reactive ui '),(2689,'alt',0,1,' an architectural campus of small ivory and graphite buildings linked to an orange spine on one shared base '),(2689,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2689,'field',4,1,' many distinct sites on one shared foundation ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2689,'filename',0,1,' blog multisite png '),(2689,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2689,'slug',0,1,''),(2689,'title',0,1,' craft multisite many sites one foundation '),(2690,'alt',0,1,' three joined ivory bridge arches carry an orange walkway across a gap in a graphite plinth '),(2690,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2690,'field',4,1,' a direct path with fewer moving parts ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2690,'filename',0,1,' blog hypermedia agencies png '),(2690,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2690,'slug',0,1,''),(2690,'title',0,1,' hypermedia a direct path with fewer moving parts '),(2691,'alt',0,1,' ivory document sheets pass through a graphite frame into three separated panels connected by orange ribbons '),(2691,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2691,'field',4,1,' clear structure makes content easier to read and reuse ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2691,'filename',0,1,' blog ai ready png '),(2691,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2691,'slug',0,1,''),(2691,'title',0,1,' ai ready content readable structure '),(2692,'alt',0,1,' an ivory module with an orange inset slides along matching guides into a larger graphite architectural framework '),(2692,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2692,'field',4,1,' a content platform joining a broader ecosystem ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2692,'filename',0,1,' blog craft laravel png '),(2692,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2692,'slug',0,1,''),(2692,'title',0,1,' craft and laravel a module in a larger ecosystem '),(2829,'alt',0,1,' three ivory modules with an open shutter a recessed panel and sliding slabs linked by an orange ribbon on one graphite base '),(2829,'extension',0,1,' png '),(2829,'field',4,1,' navigation search and filters connected by one reactive model ai generated illustration for craft kit '),(2829,'filename',0,1,' blog datastar craft twig practical png '),(2829,'kind',0,1,' image '),(2829,'slug',0,1,''),(2829,'title',0,1,' datastar in craft one reactive model for navigation search and filters '),(2830,'field',8,1,' datastar in craft cms live search filters and navigation with twig '),(2830,'field',10,1,' development '),(2830,'field',17,1,''),(2830,'field',19,1,' the useful test of a frontend stack is not whether it can build one impressive demo it is whether the ordinary interactions fit together opening the navigation revealing a search panel typing a query and filtering a list craft kit uses datastar for all of those interactions there is no alpine layer for the small pieces and a different framework for server requests craft renders the html and one reactive model connects the interface this article walks through that model using examples from the kit the snippets are shortened for readability links to the complete templates are included below if you want the comparison first read why i prefer datastar to an alpine and htmx combination for craft one model two kinds of state an open dropdown and a saved entry are not the same kind of state the dropdown can live in the browser the entry belongs to craft together with its permissions and validation datastar signals handle the temporary values whether the menu is open what is in the search input which category is selected when those values need a server response datastar sends a request and applies the returned html a local toggle does not need a round trip that is the foundation browser signals for the interaction craft for authoritative data twig for the response 1 start with the navigation and search panel the base template defines a shared ui namespace for site wide controls this is the actual shape used by the kit body data signals= ui searchopen false navopen false dropdownopen false btcopen false the search button toggles a signal and closes the mobile navigation the panel reacts to the same signal with styling and icon markup removed the interaction looks like this button type= button data on click= $ui searchopen = $ui searchopen $ui navopen = false data attr= aria expanded $ui searchopen true false search button div class= hidden data class= block $ui searchopen hidden $ui searchopen search component goes here div there is no endpoint here because no server data needs to change datastar updates the classes and the buttons expanded state in the browser navigation dropdowns use the same store the kit keeps the open dropdowns entry id in ui dropdownopen rather than creating an unrelated state system for each menu the navigation template also handles outside clicks and escape see the navigation template and the dropdown component use the menu on this page to try the behavior 2 turn a search term into a twig request live search adds the next step the browser has a value but craft owns the searchable content the search component binds the input to ui search and requests a twig endpoint after a short debounce % set type = type page % % set fetchaction = datastar get datastar search twig type type % div data signals= ui search input type= search aria label= search data bind ui search data on input debounce 300ms= fetchaction data indicator fetching div id= searchresult type div div data bind keeps the input and signal together data on input debounce 300ms waits until typing pauses before running the request expression data indicator exposes the requests loading state as a signal the craft datastar plugin creates the request expression through datastar get you point it at a template you do not need to add a json api or a separate frontend route for the result the type variable distinguishes the full search page from the search panel their result containers have different ids so a response can update the intended instance 3 let craft query and render the results on the server the search term is available through signals ui search the endpoint queries craft entries and renders links with twig this shortened version keeps the same query and target id pattern as the kit % set type = type page % % set search = signals ui search % % set query = craft entries section blog pages % % set entries = search query search search orderby score desc postdate desc limit 100 all % % patchelements % div id= searchresult type % for result in entries % a href= result url result title a % else % pno matching content yet p % endfor % div % endpatchelements % the important connection is the matching searchresult type id in the component and response the plugins patchelements tag returns an html update and datastar morphs it into the page the complete endpoint has separate messages for an empty query and a query with no results keep those states useful a blank container should not be the only feedback after someone searches try live search then compare the search component with its twig endpoint the request path is visible from the markup 4 scope reusable filters to their entry a page wide search value is intentionally shared a reusable blog block should not accidentally share its selected category with another instance the kit gives entry based components a namespace derived from their entry id the blog block uses appentry id filter and passes its block id to the endpoint % set blockid = entry id % % set fetchaction = datastar get datastar blog twig offset 0 entryid blockid % div data signals= app blockid filter json encode select aria label= filter posts by category data bind app blockid filter data on change= fetchaction data indicator blog fetching data attr disabled= $blog fetching category options go here select div the full template initializes the filter from the url renders the category options and loads the first set of entries on the server the endpoint reads the matching signal namespace resolves the category and runs the entry query the result container is scoped too result entry id signals and dom targets follow the same ownership boundary that makes the block easier to reuse without a new naming convention for every feature 5 use the same endpoint for filtering and load more the blog endpoint already knows the selected filter and pagination offset a new filter replaces the current results the load more button appends the next entries in the successful response the difference is a patch mode % set entryid = entryid null % % set filter = entryid signals app entryid filter % successful response after querying the entries % patchelements with selector result entryid mode offset == 0 inner append % % for entry in entries % entry render % endfor % % endpatchelements % the endpoint also returns an updated load more control or removes it when there are no further entries the query fetches one extra entry to determine whether another page is available that is still one feature expressed as craft queries and twig output there is no parallel list renderer in a client side component and no need to recreate the card markup in javascript try the blog filters and load more button the source lives in blockblog twig and the blog endpoint loading states urls and keyboard access still matter a request indicator is not just a spinner the blog also uses it to disable its filter and load more button while a request is active clear loading and empty states make the interaction understandable shareable urls deserve the same attention craft kit uses its urlsync macro to synchronize selected signals with query parameters using history replacestate the blog reads its filter on the initial server request the search page restores its query through the macro this is not a promise of a complete browser history or no javascript implementation use real links for navigation give controls accessible names and test focus and escape behavior datastar supplies reactive primitives it does not automatically make every component accessible or give every interaction a useful no javascript path what the server still owns validation signals and url parameters are untrusted input validate types allowed values and query limits permissions only query and mutate content the current visitor is allowed to use mutations use post server side validation and csrf protection for changes not a get request that saves data escaping keep twig auto escaping enabled returned html is not permission to trust arbitrary input caching do not reuse personalized or filter dependent output under a cache key that ignores those values an sse response can finish after sending its patches these examples do not require a permanent connection or a dedicated streaming server long lived updates are a separate hosting and application decision no alpine layer does not mean no javascript datastar runs javascript in the browser and its attribute expressions describe browser behavior the benefit is not pretending otherwise it is keeping everyday ui behavior and server requests in one model close to the html and twig that developers already work with the kit still uses leaflet for the map embla for the slider and glightbox for galleries those are specialist integrations not a second general purpose ui framework competing with datastar for the same state build your next interaction from a working example start with the navigation follow a search request into its endpoint then inspect how the blog scopes its filter and appends another page the todo list shows server confirmed mutations and the map shows filtered content feeding a specialist browser library the builder demo covers the editorial side reusable twig components rendered from matrix and ckeditor craft kit is the working starting point download it on github explore the examples and keep the parts that fit your project for the integration details use the craft datastar plugin documentation and the datastar attribute reference '),(2830,'field',27,1,' datastar in craft cms search filters navigation with twig build live search filters and navigation with craft cms twig and datastar follow real examples from craft kit with one reactive model and no alpine layer '),(2830,'field',28,1,' build live search filters and navigation with craft cms twig and datastar follow real examples from craft kit with one reactive model and no alpine layer '),(2830,'field',35,1,''),(2830,'slug',0,1,' datastar craft cms live search filters navigation twig '),(2830,'title',0,1,' datastar in craft cms live search filters and navigation with twig '),(2831,'field',11,1,' build live search filters an